  {"a":"ambessa","b":"aatrox","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your ability-into-empowered-auto comes online, but Aatrox's Deathbringer-Stance heal-on-hit refunds whatever you chip in a stand-still trade — dash his Q sweetspots, land one empowered auto, and step out, don't sit in it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses through his disengage, and your passive armor-pen plus the crash-down burst chunks him before World Ender's bonus healing and AD turn the brawl — your cleanest kill window."},{"when":"Aatrox 1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane spikes his sustained Q-rotation damage and healing, so if he lands all three Q sweetspots into Infernal Chains he out-drains your whole combo — only commit if you can dodge a Q edge."},{"when":"Late","text":"Aatrox's bruiser armor blunts your all-physical kit and World Ender's heal amp scales, so long brawls are his — anti-heal plus short, R-led bursts keep it even."}],"wants":{"you":["Dash through his Q sweetspot edges with Drakehound's Step and weave one empowered auto in short trades, never stand in for a prolonged exchange","Brace Repudiation to eat a Q edge or the Infernal Chains hit, then cash the amplified slam back into him","Fire Public Execution down a line clear of his jungler — it takes the FARTHEST champion in it — burst before World Ender heal-amps"],"foe":["Tag you with Infernal Chains and hold you in the impact area — leave slowly and the chains drag you back for a second hit","Drag every fight long so Deathbringer Stance and World Ender out-sustain your energy-gated burst","Spike Eclipse/Profane first so his Q-rotation damage and drain out-trade your combo windows"]},"early":"At Levels 1-2 you're both weak, so don't hand him a free trade — he wants to land a Q sweetspot edge and heal off the hit with Deathbringer Stance, and your single energy-gated ability can't punish that yet. Once you have Q and E, your pattern is strict: dash his Q sweetspots with Drakehound's Step, land Cunning Sweep into one empowered auto, and dash straight back out before his heal-on-hit catches up. Never sit in range trying to win a prolonged exchange at Level 3 — standing still is exactly where his drain beats you. If you read a Q edge or his Infernal Chains, brace Repudiation to swallow it and you get a free amplified slam back.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his window and you should respect it — his cooldowns are short enough to chain Q sweetspots and, if he tags you with Infernal Chains, hold you in for an extended trade where Deathbringer Stance simply out-sustains your physical burst, and your own cooldowns are at their longest here. Don't force it; farm to 6. Then everything flips: Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses through his attempt to disengage, and your passive armor-pen plus the crash-down burst chunks him before World Ender's bonus healing and AD can out-heal you. That's your kill — take it when his Infernal Chains is down so he can't lock you into a heal-back brawl.","late":"Late game stays a knife's edge. He reclaims his footing on his first item — Eclipse or Profane Hydra spikes his Q-rotation damage and drain, making his long trades lethal if you let them run, and your damage is entirely physical, so every armor item he or his team stacks blunts you hard. Don't grind out long fights with him; that's exactly what Deathbringer Stance and World Ender's heal amp are built for. Buy anti-heal early, lead with Public Execution for the suppress and armor-pen, and burst in short R-led windows. Do that and it stays the coinflip the win rate says it is — drag it out and his sustain wins.","whys":["You're both weak level-1s — he has one Q, you have one energy-gated ability, so nobody commits; deny his sweetspot last-hits and set the lane up for your level-2 spike.","At 2 Lacerate's dash strikes a second time and slows, and his Infernal Chains is 20s — hit him the moment he spends it and dash out, so Deathbringer Stance never gets the stand-still it needs to heal.","At 3 his short-cooldown Q sweetspots plus an Infernal Chains tag let him hold you in a drain trade his heal-on-hit wins, and your combo can't out-burst that yet.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window with your longest cooldowns, and his on-hit healing out-sustains anything short of a full commit — concede the trade and farm to 6.","Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses through his disengage, and your armor-pen burst lands before World Ender's bonus healing and AD turn the fight — your one clean kill.","Eclipse/Profane spikes his Q-rotation drain to lethal, and your energy-gated combo can't trade back through that much sustain — play for picks, not the straight 1v1.","Stacked bruiser armor blunts your all-physical output and World Ender's heal amp scales, but anti-heal plus short R-led bursts keep it the coinflip it is — don't brawl long."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"akali","win":["Skill","Akali","Akali","Skill","Skill","Akali","Akali"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"You out-stat her bare-handed and her W Twilight Shroud is still locked — walk up and Q-cone her every time she steps to last-hit a melee minion, then cash the Maxim stack into an empowered auto."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Akali has Shroud (lvl 2) plus E shuriken + recast online, so she can poke-dash in and out and vanish from your R line and E-slow before your empowered auto ever lands."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R is the threat: the two-part dash + execute lets her all-in from outside your E-slow range, and she can second-cast it straight out of your R suppress once the stun ends."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once she has Gunblade/Rabadon's her AP burst outscales your physical chip; Shroud-resets in extended fights mean you can no longer one-combo her, so the lane has to be closed before then."}],"wants":{"you":["Punish level 1 before W Twilight Shroud exists — Q-cone and empowered-auto her on every melee-minion approach, since at lvl 1 she literally cannot vanish","Bait her E shuriken dash, then time W Repudiation to brace the return damage so the blocked hit amplifies your next Q slam","Land R Public Execution when she has burned Shroud or is mid R-dash — the suppress + stun catch her before she can Shroud or recast out"],"foe":["Drop W Twilight Shroud to go untargetable and break your R blink line, dodging the E-slow and empowered auto","Poke with E shuriken and passive-empowered autos from outside your Q2 reach, then dash out before you can chain ability-into-auto","Stall to two items so Shroud resets and her R burst out-damages your physical-only chip"]},"early":"Level 1 is unambiguously yours: Akali's W Twilight Shroud doesn't unlock until 2, so she literally cannot go untargetable, and your bare-handed Q-cone plus a Maxim-stacked empowered auto out-trades her energy-gated shuriken pokes. Stand on the melee minions she has to walk up for and slam her every time she steps in. Don't chase her past Sundering Slam range or you just feed her E poke for free; bank the lead and your lane health, because once she has Shroud and her E recast at 2-3 the trade pattern flips and she stops having to eat your follow-up.","mid":"From 3 onward this gets genuinely annoying: her E shuriken-dash tags you and leaves before your empowered auto resolves, and Shroud deletes your R blink-target and your E-slow if you commit blind. Don't force extended fights through 4-5 when your Q and E are on their longest cooldowns and she just dances out of them. Save your all-in for when she misuses Shroud or burns E with no escape — bait those out with a feint, then brace W Repudiation on her return damage so the block amplifies your Q slam. At 6 respect her R: it dashes twice and executes, so she can open from outside your slow range, and remember your suppress only holds her until the stun ends — she can recast R straight out of it, so don't blow your own ult expecting a free kill.","late":"She's the harder scaler and this is where she reclaims the lane: once Gunblade or Rabadon's is online her R burst out-damages your physical-only chip, and Shroud-resets mean you can't one-combo her down in a single ability-into-auto chain anymore. You stay a respectable scaler, but Ambessa deals almost entirely physical, so any armor she or her team forces you to itemize around plus her untargetability erodes your edge fast. Your whole plan is to make the level-1/2 lead matter on the map before her items land — use your R armor-pen and roam pressure to take towers and pick fights on your terms, and never let this drift into a 1v1 splitpush where her mobility and burst beat your bruiser pattern.","whys":["Her W Twilight Shroud is locked at level 1 so she cannot go untargetable — your Q-cone plus a Maxim-empowered auto out-trades her energy pokes the moment she steps to a melee minion.","She has Shroud at 2 but limited tools and you both trade on cooldowns, so it's a coin-flip on who lands the committing hit first before her E recast is online.","Her E shuriken-dash and recast come online — she pokes in and dashes out before your empowered auto lands, and Sundering Slam's reach can't pin a target that just teleports.","This is your weakest window: longest Q/E cooldowns while she kites your E-slow and empowered autos with her dash and farms safely toward 6.","Her R's two-part dash and execute let her open from outside your slow range and recast straight out of your suppress once the stun ends — her level-6 spike beats yours.","Shroud-resets plus her first-item AP burst chunk you faster than your physical chip rebuilds, so she dictates every all-in around her own cooldowns.","You're both scalers, but her Shroud untargetability and AP burst answer your physical-only damage — the lane only stays even if your early lead already closed the game."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"akshan","win":["Akshan","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Akshan","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q (Cunning Sweep) into its Sundering Slam follow-up plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto is your first real chunk — punish him the moment he steps inside Heroic Swing range to last-hit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Akshan's best window: Going Rogue camouflages him while he hugs terrain and his revive lets him fight greedier, so hold a Control Ward on the brush he hooks off and never facecheck for him."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse done plus the lvl-9 Q max is your peak — Q1, empowered auto, Q2 (Sundering Slam) with R's passive armor pen and on-damage heal melts his squishy frame the instant you pin him."},{"when":"Late","text":"You stay the cleaner scaler, but a snowballed Akshan with revive up and crit online can burst you from a flank before you land R — vision and not walking into his swing range matters more than the duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his E (Heroic Swing) toward you, then Drakehound's Step dash in and land Q into Sundering Slam before he can swing back out of range","Force the lvl-6 all-in: R (Public Execution) blinks you behind him and suppresses, locking down a champion whose entire kit is built to swing away","Keep the lane short and deny roams — your empowered-auto chains out-trade his Q/W poke once you're glued to him"],"foe":["Kite with Heroic Swing and chip you with Q (Avengerang) before you ever reach empowered-auto range","Roam off E mobility and snowball, leaning on his W revive to fight greedier than the matchup should allow","Keep trades short — every third hit of Dirty Fighting shields him, so your burst starts already short"]},"early":"Akshan's early is poke-and-swing — his Q (Avengerang) boomerang and Heroic Swing keep him at range while he chips, so don't throw Q at empty air chasing him. At Level 1 you're both soft; just farm cleanly and don't eat free poke. The moment you hit 2-3, your Q (Cunning Sweep) into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto out-damages anything he can poke for — bait the swing, dash in, and make him pay for stepping up to last-hit.","mid":"Through 4-5 your cooldowns are long and he'll happily kite, so farm toward your spike and don't force a fight he can swing out of. At 6 he gets dangerous — not in a straight 1v1, but his E roams and his W revive let him fight greedier than he should, so ward the terrain he hooks off and don't get caught facechecking. When you all-in, R (Public Execution) blinks you behind him and suppresses through the grapple — that's how you pin a champion whose entire kit is built to disappear.","late":"First item is yours: Eclipse plus the Q max means Q1-auto-Q2 with your R's passive armor pen and on-ability healing halves his squishy frame the second you connect, and you hold up as a scaler into two items. The danger isn't his duel — it's the map. If he's fed off roams, his revive and crit burst can blow you up from a flank before you land R, so keep vision tight, never walk into his swing range low, and trust that your R lockdown beats his escape every time you actually catch him.","whys":["You're both weak at Level 1 — he can only poke with Q (Avengerang) and you have one ability, so last-hit clean and don't chase his Heroic Swing.","Your Q into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto out-trades his poke the moment he steps up to farm.","He swings out on Heroic Swing and kites your cooldowns, but your dash-weave combo punishes any time he stands still — it's a coinflip on who commits first.","Your combo cooldowns tighten and your empowered autos out-sustain his Q/W chip once you force a trade he can't grapple away from.","At 6 his E roams and W revive let him fight greedier and snowball off your weak window — respect the swing-out, don't get flanked.","Eclipse plus the lvl-9 Q max is your peak: Q1-auto-Q2 with R's armor pen and on-damage heal shreds him the instant R blinks you behind him.","You stay the cleaner scaler and your R suppress beats his disengage in every clean duel — just don't let a fed Akshan delete you from a flank first."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"aurora","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Land Cunning Sweep to unlock Sundering Slam, then Lacerate's near-total slow plus a Drakehound's Step dash lets you finally stick and weave an empowered auto before her E blink resets the gap."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind the farthest target and suppresses through her E blink or W exile — your first guaranteed catch on a champ built entirely around blinking away."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the Level 9 Q max: cone-Q into empowered auto into Sundering Slam, with R's flat armor pen and healing-on-ability-damage, chunks half her bar while Repudiation's shield eats her return poke."},{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Aurora's window — Twofold Hex free-pokes you while you hold one ability, no Sundering Slam follow-up and no dash threat to punish the recast."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her E blink early, then land Cunning Sweep so Lacerate's slow and a Drakehound's Step dash can stick before she resets the gap","Hold Public Execution to blink-suppress her the instant she E-blinks or W-exiles, then crash her down for the stun and weave empowered autos","Get to Eclipse and the Level 9 Q max where cone-Q into empowered-auto into Sundering Slam with R's armor pen and healing stomps her squishy bar"],"foe":["Poke with Twofold Hex and heal it straight back off Spirit Abjuration before your 6","Save Across the Veil and The Weirding to dodge your R and Lacerate's slow, denying every gap-close","Curse you with Twofold Hex and recast it through you, then leap out before your long early cooldowns buy an empowered auto"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 belong to her: you have one ability, no Sundering Slam follow-up and no dash threat, so she stands back, pokes with her Q and out-last-hits you for free. Don't throw Cunning Sweep at max range hoping to chip her — you'll just whiff the cone, eat a Q-root and burst in return. At 3 it flips: once you can land Cunning Sweep to unlock Sundering Slam and your Drakehound's Step dash is online, you can finally close, but bait her E blink first — if you commit Lacerate's slow into a held blink she's gone and you've burned your window. Last-hit safe, soak the poke, and look for the level-3 all-in only when her E is on cooldown.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your weak patch — your cooldowns are at their longest and she can root-and-burst on repeat while blinking out of your follow-up, so concede a little and farm toward six. Then Public Execution changes everything: it blinks you behind the farthest target and suppresses, the one tool that beats a champ whose entire identity is blinking away — time it onto her E blink or W exile and the suppress locks her in place, then crash her down for the stun and weave empowered autos. Don't ult into a held E if you can help it; bait the blink, then R the moment it's down.","late":"First item is your peak and it's a hard one for her — Eclipse plus the Level 9 Q max means cone-Q into empowered-auto into Sundering Slam, with R's flat armor pen and healing-on-ability-damage, chunks half her bar while Repudiation's shield blocks her return poke and amps your next slam. She stays a slippery teamfight threat with her blinks and W exile, so you don't get to ignore her, but the straight 1v1 is yours all game — there's no scaling cliff like a Vayne or Kayle here, just a squishy mage who folds the second your R lands. Force the all-in on her E cooldown and end the side lane.","whys":["You have one ability, no Sundering Slam and no dash, while her Q pokes you and out-last-hits you for free — concede the opening and farm.","At 2 a landed Cunning Sweep gives a trade, but your cooldowns are long and her E blink dodges the Sundering Slam follow-up, so it stays a coin-flip on her positioning.","Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step dash finally lets you stick once her E is down and weave an empowered auto she can't kite.","Your cooldowns are longest here and Twofold Hex's recast chunks you while Across the Veil removes the return — give ground and reach six.","Public Execution blinks you behind her and suppresses through her E blink and W exile — the one tool that catches a champ built to escape.","Eclipse and the Q max turn cone-Q into empowered-auto into Sundering Slam, with R's armor pen and healing, into half her health while Repudiation's shield eats her poke.","No scaling cliff here — she's a squishy mage who folds to your R suppress-and-stun, so the clean 1v1 stays yours into the late game."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"camille","win":["Skill","Camille","Camille","Skill","Skill","Camille","Camille"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Camille walks up and procs her Q second-hit true damage while your single ability and energy-gated cooldowns leave you unable to answer — concede CS and dodge her empowered Q auto rather than trading."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind Camille, suppresses her and crashes her down for a stun — your one window to flip a trade while her E hookshot is on cooldown so she can't wall-dash away."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Eclipse and the Level 9 Q max your Q1-empowered-auto-Q2 finally chunks her, but she answers with W's true-damage heal and Q sustain on any extended trade — the window reads even, not yours."},{"when":"Late","text":"Camille's R walls you into an isolated 1v1 her items win — Q and W true damage cut through your armor while your purely physical burst stalls on her resists and E wall-mobility kites your dashes."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 6 and use Public Execution's blink-suppress-stun to flip a trade while her E hookshot is on cooldown and she can't wall-dash off","Land a clean outer-edge Q into Sundering Slam to lock her, then slap Lacerate's near-total slow on so she can't reposition off terrain","Reach your Eclipse and Level 9 Q-max first-item window where Q1-empowered-auto-Q2 out-bursts her sustain"],"foe":["Land her E hookshot to stun you and cancel your Drakehound's Step dash chains mid-combo","Catch you in the outer half of Tactical Sweep — that half alone slows, hits harder and heals her","Stall lane even, reach 2+ items, then R-isolate you into a 1v1 her true-damage scaling wins"]},"early":"Her E hookshot is the whole early game — it stuns you and cancels your Drakehound's Step dash chains, so never throw a Q cone when you're inside its range with nothing to follow up. At Levels 1-2 you have one ability and brutally long cooldowns while she walks up and procs her Q second-hit true damage on you, so concede the CS and dodge her empowered Q auto rather than trying to trade. Bait her E onto a minion or a wall-dash, then look to land your outer-edge Q sweetspot into Sundering Slam and slap Lacerate's near-total slow on so she can't reposition off terrain.","mid":"Through Levels 4-5 you're in your weakest window — your cooldowns are longest and her Q-W sustain out-trades you, so farm and wait for your spike. At 6 you finally get a real answer: Public Execution blinks you behind Camille, suppresses her and crashes her down for a stun, and that's your one clean flip — burn it when her E hookshot is on cooldown so she can't dash a wall and stun you out of your combo. Don't waste R chasing a Camille who still has E up; she'll hookshot away, true-damage you down, and heal it back with W.","late":"This is where she takes it. Camille's R drops a wall around you and isolates you into a 1v1 her items are built to win — her W outer-cone true damage and Q second-hit cut straight through your armor stacking, and your damage is purely physical into her growing resistances. Your Eclipse-and-Q9 first-item window was the high point; at two-plus items she kites your Drakehound's Step dash chains with E wall-mobility, blocks your burst, and out-duels you. Don't take the isolated fight — group, force her off you, and make her splitpush instead of letting her catch you alone.","whys":["Camille walks up and procs her Q second-hit true damage while your single ability and energy-gated cooldowns leave you with no answer at Level 1.","Her Q-W poke and W heal out-trade you at Level 2 when your cooldowns are still long and you can't force an extended fight she'd lose.","Level 3 evens out — your outer-edge Q into Sundering Slam plus Lacerate's slow can punish a missed E hookshot, but it still threatens to cancel your dash chains.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window with your longest cooldowns, and her Q-W sustain simply out-trades you here.","At 6 your Public Execution blink-suppress-stun guarantees the gap-close and flips a trade while her E hookshot is down — your one stage to threaten a kill.","Your Eclipse and Level 9 Q-max let Q1-empowered-auto-Q2 finally chunk her, but her W true-damage heal keeps the window even, not yours.","At 2+ items Camille's R walls you into an isolated 1v1 her Q-W true damage, resists and E wall-mobility win as a hard scaler."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Her Miasma (W) grounds you the moment you commit, so the dash off Drakehound's Step gets denied and your ability-into-empowered-auto trade strands you in the poison cloud taking free Q (Noxious Blast) ticks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind her and suppresses through her kite — your one clean gap-close past the grounding, and if her Petrifying Gaze is down she can't cone-stun you out of the all-in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus the level-9 Q max: dodge a Miasma, Q1 (Cunning Sweep) into Q2 (Sundering Slam) and an empowered auto chunk her squishy frame before she can stack poison."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two-item Cassiopeia kites you forever — her Twin Fang (E) poison-procs out-DPS your physical-only burst and a forward Petrifying Gaze cone stuns you mid-dive while her no-boots move speed keeps the gap open."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait or sidestep her Miasma (W) so your Drakehound's Step dash and Lacerate (E) dash-out aren't grounded mid-trade","Hit 6 and use Public Execution's blink-suppress to close the range her poke keeps open — ideally while her Petrifying Gaze is on cooldown","Force your level-6-through-first-item all-in before her second item lands, since she only gets stronger after"],"foe":["Land Noxious Blast (Q) + Miasma (W) poison from max range and ground you the instant you dash so you eat free Twin Fang procs","Keep the lane long and kite on her no-boots move speed, refreshing Twin Fang (E) on poisoned targets to out-sustain your trades","Survive to two items where a forward Petrifying Gaze (R) cone stuns your dive and her DPS out-races your physical burst"]},"early":"Cassiopeia's Miasma (W) is the whole early problem: it grounds you, so the dash off Drakehound's Step is denied the moment you commit and weaving ability-into-empowered-auto just parks you in the poison cloud. Don't walk up to free-cast Q (Cunning Sweep) into a laid Miasma — she'll Noxious Blast you, ground you, and refresh Twin Fang while move-speeding away on her no-boots passive. Last-hit at max range, eat minimal poison, and respect that her sustained ranged DPS out-trades your weak level-1-through-3 cooldowns. Save Lacerate (E) and your dash for after she's spent her Miasma, not before.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are her cleanest poke window — short cooldowns for her, your longest for you, so keep farming and don't force a trade through a fresh Miasma. At 6 the lane flips: Public Execution blinks you behind her and suppresses through the kite she's relied on, so wait for her Petrifying Gaze to be down or for her to misposition, then R-in, brace Repudiation (W) to eat her return poison, and Q1 (Cunning Sweep) into Q2 (Sundering Slam) with an empowered auto. That blink-suppress is your only reliable answer to a champion who can ground every dash you have — but if she lands a forward Petrifying Gaze cone as you arrive, the all-in stalls, so respect her ult timer too.","late":"This is hers and you have to know it. A two-item Cassiopeia kites you out of every fight — her poison and Twin Fang procs out-DPS your physical-only burst, and a forward-aimed Petrifying Gaze cone stuns you mid-dive (it won't interrupt your near-instant R blink, but it pins you the moment you land) while she move-speeds around you on her no-boots passive. Your window was 6-through-first-item; if you didn't get a lead there, don't flip a sidelane 1v1 into her. Group, let your frontline force her Miasma and ult, and use Public Execution to peel or pick a softer target instead of diving the grounding.","whys":["She pokes with Noxious Blast (Q) + Miasma (W) poison from range while your one ranged-ish tool is energy-gated — and Miasma can ground your dash before you ever close the gap.","Her Miasma grounds you and her Twin Fang refreshes on poisoned targets, so your level-2 Q+E trade bleeds out the instant she denies your dash and sustains through it.","Your short combo comes online and you can dash-weave in brief windows, but her grounding can still cancel it on reaction — genuinely even and skill-dependent.","This is her strongest poke window and your longest cooldowns — she out-trades you with short CDs, so you concede and farm toward 6.","Public Execution blinks you behind her and suppresses through her kite — your one guaranteed gap-close past the grounding, flipping the lane if her Petrifying Gaze is down.","Eclipse/Profane plus Q max means a dodged Miasma lets Q1-Q2 and an empowered auto chunk her squishy frame in one all-in while Repudiation braces her return poison — force it now.","Two-item Cassiopeia kites and out-DPSes you, and her Petrifying Gaze cone stuns you only while you face her — turned away it is merely a slow."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"chogath","win":["Skill","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath","Skill","Skill","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q's cone unlocking Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step dash, you can land an empowered auto onto Cho'Gath the moment his Rupture knockup is on cooldown and he can't peel you off."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses and stuns through his Feast bulk for guaranteed lockdown — your cleanest all-in before his HP stacks pile up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus the Level 9 Q max: Q-cone into Sundering Slam plus an empowered auto chunks him while R's flat armor pen shreds his still-thin early tankiness."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once he has 6+ Feast stacks and his percent-HP true-damage R execute is online, your physical-only burst stops killing him through his armor and he reclaims the lane as a scaler."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait or sidestep his Rupture knockup, then dash in with Q-cone into Sundering Slam and an empowered auto while it's down","Hit Level 6 and use Public Execution's blink-behind suppress to land your hardest all-in before his Feast stacks pile up","Close the lane on your first-item Q-max spike before his percent-HP true-damage R and Feast scaling take over"],"foe":["Land Rupture to knock you out of your dash-into-empowered-auto window and interrupt the combo","Silence you with Feral Scream: no cast means no Drakehound's Step, so you have no dash","Drag the game past two items where his true-damage R execute ignores your R's healing and his HP outscales your armor pen"]},"early":"Cho'Gath's Rupture (the delayed ground-spike knockup) is the only thing that interrupts your dash chains, so never step into trade range while it's up — bait it out or walk through where the spike won't land. Once it's on cooldown his body is slow and immobile, exactly what you want: cast Q for the cone, dash in off your Drakehound's Step, and land the empowered auto before he can W-silence you mid-combo. He has no kill threat on you early, so don't poke aimlessly into his Vorpal Spikes and passive sustain — wait for the Rupture window and commit a real trade or take nothing.","mid":"This is your stretch of the lane, but it's still even on the clock — your cooldowns are long here too, so trade strictly on Rupture's timer and a clean dodge is worth more than forcing. At 6 your R is the unlock: Public Execution blinks behind him and suppresses through his bulk, so you ignore his size and burst him before Feast really matters. With your first item and Q max, Q-cone into Sundering Slam plus an empowered auto and R's flat armor pen chunks him while R's heal-on-ability damage keeps you topped. Just respect his W silence mid-combo — eat it early, not on your R cast.","late":"This is where it flips and you have to be honest about it. Six-plus Feast stacks make him a wall your physical-only damage can't punch through, and his R becomes a percent-HP true-damage execute that ignores the heal-on-ability your R gave you in lane. Your flat armor pen can't keep pace with his raw HP pool, and one missed dash into Rupture-into-R can delete you outright. Win the game on your mid-lane lead and your team's terms before ~25 minutes — if it goes long, he out-scales you cleanly and you become the one getting executed.","whys":["His Rupture can knock you out of a trade but he has no way to commit on you yet — last-hit safely and learn his Rupture cooldown timing.","Your dash-into-empowered-auto chain is real but your cooldowns are long and his Rupture still interrupts it, so it stays even — don't force extended fights.","Full combo online: dash his Rupture, then Q-cone into Sundering Slam and an empowered auto chunk his immobile body before he can W-silence you.","Your cooldowns are longest here and his Feast bulk is climbing — trade only when Rupture is down and bank small leads instead of all-inning.","Public Execution blinks behind him and suppresses through his size, giving you a guaranteed lockdown all-in before his HP stacks make him unkillable.","Eclipse/Profane and the Level 9 Q max with R's flat armor pen let your Q-cone-into-slam plus empowered auto chunk him while you stay full — your peak window.","Six-plus Feast stacks and his percent-HP true-damage R execute ignore your healing and outscale your physical-only damage — he owns the lane from here, so close it earlier."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"darius","win":["Skill","Darius","Darius","Skill","Skill","Darius","Darius"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Darius owns the opening: a single Crippling Strike (W) auto out-chunks your one ability and starts Hemorrhage bleed before your Q-into-Sundering-Slam combo is even online, and he heals off any Decimate (Q) outer-blade that clips you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution is your flip — it blinks you behind Darius, suppresses and stuns him for armor-pen burst, ending the trade before a five-stack Noxian Guillotine can execute you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus your level-9 Q max is your strongest window: Q-empowered-auto-Sundering-Slam chunks half his health while your R passive heal and W shield carry you through the bleed ticks."},{"when":"Whiff-punish","text":"Darius's whole lane is his E (Apprehend) pull: one landed grip drags you onto a Crippling Strike slow and outer-blade Decimate, locking in the long bleed-stacking all-in your dash kit is built to avoid."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive to 6, then open every all-in with Public Execution so the suppress lands before his E (Apprehend) can grip you","Dash out with Drakehound's Step the instant his E arm winds up, then punish the whiffed pull on its long cooldown","Reach Eclipse and your level-9 Q max and force the fight there, weaving Q-into-empowered-auto while your R passive heal offsets the bleed"],"foe":["Land E (Apprehend) to yank you onto his Crippling Strike slow and outer-blade Decimate, locking you in a long trade","Stack five Hemorrhage bleeds in every exchange to arm Noxian Guillotine before you can disengage with a dash","Keep trades long and grounded so your Drakehound's Step dash-chains never get the short-trade reset they need"]},"early":"Levels 1-5 belong to Darius and you have to respect that — one Crippling Strike (W) auto out-trades your single ability while you have no combo, and his Decimate (Q) outer blade heals him for every cone that clips you. Do not stand in E (Apprehend) range: a landed pull drags you onto that W slow and outer-blade Q, and that long, grounded trade is exactly the fight your dash kit wants to avoid right now. Farm with the tip of your Q cone, hold Drakehound's Step to dash out of any spin-trade before he can grip you, and if you must contest, make it one empowered-auto poke and leave — never a sustained exchange while Hemorrhage is ticking.","mid":"Level 6 is the whole matchup. Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses and stuns, and the armor-pen burst plus your R passive heal lets you flip a trade Darius would otherwise win — open with it so he is locked down before a five-stack Guillotine can execute you. Hold it until his E (Apprehend) is on cooldown; popping R into a fresh pull just hands him the long fight. Through levels 4-5 you are still conceding, so play for that one R window, not for raw trading.","late":"Your Eclipse spike and level-9 Q max are where this becomes genuinely even — Q-empowered-auto-Sundering-Slam chunks half his health while your W shield and R passive heal carry you through Hemorrhage. From here it comes down to who lands their key cast: your R suppress versus his E (Apprehend) into Guillotine. Force the all-in on his pull's cooldown, use your dash mobility to break his stickiness, and remember he stays a brutal side-lane duelist — do not solo him in a brush with five bleed stacks already on you.","whys":["Darius out-trades you at 1: Crippling Strike is a 5s attack reset, so the wind-up is the hit, and Hemorrhage bleeds before your combo exists.","His E (Apprehend) pull is the whole lane — one grip drags you onto the W slow and outer-blade Decimate, so don't give him the target.","His full chain (pull, W slow, healing outer-blade Q) out-damages your barely-online combo, and every exchange stacks bleed you can't out-heal yet.","This is your weakest window — longest cooldowns, no spike — while his five-stack Guillotine threat only grows; concede and farm toward 6.","Public Execution flips it: you blink behind him, suppress and stun for armor-pen burst, ending the trade before his execute can land.","Eclipse and your Q max draw it even — Q-auto-Sundering-Slam chunks him while R heal and W shield sustain the bleed, but his Guillotine keeps it a coinflip.","Even duel late: your Drakehound's Step mobility and R suppress trade blows with his Apprehend-into-Guillotine, so it comes down to who lands the key cast."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"drmundo","win":["Skill","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo","Skill","Skill","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Mundo's Infected Bonesaw cleaver costs him health to throw and does nothing back in melee, so walk up: cast Q and weave the empowered passive auto every time he winds up a cleaver, chunking him faster than his W regen ticks back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses and crashes him down with flat armor pen — but Goes Where He Pleases resists the first immobilising effect, so make him spend it before you commit your one kill window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level-9 Q max means Q outer-edge into Sundering Slam into empowered auto chunks half his bar, but his W passive heal and Maximum Dosage claw most of it back — he edges this trade on raw sustain."},{"when":"Late","text":"Maximum Dosage's percent-HP heal plus stacked armor outscale your physical-only burst — by two-plus items you can't kill him inside one R channel and his cleaver poke whittles you while you try."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk up on every Infected Bonesaw wind-up and punish it with a Q-into-empowered-auto before his percent-HP cleaver poke stacks up","Hit level 6 and use Public Execution's suppress, armor pen and ability-hit healing to burst him in one locked window","Win the lane outright before two items — anti-heal (Executioner's into Mortal Reminder) is mandatory or his W and R regen erase everything"],"foe":["Throw Infected Bonesaw cleavers to poke your percent-HP and refund his own health without ever stepping into Ambessa's dash range","Detonate Heart Zapper on top of you — the burst only heals him if it actually connects","Stall to two-plus items where stacked armor and Maximum Dosage's heal make your physical-only burst harmless"]},"early":"Mundo's whole early game is the Infected Bonesaw cleaver — it slows, chunks percent-HP, and refunds his health when it lands, so never eat one for free. The upside: at level 1 he throws the cleaver at a health cost and does almost nothing back in melee, so cast Q and weave your empowered passive auto each time he winds up to last-hit, chunking him faster than his W heals. Don't burn your Drakehound dash chasing a cleaver-slowed retreat — he wants you to overcommit while his regen ticks the trade back to even.","mid":"By level 3 your Q-into-Sundering-Slam and E slow are online, but Mundo's W regen and cleaver sustain quietly out-trade your dash-weave pokes — through levels 4-5, your weakest window with long cooldowns, he just heals through your chip. Wait for 6: Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses through his passive immunity, and the R passive heals you off every ability hit while its armor pen shreds his resistances. That suppress is your one clean kill threat before Maximum Dosage flips an obvious-loss fight — if he ults to survive, disengage and re-set rather than feeding the heal.","late":"This is where the lane slips away. Your damage is entirely physical, so once he stacks armor and has Maximum Dosage up, your Q-Slam-auto burst just gets healed back inside one R channel while his cleavers keep poking you. You MUST have anti-heal by your first completed item or none of your trades stick. Realistically you win this before two items or you don't win it — close it on your level-6 and first-item windows, take the tower, and roam, because a fed Mundo simply doesn't die to physical burst late.","whys":["At level 1 the Infected Bonesaw cleaver costs Mundo health and does nothing back in melee — cast Q and land your empowered passive auto every time he winds one up.","Your Q outer-edge into E slow sets up a trade, but cooldowns are long and his W regen sustains the chip — it's genuinely even, so take only short pokes.","Your dash-weave combo is online, but the cleaver poke and W regen out-sustain short trades — Mundo quietly wins the war of attrition here.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window with your longest cooldowns, and Mundo heals through your chip — concede the wave and farm toward your 6 spike.","Public Execution blinks you behind him and suppresses, but Goes Where He Pleases resists the first immobilising effect — bait the cannister out or your one window is spent.","Your Eclipse and Q-max burst chunk him, but Maximum Dosage's heal plus W regen claw it back — he edges the first-item trade on sustain alone.","His stacked armor plus Maximum Dosage eat your physical-only damage — without early anti-heal you can't kill him, so it becomes a coin-flip scaling race."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"fiora","win":["Skill","Fiora","Fiora","Skill","Skill","Fiora","Fiora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Fiora owns it: Lunge plus Vitals chip you for percent-max-HP true damage while your single ability has no chain behind it — but Riposte only stuns what it parries as an immobilise, so a thrown-away Q-cone buys the window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution is your flip — it blinks you behind her, suppresses (her Q dash can't break a suppress), then crashes down with passive armor-pen burst for a guaranteed all-in whenever her Riposte is on cooldown."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your hardest window: ability-into-empowered-auto chains via Medarda Maxim let you weave full combos while she's still building, so you out-trade her here as long as you respect the parry."},{"when":"Late","text":"At 2+ items she reclaims it — a single Riposte on your R or empowered auto stuns you and turns the duel, and her Vitals out-grind you over a long fight, so close before her duelist items come online."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her W parry with a throwaway Q-cone or E-slow, watch it whiff, then commit your ability-into-empowered-auto chain and R while Riposte is down","Reach Level 6 and first item, where Public Execution's suppress and your Medarda Maxim auto-weaving flip the duel in your favour","Keep trades short and explosive so her percent-HP Vitals never get the four-proc grind that wins her a drawn-out fight"],"foe":["Hold Riposte for your R — parrying an immobilise is the only way her stab stuns instead of slowing","Proc all four Vitals with Q dashes and autos to true-damage you down across a long trade your shields can't soak","Stall to 2+ items where Riposte plus her duelist spike out-duels your physical-only burst"]},"early":"Fiora owns these levels and you have to respect it — at 1 you have a single ability and she has a Q dash plus Vitals that chip you for percent-max-HP true damage. Do not throw a naked Q-cone or E at her: she'll Riposte it, stun you, and proc a Vital. Last-hit at max range, take the wave, and farm toward your combo at 3 — you don't have the cooldowns or the empowered-auto chain yet to win a stand-up fight, and her Vital sustain out-trades your single-spell pokes.","mid":"This is where you claw it back to even. At 6, Public Execution blinks you behind her, suppresses, and crashes down with passive armor-pen burst — her Q dash can't break a suppress, so as long as Riposte is on cooldown that's your kill window. The whole lane is a Riposte mind-game: bait the parry with a throwaway Q-cone or E-slow, watch it whiff, then dash-weave your Medarda-empowered autos and R. Levels 4-5 are still hers if you misplay the W, so only commit once you've seen Riposte go down.","late":"Your first-item window (Medarda-Maxim auto-weaving while she's still building) is the one stretch you clearly own — you can land full ability-into-empowered-auto chains, and on her Riposte cooldown you win every all-in. But don't kid yourself about the long game: at 2+ items Fiora is a dedicated duelist who reclaims the matchup. Her Vitals are percent-HP true damage your armor can't touch, and a single parried R or empowered auto flips the fight. Force the lane in your spike windows and look to splitpush or roam before her item-stacked duel takes over.","whys":["Fiora's lead: you have one ability and no chain while her Q dash and Vitals out-poke you — she Ripostes your only spell and procs a Vital off the punish.","Skill: by Level 2 your Q-cone plus E-slow lets you trade back, but her Vitals and Q spacing keep it a coin-flip — don't force a committal.","Skill: your combo is online at 3 and empowered-auto weaving evens the trades, but a well-timed Riposte still flips anything you commit.","Fiora's window: levels 4-5 are hers — your cooldowns are longest and a parried key cast plus a four-Vital proc out-trades you, so farm and wait for 6.","Ambessa's flip: Public Execution blinks behind her and suppresses through her Q dash — on Riposte's cooldown that's a guaranteed all-in into a kill.","Ambessa's spike: at first item your Medarda-Maxim ability-into-empowered-auto chains land before she's built her duelist items — out-trade her here.","Fiora reclaims it: at 2+ items her Vitals' percent-HP true damage ignores your armor and one parried R or empowered auto turns the duel."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"galio","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Galio's passive empowers his auto with bonus magic damage and his Q (Winds of War) tornado pokes you for free while your kit is one ability deep and energy-gated, so you can't trade back yet."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your short combo is online: Q-cone into the Sundering Slam line, weave a Lacerate (E) near-total slow, and dash-chain an empowered auto to out-trade his single-target Q poke before it recovers."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Galio's W (Shield of Durand) channels a damage-reduction taunt that can eat your entire R suppress-and-slam — bait the channel or wait it out before you commit Public Execution."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item plus Level 9 Q max is your peak: R's passive armor-pen and Q1-auto-Q2 chunk him through plating, and his magic-resist stacking does nothing against your pure physical damage."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and dash-weave Q-cone into Sundering Slam plus an empowered auto on the cooldown of his Justice Punch knock-up","Pre-brace W (Repudiation) into his Q tornado so the blocked poke amplifies your next slam, then commit","Bait or wait out his W taunt-channel before spending R so your suppress-and-crash actually lands"],"foe":["Poke you down with Q (Winds of War) tornadoes and passive magic-damage autos through your weak Levels 1-2 and 4-5","Land Justice Punch (E) knock-up to interrupt your dash chains and answer your engage","Channel W (Shield of Durand) to taunt you mid-combo, reduce your damage, and stall until his global R or jungler arrives"]},"early":"Galio out-pokes you early because you are one ability deep and energy-gated at Level 1 while his passive-empowered autos and Q (Winds of War) tornadoes chip you for free. Don't walk up to last-hit into Q range — soak the cone, farm safe, and wait. At Level 3 the maths flips: dash-weave the Q-cone into the Sundering Slam line, drop Lacerate for the near-total slow, and crash an empowered auto before his single-target poke recovers. Commit only once his E (Justice Punch) is spent — that knock-up is the one thing that interrupts your dash chain, it is 11s at rank 1, and he steps backward to wind it up, so the back-step is your cue. Pre-bracing W into his Q tornado turns his poke into an amplified follow-up slam.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your weakest window — your cooldowns are longest and his Q poke plus his tankiness let him farm even while chipping you, so concede and stack toward 6. At Level 6 respect his W: Shield of Durand is a charge he holds while moving slowly, and the taunt only lands on release, inside 275 units. Dash out of that radius during the charge and it hits nothing; feed your R into it and your whole combo is wasted. Bait it first, then re-engage on the 18s. Your R wants a clean window behind him, not a taunt he is holding.","late":"This is where I quietly win the side lane: my first-item spike and Q max let me Q1-auto-Q2 him for half his bar, and his entire identity — stacking magic resist — does nothing against my pure physical damage and R's flat armor pen. Plated Steelcaps and an early armor item are what actually scare me, not his MR. The catch is his global R: he can be losing our lane and still flip a fight across the map, so close this side before his ult and roams start mattering more than the 1v1 I'm winning.","whys":["Galio owns Level 1 — you are one ability deep and energy-gated while his passive-empowered auto and Q (Winds of War) tornadoes poke you for free.","It evens at 2: your Q-cone gives a slow-into-trade, but your cooldowns are long, so match his poke rather than force anything.","Level 3 is yours — the full short combo dash-weaves Q-cone into Sundering Slam and an empowered auto faster than his single-target poke recovers.","Galio reclaims 4-5: your cooldowns are at their longest and his 11s Q chip plus tankiness out-farm you while you stack toward your spike.","Six is even — your R suppress is a real kill threat, but his 275-range Shield of Durand taunts on release and eats the combo, so bait the charge first.","First item is yours: Q max plus R's armor pen mean Q1-auto-Q2 halves him, and his MR stacking is wasted against your physical-only damage.","Late stays a coin-flip — you win the straight 1v1 with armor pen and your W shield, but his 180s global R decides fights you are not even in."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"gangplank","win":["Skill","Gangplank","Gangplank","Skill","Skill","Gangplank","Gangplank"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Gangplank owns the opening — keg poke and periodic Trial by Fire strikes chunk you while your kit is just Cunning Sweep and a single second ability, with long pre-6 cooldowns and no real all-in until R."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution flips it: your R blinks behind the farthest enemy in the line, suppresses and stuns through his kiting, and Remove Scurvy can't cleanse a suppress — so the armor-pen passive and ability-damage heal let you commit before his barrel chain matters."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus a level-9 Q max is your peak — Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam chunks half a squishy GP while your passive refunds energy and your W shield keeps you full through his return poke."},{"when":"Late","text":"Gangplank reclaims it — full-build barrels crit for hundreds, Remove Scurvy cleanses every slow you have, and his global R impacts fights you're not in while your physical-only burst stalls into his climbing health and enemy armor."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach level 6 and land Public Execution behind him — the blink-suppress-stun ignores his kiting and Remove Scurvy can't cleanse a suppression","Hit your Eclipse/Profane first-item spike and force Cunning-Sweep-into-empowered-auto-into-Sundering-Slam all-ins before his barrel chain and crit out-trade you","Use your passive dash out of Lacerate and the E slow to close before Remove Scurvy cleanses it, then chain ability-into-empowered-auto in the extended trade"],"foe":["Chain and detonate barrels to poke you down and land the slow-and-crit before you ever close the gap","Pop Remove Scurvy to cure your Lacerate slow and heal, then kite out of empowered-auto range — it is 22s, so make him spend it early","Survive lane and scale — his full-build crit barrels and global R win the long game against your physical-only burst"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Gangplank — his barrel poke and passive crit autos out-damage you while your kit is just Cunning Sweep plus one more ability, with brutal pre-6 cooldowns and no all-in until you have R. Don't step up to free-throw a Q he can poke around; last-hit at the edge of Cunning Sweep and eat a little chip. Crucially, his W (Remove Scurvy) cleanses your E (Lacerate) slow, so don't burn your only commit tool expecting the slow to stick — if he cleanses it, your dash chain has nothing to chase and you're stuck in barrel range.","mid":"Level 6 is where you take over. Public Execution blinks you behind the farthest enemy in the line, suppresses and stuns regardless of how he kites, and the passive flat armor-pen plus the heal on ability damage turn a poke lane into a kill threat — and Remove Scurvy cleanses CC, but not an active suppression. Bait his W or wait until it's down, then R in, Q-sweetspot the outer cone, W to shield his return barrel, and run him down chaining empowered autos. Your Eclipse/Profane first-item spike plus the level-9 Q max is your hardest favor window: Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam halves a squishy GP while your passive refunds the energy.","late":"This is where Gangplank reclaims the matchup as the scaler he is. Full-build barrels crit for enormous bursts, Remove Scurvy cleanses every slow in your kit, and his global R lets him impact fights you're nowhere near. Your damage is entirely physical, so as the game stacks armor and his health climbs, even a clean R-into-combo stops one-shotting him. Win it in the mid-game — force every fight on your R cooldown and first-item timer — because once he's online globally, both the duel and the map tilt to him.","whys":["His keg poke and periodic Trial by Fire strikes punish you while your kit is one Q chain plus a single ability, long cooldowns and no R to commit — concede the opening.","Even with Q into E for a slow-and-trade, Remove Scurvy cleanses your slow and his barrels out-poke any extended trade — stay even, don't force it.","Your short ability-into-empowered-auto combo wins a dash-weaving trade, but his ranged barrel chain keeps you out of auto range — it's a coin-flip on whether he's cleansed your slow.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window — longest cooldowns, still no game-ending all-in — while his barrels and crit keep chipping; farm toward 6.","Public Execution blinks behind him, suppresses through his kite (and Remove Scurvy can't cleanse a suppress), and the armor-pen burst plus heal flips the lane into a kill.","Your Eclipse/Profane and Q max land Cunning-Sweep-empowered-auto-Sundering-Slam for half his health while your passive refunds energy and he can't W out of your R lockdown.","He out-scales hard: full-build crit barrels, Remove Scurvy cleansing every slow, and a global R that wins the map — close it before late game."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"gnar","win":["Skill","Gnar","Gnar","Skill","Skill","Gnar","Gnar"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q (Cunning Sweep) into its Sundering Slam follow-up plus a passive-empowered auto lets you punch back through mini-Gnar's boomerang once your Drakehound's Step dash-weave is online — only when his Q is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind mini-Gnar, suppresses him through his Hyper hop-kite, and the heal-on-ability sustains the all-in — your cleanest kill window before he builds full rage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse spike plus the Lvl 9 Q max: Q-cone, empowered auto, Sundering Slam chunks half his bar while R's flat armor pen and heal carry the dive through his kite."},{"when":"Mega rage","text":"Gnar's threat window: at full rage Rage Gene transforms him and Wallop's flat 7s area stun lands, while GNAR! only stuns if it throws you into a wall — never dash-chain into full rage near terrain."}],"wants":{"you":["Catch mini-Gnar with R to blink behind and suppress through his Hyper hop, then E-slow so he cannot kite back out","Land Q's outer-edge cone (double damage) and the Sundering Slam line to open every passive-empowered-auto trade","All-in during his low-rage windows while he is locked in mini form, before he can transform to mega"],"foe":["Kite in mini form with boomerang (Q) poke and Hyper move speed to deny your empowered autos and dash-weave","Build rage at range, then catch you mid-dash with Mega Gnar's flat 7s Wallop stun","Hold the transform for your R blink, then Wallop-stun and burst you into a wall while you are committed"]},"early":"Gnar owns the first levels — his mini-form boomerang (Q) and Hyper move speed poke you for free while your single ability and energy gate leave you little to answer with. Don't walk up to throw a Q he just hops away from; last-hit at the outer edge of your cone and eat a little poke. Once you hit 3, Q into its Sundering Slam follow-up plus a Drakehound's Step dash and a passive-empowered auto finally let you punch back in short trades — but only when his boomerang is down and his rage bar is low.","mid":"This is where you take over, but watch the rage bar like a hawk. With the full combo and Lacerate's near-total decaying slow online, you out-trade mini-Gnar: E to pin him, Q-cone, and weave the empowered auto so he can't hop away. At 6, Public Execution answers his kite — it blinks you behind him, suppresses through the Hyper hop, and the heal-on-ability plus R's armor pen flips the trade. The trap: never blow your dash chain into a full rage bar, or he transforms and the mega GNAR! knockback-stun turns your all-in into his kill.","late":"Your first-item spike (Eclipse, Q max) is your peak 1v1 — Q-cone into empowered-auto into Sundering Slam halves him and R still gaps his kite. But in grouped fights Gnar reclaims value: mega-form's AOE knockback-stun is exactly the hard CC that interrupts your dash chains, and your physical-only damage runs into the armor his team stacks. Snowball the side lane and force the 1v1 before fights get big — his transform timing is a coinflip you'd rather not gamble on once he's even.","whys":["Mini-Gnar's boomerang (Q) and Hyper move speed poke you for free while you have only one ability and no combo to answer.","You get Q+E for a slow-into-trade but cooldowns are long and his boomerang still out-ranges you — neither side commits, so farm it even.","Q-cone into Sundering Slam plus a dash-weaved empowered auto lets you win short trades the moment his boomerang is on cooldown.","Lacerate's near-total slow pins him so he can't hop-kite, and your full combo out-trades mini-Gnar through this window.","Public Execution blinks behind him and suppresses through the Hyper hop — his kite can't escape your R gap-close, burst, and heal.","Eclipse and the Q max make the cone-auto-Slam chunk half his bar while R's flat armor pen and heal carry the all-in.","It's a read: punish his low-rage windows and you keep winning, but GNAR! only stuns what it throws into a wall — fight in open lane and his transform is a knockback, not a kill."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"gragas","win":["Skill","Gragas","Ambessa","Gragas","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q cone into Sundering Slam plus E's near-total slow and a Drakehound dash all come online — first real window to pin a Body-Slammed Gragas and win a short empowered-auto trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks up to 1250 units to Gragas and suppresses him straight through the Body Slam escape, then slams him down stunned — your first hard kill threat."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane completion plus the level 9 Q max drops Q to 10s: Q1-auto-Q2 chunks half his bar, and Grievous Wounds on Happy Hour wins the AP brawl."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Gragas's biggest swing — Drunken Rage is a 5s cooldown, so the damage cut is always up and a Body Slam stun into Barrel Roll beats a half-built combo."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach level 3 and land Q's cone to unlock Sundering Slam, then E-slow and Drakehound-dash to keep him pinned for the empowered-auto chain","Hit 6 and blink 1250 units with Public Execution — the suppress beats his Body Slam escape and the stun holds him for Sundering Slam","Buy Executioner's early — Happy Hour heals him off every cast, and Grievous Wounds is what makes your extended trades actually stick"],"foe":["Sip Drunken Rage for the damage cut, stun you with Body Slam, then Barrel Roll out before your dash chain can answer it","Barrel Roll-poke you down at range and shove the wave so your weak early window never lets you all-in","Hold Explosive Cask, 100s at rank 1, to knock you off a dash the moment your Public Execution lands"]},"early":"Levels 1 and 2 are even — one ability and long cooldowns, while Drunken Rage's 5s cooldown hands him a permanent damage cut into a Body Slam stun you can't yet answer. Don't throw a lone Cunning Sweep he can Body-Slam through. At 3 it tips your way: land the Q cone to arm Sundering Slam, then Lacerate for the slow and Drakehound-dash to stay glued — Body Slam is 14s at rank 1, so it disengages once and no more. Brace Repudiation on his Barrel Roll, not the wave: non-minion damage blocked makes its slam hit harder.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your soft spot — your Q still sits on 13-11s while Drunken Rage refreshes every 5s, so farm and don't force extended fights without your combo up. At 6 you flip it: Public Execution blinks up to 1250 units to him, suppresses him straight through the Body Slam escape, then slams him down stunned — more lockdown than a 14s dash can trade with. Bait the Body Slam, dash in on its cooldown, and chain Q1-auto-Q2 with Lacerate. Watch Explosive Cask — on 100s he saves it to knock your dash away or flip you into his tower.","late":"First item is your peak — Eclipse or Profane plus the level 9 Q max drops the Q to 10s, so Q1-auto-Q2 halves his health while Repudiation's shield eats the return, and you beat him in a straight brawl. Unlike a hard-scaling carry, Gragas doesn't reclaim this lane at two items: he's an AP bruiser, not a kiter, so your R gap-close and ability-weaving stay ahead of him. Keep Grievous Wounds up — Happy Hour heals him off every cast, and that trickle is what drags your won trades back to even. The one late threat is a teamfight Explosive Cask catching you mid-dash.","whys":["You have one ability and long cooldowns, but so does he at 1 — neither of you commits, so deny his Barrel Roll last-hits and set up the lane.","Gragas can W-reduce and Body Slam into a Barrel Roll for a real trade, while your Q+E combo is still on long cooldowns — stay even and don't force it.","Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam, Lacerate's slow and the Drakehound dash all land inside Body Slam's 14s — take the short trade on it.","Drunken Rage is a 5s cooldown, so his damage cut never lapses while your Q sits on 13s — farm, and brawl only on a spent Body Slam.","Public Execution blinks up to 1250 units, suppresses him straight through the Body Slam escape and stuns — your first real kill threat here.","Eclipse/Profane plus the rank-5 Q at 10s chunks half his bar, and Executioner's cuts the Happy Hour heal he banks off every cast — force the all-in.","Gragas is an AP bruiser, not a scaling kiter, so your R gap-close and ability-weaving stay ahead of him through two items — keep winning the duel."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"garen","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Garen's Q silences you mid-cast, cutting off the ability chain that feeds your Medarda Maxim auto, and the empowered strike out-trades your single cone Q while every Ambessa cooldown is still long."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him and suppresses — suppression ignores his tenacity, so this is your first real flip; land it at low HP before his R execute threshold can save him."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the Q rank-up gives you the Q1-into-Sundering-Slam burst with an empowered auto between, but his missing-HP R means you must finish before you chunk him into execute range."},{"when":"Late","text":"His R's missing-HP true damage cuts straight through your R's flat armor-pen, and his W damage reduction blunts your all-in burst — extended fights hinge on whether you finish inside his ult timer."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 6 and land R to blink behind Garen and suppress him — suppression ignores his tenacity, so commit the armor-pen burst before he can react","Chain Q-W-E into empowered Maxim autos in extended trades where his short Q-strike-then-disengage can't sustain against your dash-weave","Hit your first-item Q1-into-Sundering-Slam window and force the all-in while his Q silence is on cooldown"],"foe":["Land Q to silence you mid-cast, break your ability chain so no empowered auto fires, then strike and disengage before your cooldowns return","Pop W to cut your R-burst with damage reduction and ride the passive regen so your chip never sticks","Bait your all-in, survive low, and flip you with the missing-HP R execute the moment you drop below the threshold"]},"early":"Garen owns the early game and it is all about Decisive Strike. The silence cancels whatever you are mid-cast on and breaks your passive chain, so the empowered Maxim auto never fires. Worse, that same Q breaks every slow on him, so Lacerate does not hold him for the follow-up. You cannot punish it yet: at Levels 1-3 you have one or two abilities, no full combo, and you are energy-gated. Farm with the outer edge of your Q, refuse extended trades you cannot win, and bait the 8s Decisive Strike before you commit any cast.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — his Q-strike-disengage out-trades my longest-cooldown window, and his passive regen heals the chip the second I back off. The lane flips at 6. My R blinks me behind him and suppresses, and suppression ignores his tenacity entirely, so the armor-pen burst lands clean; only the brief stun at the end of R is shortened by his W. Save R until his W is down or his HP is low enough that his own execute can't bail him out — that's the cleanest kill threat I get all lane.","late":"It evens back out late, and honestly so: this is a skill lane from items on. Your first-item Q1-into-Sundering-Slam chunks him, but Demacian Justice is missing-HP true damage, so poking him low instead of bursting him dead just hands him the execute. Courage's damage reduction cuts your biggest combo and that true-damage ultimate ignores your flat armor pen entirely. You win the fights you commit R to and finish inside his execute threshold; he wins the ones where Perseverance and Courage let him survive to flip it. Respect the 120s ult timer and never let a trade drag.","whys":["Decisive Strike silences you mid-cast and breaks your ability chain so no empowered Maxim auto fires, and at Level 1 you have one ability and no combo to answer his empowered strike.","His Decisive Strike into empowered strike out-trades your Level 2, where your cooldowns are long and you lack the energy to chain a second ability into an auto.","He silences the instant you commit and that same Q breaks Lacerate's slow, so your short Level 3 trade cannot hold him while Perseverance heals the chip.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window with your longest cooldowns, so his short trade plus Courage and Perseverance regen out-sustains you.","At 6 my R blinks me behind him and suppresses — suppression ignores his tenacity, so the armor-pen burst lands and flips the lane; only the end stun is shortened.","Your first-item Q1-into-Sundering-Slam burst trades evenly with his power, but the 8s silence and his missing-HP execute keep it a genuine coinflip on cooldowns.","Late it is skill: you win by committing R fully before his missing-HP true-damage execute threshold, he wins if Courage and Perseverance let him survive to flip it."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"graves","win":["Graves","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Graves"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Graves' point-blank spread out-trades your single ability before any Medarda combo exists — but his 4 bullets stop on the first unit, so last-hit from behind a melee minion."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks up to 1250 units and suppress-stuns through a Quickdraw dash — your first real flip onto a kiter who otherwise dashes away and reloads."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus your Lvl 9 Q max drops Q to 10s: Lacerate's slow into Q1-auto-Q2 chunks him inside the 22s hole between Smoke Screens, before he resets spacing."},{"when":"Smoke + 2 items","text":"His biggest window: Smoke Screen nearsights and slows you so the chase breaks, and a Quickdraw dashed into you grants two True Grit stacks right as your burst lands."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Lacerate's slow before he reacts, so Quickdraw is a reset he already spent when Drakehound's Step sticks for the empowered auto","Hold R for level 6 to blink behind him and suppress-stun through the kite, denying his dash-and-reload spacing","Rush Plated Steelcaps — his shotgun spread is the bulk of his damage, and the ranged-auto reduction blunts all four bullets at once"],"foe":["Burst you with a point-blank pellet spread then Quickdraw away before your Medarda-empowered auto resets onto him","Drop Smoke Screen on you to nearsight the chase and slow you out of the dash-weave","Dash Quickdraw into you for two True Grit stacks, then kite while your physical-only combo bounces off"]},"early":"Graves owns the very first levels — a point-blank pellet spread plus an End of the Line Q simply out-damages your one ability before your Medarda combo comes online, so don't step into his shotgun range to grab a single CS. New Destiny fires 4 bullets that stop on the first unit they hit, so last-hit with a melee minion between you and most of the spread never reaches you. Quickdraw is both his escape and his resist stacker, so land Lacerate's slow first, then Drakehound's Step sticks for the empowered auto and Sundering Slam.","mid":"This is where it tilts to you. At 6 Public Execution is the answer to a kiter: it blinks up to 1250 units to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses through his Quickdraw, and slams him down stunned — he can't just dash and reload anymore. Pair it with Lacerate's slow into Repudiation, bracing his pellet burst so the blocked damage amps your slam, and Q1-auto-Q2 chunks half his bar. What saves him is Smoke Screen on 26/24/22s: it nearsights you and slows on impact, so he breaks the chase inside it. Bait it or go once it's spent.","late":"Past two items it slides back to Graves and he can reclaim the lane. He builds bruiser-tanky for a marksman, and a Quickdraw dashed toward you grants two stacks of True Grit instead of one, so his armour and MR double at the exact moment your physical-only burst arrives — and his basic attacks keep shaving that 16s cooldown back down. Smoke Screen every 18s at rank 5 nearsights you and slows on impact, which is enough to break a chase in the open. Your edge is still the R flip — blink-suppress him onto your team before he resets spacing and you win the skirmish. Close it on your first-item spike.","whys":["His point-blank spread out-trades your single level-1 ability, but the 4 bullets stop on the first unit — last-hit with a melee minion between you and concede the rest.","Q+E gives you a slow into a trade, but Quickdraw dashes out first and his basic attacks keep shaving its 16s — roughly even here, so don't force it.","Your short combo is online and E's slow can pin him, but his pellet autos still match your dash-weave at this range — a skill trade over who lands first.","Your longest cooldowns against his peak kite — Quickdraw resets distance and Smoke Screen nearsights and slows you, so he edges the farm window.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units to him and suppress-stuns through Quickdraw — the one tool that beats a kiter, and your kill threat starts here.","Eclipse/Profane plus Q-max: Lacerate's slow into Q1-auto-Q2 lands inside the 22s Smoke Screen gap — that hole is your hardest favour window.","He builds bruiser-tanky and a Quickdraw dashed at you grants two True Grit stacks, so his resists double exactly as your physical-only burst arrives."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"gwen","win":["Skill","Gwen","Skill","Gwen","Ambessa","Ambessa","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q's cone slow plus a Maxim-empowered auto pins Gwen for the Sundering Slam — and if she answers with Hallowed Mist, step into it: inside, she is a normal target."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 units and suppresses her, landing you inside Hallowed Mist where she is targetable normally — the window she can't reposition out of."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus your level-9 Q max drops Q to 10s and lets Q-empowered-auto-into-Sundering-Slam chunk her before she stacks AP — with Executioner's stopping A Thousand Cuts refilling her."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once Gwen finishes her second AP item, Snip Snip's centre true damage walks through your armour and Skip 'n Slash refunds itself on hit, so her kite outlasts your dash chains."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade with Q's cone slow into a Maxim-empowered auto, and step inside Hallowed Mist rather than backing off it","Land Public Execution at 6 from point-blank so the suppress holds her while you stand inside her mist and finish the chain","Buy Executioner's early — A Thousand Cuts heals her off every champion hit and refills what you chip off"],"foe":["Drop Hallowed Mist and trade from inside it so your jungler and the rest of your team are locked out of the fight","Stack AP and chip with Snip Snip's centre true damage, healing off every hit","Reach 2+ items where centre true damage and a refunded Skip 'n Slash reclaim the duel"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a knife-fight you don't have to win. Q's cone slow into a Maxim-empowered auto can pin her for a Sundering Slam, and if she answers with Hallowed Mist, walk into it — the mist shields her from enemies standing outside, so a melee commit is already past it. What actually hurts is Snip Snip: 450 range, and true damage only down the centre of the cone, so hold its outer edge. Last-hit, build Maxim stacks, and respect that A Thousand Cuts heals her off every hit.","mid":"Level 6 is the equalizer. Public Execution blinks up to 1250 units and suppresses her, and it drops you inside Hallowed Mist where she is an ordinary target — the mist only locks out enemies who stay outside. Point it at her, not into the wave. Through 4-5 you concede short windows to Snip Snip's centre true damage on a 5s cooldown, so farm toward 6. With Eclipse and your level-9 Q max, Q-empowered-auto-into-Sundering-Slam halves her while Repudiation's shield eats the return. Fight with Grievous Wounds up.","late":"Be honest here: Gwen out-scales you. Past two AP items Snip Snip's centre true damage cuts straight through your armour stacking, Skip 'n Slash refunds part of its own cooldown every time she connects so the kite never lapses, and A Thousand Cuts heals her off your health bar. Your purely physical kit loses extended fights. Win it before then — close the lane on your 6 and Eclipse spikes, take plates, keep Grievous Wounds up, and let your team handle late Gwen instead of dueling her.","whys":["Snip Snip reaches 450 against your 650 Cunning Sweep, but you're energy-gated and comboless too — nobody owns the opening, so just deny her last-hits.","Q's cone slow into a Maxim-empowered auto trades fine — Hallowed Mist only shields her from enemies outside it, and a melee commit already puts you inside.","Your full ability-into-empowered-auto chain is online, but Snip Snip is a 5s cooldown of centre-line true damage — a skill trade over who spaces the cone.","Levels 4-5 are your longest cooldowns while Snip Snip sits near 5s — she chips you with centre-line true damage while you farm toward 6.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units and suppresses her, and it lands you inside Hallowed Mist where she is a normal target — the tool she leans on buys nothing.","Eclipse and Q max let Q-auto-Sundering-Slam chunk Gwen before she scales — force it here, with Grievous Wounds cutting the A Thousand Cuts heal.","Past two AP items Snip Snip's centre true damage ignores your armour and Skip 'n Slash refunds its own cooldown on hit — the physical kit loses the long duel."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"heimerdinger","win":["Skill","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Heimer's window: H-28 G turrets plus 1325-range Hextech Micro-Rockets zone you off the wave while you hold one Cunning Sweep and cooldowns too long to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution flips it — a 1250-unit blink over the turret wall into a suppress and a stun, and a 970-range grenade thrower has no answer to you at point-blank."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane Hydra with your level-9 Q max drops Q to 10s: Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam plus Lacerate's slow bursts him inside CH-2's 11s."},{"when":"Late","text":"Don't let the turret fortress go up — Hextech Affinity speeds him inside it, so clear turrets first and save R to blink onto him off the backline."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit 6 and blink 1250 units with Public Execution over the turret wall — the suppress and stun land before CH-2 can peel you off","Reach first item so Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam plus Lacerate's slow closes inside CH-2's flat 11s window","Weave Drakehound's Step out of each cast to cross turret fire, and leave the grenade's centre so it only slows"],"foe":["Nest H-28 G turrets and add 1325-range Micro-Rockets to chip you off the wave pre-6","Land CH-2 directly on you for the stun — the outer ring only slows — and reset the distance","Fight inside the nest, where Hextech Affinity's move speed keeps him ahead of your dashes"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Heimerdinger and you have to eat it. H-28 G Evolution Turrets plus 1325-range Hextech Micro-Rockets chip you off the wave while you hold one Cunning Sweep and cooldowns too long to trade back. Don't throw a Q into the nest — he answers with CH-2 Electron Storm Grenade and a turret volley. CH-2 only stuns whoever it lands directly on; the surrounding ring slows, so a sidestep downgrades the whole peel. Last-hit at the edge of your Q cone and farm toward 6 rather than proving a point.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay even-to-rough — your cooldowns sit at their longest, so farm and count CH-2, which is a flat 11 seconds at every rank. Level 6 is the flip: Public Execution blinks 1250 units over the turret wall, suppresses him and slams him down stunned, and a 970-range grenade thrower has nothing at point-blank. Bait the grenade first, and watch for UPGRADE!!! — it makes his next spell hit harder, so a held E becomes a far worse stun. Use Lacerate's slow and a Drakehound's Step dash to stay glued.","late":"First item is your peak — Eclipse or Profane Hydra with the level-9 Q max drops Cunning Sweep to 10s, so Q into empowered auto into Sundering Slam chunks half his health and you win any straight 1v1. The danger is the map, not the duel: his turret nest defends objectives and chokes teamfights, and Hextech Affinity hands him move speed inside it and near any allied tower. Close the lane before the fortress goes up, clear turrets instead of walking past them, and save R to blink onto him off the backline.","whys":["H-28 G turrets and 1325-range Hextech Micro-Rockets zone you while one Cunning Sweep can't punish back — last-hit at Q range and eat the poke.","Turrets plus CH-2 Electron Storm Grenade answer any step-up, and its 11s never shortens — your level 2-3 combo can't break that wall yet.","Your short combo is online, but a direct CH-2 hit plus a turret volley out-trades your dash-weave here — stay even and farm.","Your cooldowns are longest here while Micro-Rockets tick every 9s — concede the window and learn his CH-2 timer for 6.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units over the turret wall, suppresses and stuns him — a 970-range grenade thrower has no answer at point-blank range.","Eclipse/Profane Hydra with Q max makes Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam burst him from full inside CH-2's flat 11s — force every all-in now.","You own the straight duel with items, but Hextech Affinity speeds him up inside his own nest — end the game before that fortress matters."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"illaoi","win":["Ambessa","Ambessa","Illaoi","Illaoi","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Casting any ability gives you a Medarda Maxim empowered auto with bonus range and damage, so you out-trade a one-ability Illaoi in raw last-hits before her tentacles exist."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Illaoi's window: Test of Spirit on 16s, and the spirit echoes a share of every hit it takes straight back onto you while your own cooldowns are at their longest."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your flip — Public Execution blinks 1250 units and suppresses, dragging her off her tentacles, and Leap of Faith spawns one tentacle per champion hit, so solo that is one."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus Q max is your turning point — Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam chunks her, the rank-5 Q returns in 10s, and Grievous Wounds starves the tentacle heal."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge Test of Spirit; if it lands, stay on the spirit and kill it, because distance from it is what turns you into a Vessel","Fight in open lane, since tentacles only spawn on impassible terrain","Reach Eclipse and Q max, and buy Grievous Wounds — every tentacle that hits you heals her up"],"foe":["Land Test of Spirit so you fight her vessel and your own spirit at once","Land Harsh Lesson every 4s so nearby tentacles swing at you and heal her","Leap of Faith into a group, where each champion hit spawns her another tentacle"]},"early":"Level 1 is genuinely yours — Illaoi has one ability and no tentacles, so casting an ability for a Medarda Maxim empowered auto wins the straight last-hit trades. Her tentacles only swing at spirits, Vessels, and whoever she lands Harsh Lesson on, so the 4-second leap is what you dodge, not the ground itself. And they spawn on impassible terrain, so the open middle of the lane is the safe half. If Test of Spirit does land, stay on your spirit and kill it — walking away from it is what turns you into a Vessel. By level 3 her Tentacle Smash poke out-sustains my long cooldowns, so farm at range and wait for six.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are Illaoi's window, not mine — my cooldowns are longest while her tentacle count peaks, so I trade only when Test of Spirit's 16 seconds are ticking. Six is mine: Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses, and drags her off her tentacles. Leap of Faith answers with one tentacle per champion it hits, so in a solo lane that is exactly one — respect the damage, not the wall. Commit once she has spent Test of Spirit, and stay off Harsh Lesson's 4s leap.","late":"My Eclipse and Q max are where I finally pull ahead — Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam chunks half her bar, the rank-5 Q comes back in 10 seconds, and Drakehound’s Step refunds energy on every empowered auto so I go again. She never falls off the way other bruisers do: tentacles spawn on impassible terrain, so any grouped fight along a wall is hers, and I want her isolated in the open with Public Execution ready to yank her out. Anti-heal is non-negotiable — Prophet of an Elder God heals her every time a tentacle damages a champion.","whys":["You own level 1 — Illaoi has only her Q and zero tentacles, so casting an ability for a Medarda Maxim empowered auto wins the raw last-hit exchanges outright.","Even now: her Q-slam poke trades with your Lacerate slow, but both of you are fragile and her tentacles aren't stacked yet, so neither commits.","Illaoi takes it — your spirit echoes a share of every hit it takes back onto you, and your level-3 cooldowns are too long to race that.","Your weakest window against her strongest: longest cooldowns while her tentacle count peaks, so concede and farm away from the walls.","Six is yours — Public Execution blinks 1250 units and suppresses her off her tentacles, and Leap of Faith answers a solo laner with a single tentacle.","Eclipse plus the rank-5 Q at 10s turns it — your burst beats her tentacle healing the moment Grievous Wounds is on her.","Your Q max out-damages her and Public Execution yanks her off the tentacles — late fights go to whoever isolates first, and that is you."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"irelia","win":["Skill","Irelia","Skill","Irelia","Ambessa","Skill","Irelia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Irelia's Q (Bladesurge) costs 15 mana, heals her on the way in, and refreshes whenever the target is Marked or dies, while Ionian Fervor stacks attack speed off her spells — with only Cunning Sweep up, pull the wave so her reset lanes dead-end."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your combo comes online — bait her Q-dash in, then drop E (Lacerate) so the slow pins her before she can Bladesurge to a minion and reposition, and land a Medarda-empowered auto on the trapped target."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution is your flip: a 1250-unit blink into a suppress that holds clean through Bladesurge, with Lacerate's slow denying the reset — your one clearly favoured all-in window, on 130s."},{"when":"1st item + late","text":"Irelia's biggest threat: once Trinity Force lands, her on-hit DPS plus Vanguard's Edge — which Marks you for a free Bladesurge and walls off your exit — out-trades your burst between R cooldowns. Close the lane before she snowballs."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her Q-dash forward, then land E (Lacerate)'s slow so she cannot Bladesurge to a minion and reset out before your empowered auto lands","Hold for Level 6 and blink 1250 units with R, suppressing clean through Bladesurge, then finish before Defiant Dance's 20-second charge comes back around","Buy Grievous Wounds early — Bladesurge heals her on every dash in, and that steady trickle is what pays for all the trades she starts on you"],"foe":["Bladesurge off your minions or off a Marked you, healing on each dash and repositioning free","Land Flawless Duet’s stun — it Marks you, and that Mark instantly refreshes Bladesurge for a free dash right onto you","Charge Defiant Dance into your physical burst, then land Vanguard’s Edge to Mark you again and wall off your escape route"]},"early":"Irelia owns the opening — Bladesurge dashes onto any target, heals her on the way in, and refreshes the moment that target is Marked or dies, so she dances around your single Cunning Sweep while energy and long cooldowns leave you flat. Do not step up to throw a cone she just dashes out of; manage the wave so her reset paths dead-end, and last-hit at the outer edge where Cunning Sweep doubles. At 3 you finally have E (Lacerate): if she Q-dashes onto you, drop the spin so the slow pins her before she can Bladesurge to a minion, and only then commit a Medarda-empowered auto. Respect Flawless Duet — its stun Marks you, and that Mark refreshes Bladesurge instantly, so eating it hands her a free dash straight back onto you.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your worst window and hers to abuse — your cooldowns are longest while Flawless Duet returns every 16 seconds, so farm toward 6 and refuse extended fights unless she whiffs it. Level 6 is the flip you have been waiting for: Public Execution blinks 1250 units and suppresses straight through the Bladesurge mobility she disengages with, and Lacerate's slow means she cannot reset away from the all-in. Bait Flawless Duet and the Defiant Dance charge first — it cuts physical damage while she holds it, and physical is all you deal — then R once both are spent.","late":"This is Irelia's game to reclaim. Once Trinity Force lands and Ionian Fervor stacks, her on-hit DPS chunks you through trades, Vanguard's Edge Marks you for another free Bladesurge and drops a slowing wall across your retreat, and Defiant Dance cuts the physical burst you need your R for — which is 130 seconds between fights. Whatever armour she buys compounds it. Win or heavily pressure the lane around your Level 6 and first-item spike; past that she dances out of your all-ins and takes over as a splitpush threat.","whys":["Bladesurge resets off a dying minion and Ionian Fervor stacks attack speed off her spells, while you hold one energy-gated cone — concede the opening.","At 2 her Q-reset into trade beats your long cooldowns, and Bladesurge heals her on every dash in — you have no dash yet to catch it.","At 3 Lacerate's slow pins her between resets and an empowered auto answers, but Defiant Dance cuts physical damage while she charges — genuinely even.","Your longest cooldowns while Flawless Duet returns on 16s and its Mark hands her a free Bladesurge — farm, do not fight.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units and suppresses through Bladesurge while Lacerate's slow denies the reset — the one all-in she cannot dance out of, so spend the 130s here.","Q-max with full Medarda stacks chunks her on a clean combo, but Defiant Dance eats physical damage as it charges and Trinity answers — contested, not owned.","Trinity Irelia out-DPSes with on-hit, Marks you with Flawless Duet or Vanguard's Edge for a free Bladesurge, and cuts your physical burst with Defiant Dance."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"jax","win":["Skill","Jax","Ambessa","Jax","Ambessa","Ambessa","Jax"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With Q unlocking Sundering Slam and Lacerate's slow pinning him, you chain two empowered autos in a short trade — but only once his 17-second Counter Strike is spent."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 units and suppresses through his leap — your cleanest all-in. Counter Strike dodges basic attacks only, so spend abilities into it and save the empowered hit."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level-9 Q max drops Q to 10s, giving a Q1-auto-Q2 empowered burst before his Trinity Force rhythm and resist stacking out-trade you."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once Jax stacks Trinity into Steelcaps and an armour item, his ultimate adds resists and bonus magic damage on every third attack, and he wins the extended fights."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to unlock Sundering Slam, then Lacerate to pin him and chain empowered autos once his 17s Counter Strike is spent","Reach 6 even, then Public Execution for the suppress — pour abilities into a raised Counter Strike and hold the empowered auto","Cash your first-item Eclipse window on the Q max before his Trinity Force and Steelcaps come fully online"],"foe":["Raise Counter Strike to eat your empowered autos, then stun you mid dash-chain","Leap Strike in and Empower on a 7s cooldown, then disengage before your energy refund lets you re-engage","Scale to Trinity Force, Steelcaps and his ultimate’s resists, then take over every extended duel at 2+ items"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are even and you have no combo yet — don't throw a lone Q into his 700-range Leap Strike, since one ability and an empowered auto lose to it plus Empower. The early game lives on his E: Counter Strike dodges basic attacks for its duration, so your empowered autos vanish into it while every ability you cast still lands. At 3 your window opens — land Q to unlock Sundering Slam, drop E for the slow, and take a SHORT trade once his 17s E is spent.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your weakest patch — your cooldowns are longest while Empower refreshes every 5 seconds for 30 mana, so farm and don’t force a trade you’ll lose. Six flips it: Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses him and slams him down stunned, and that chain beats a 700-range leap. The trap is Counter Strike, 17s at rank 1: if it is raised when you land, pour abilities into it — they connect — and hold the empowered auto until the counterattack has fired, then finish him.","late":"Your first-item Eclipse spike with the Q max is your last clean favor window — the rank-5 Q returns in 10s, so Q1-auto-Q2 chunks him before Trinity Force lands. After that he reclaims the duel: his ultimate adds armour and MR and makes every third consecutive attack deal bonus magic damage, Steelcaps walls your physical burst, and Counter Strike is down to a 9-second cooldown. Don’t solo a two-item Jax — split, take towers, and save R for picks.","whys":["You're one ability and energy-gated at level 1 with no combo, and so is he pre-Empower — neither side wins, just deny his last-hits.","At 2 he leaps 700 units in and Empower-bursts on a 7s cooldown while your long early cooldowns sit idle, so he edges the level.","Landing Q unlocks Sundering Slam and Lacerate's slow pins him for chained empowered autos, provided his 17s Counter Strike is already spent.","Your cooldowns are longest at 4-5 and a leveled Jax out-duels you here — he owns the window, so concede and farm to 6.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units into a suppress and stun; Counter Strike only dodges autos, so cast through it and hold the empowered hit.","Your Eclipse plus Q max delivers a Q1-auto-Q2 chunk that beats him before Trinity Force completes — force it before he spikes.","Two-item Jax stacks his ultimate’s resists and Steelcaps while every third attack adds magic damage, so he out-scales your physical burst."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"jayce","win":["Jayce","Skill","Skill","Jayce","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Jayce fires Shock Blast through Acceleration Gate, which raises the missile's speed, range and damage, chunking you from a screen away while you hold only Cunning Sweep — last-hit at max range and eat the least poke you can."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution flips it: a 1250-unit blink, a suppress that holds through the Thundering Blow knockback, then a slam and a stun — 130 seconds spent closing the one gap Jayce spends the whole lane maintaining."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus the Lvl 9 Q max drops Cunning Sweep to 10s — Q into Sundering Slam, then a Drakehound's Step empowered auto, chunks half an escape-less Jayce in one chain."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Jayce's biggest window: he sits in cannon stance and gate-boosted Shock Blast denies your last-hits, so you never build the Medarda Maxim stack you need to close."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the Shock Blast poke to 6, then Public Execution to suppress and stun straight past the Thundering Blow knockback","Land Cunning Sweep's cone to unlock Sundering Slam, then chain a Drakehound's Step empowered auto in one trade","Hold Repudiation's brace for a telegraphed Shock Blast so the blocked champion damage amplifies the slam that follows"],"foe":["Keep you at gate-boosted Shock Blast range so you can never stack a Medarda Maxim empowered auto","Swap to hammer for the bonus Armor and MR, then land Thundering Blow to knock you out of your dash chain","Poke you below half pre-6, then swap to cannon so his first attack shreds your resists"]},"early":"Jayce owns the opening — Shock Blast fired through his Acceleration Gate gains missile speed, range and damage, and at Lvl 1 you only have Cunning Sweep with no Sundering Slam to answer it. Don't walk up to throw a Q he just steps back from; farm at max cone range and accept the chip. Your one tool is Repudiation: brace it into a telegraphed cannon Shock Blast so the blocked champion damage amplifies your next slam instead of eating poke for free. And note Thundering Blow is only 240 range — if he is close enough to knock you back, he is already inside Lacerate.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — Shock Blast is back every 12 seconds while your cooldowns sit at their longest, so he pokes and you farm toward 6. Then it flips hard: Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses straight through the Thundering Blow knockback and slams him down stunned, and a Cunning-Sweep-into-Sundering-Slam empowered-auto chain turns a poked-out Jayce into a kill. Bait the hammer E first — 240 range and 20 seconds at rank 1, so once he spends it your dash chain has nothing to cancel it. Land the Q cone, dash off Drakehound's Step into the empowered auto.","late":"It evens back out — you're a clean AD bruiser with strong ratios and short cooldowns, but Jayce never stops poking and his cannon-to-hammer burst stays relevant from range. The swap is only 6 seconds, and it hands him bonus Armor and Magic Resist the moment he picks up the hammer to fight your physical burst. You win every time you land Public Execution and close; you lose every time he gate-kites Shock Blast into Thundering Blow. Make him over-step into your Q cone and a Repudiation-amplified slam.","whys":["Shock Blast through Acceleration Gate gains speed, range and damage while you hold one Cunning Sweep — concede the opening and last-hit at range.","Cunning Sweep plus Lacerate's slow sets up a trade, but Thundering Blow knocks you out of it and his weapon swap is a 6s cooldown — stay even for now.","Your Q-into-Sundering-Slam is online, and Thundering Blow is only 240 range — if he is close enough to knock you back, he is inside Lacerate.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window, cooldowns at their longest, while Shock Blast returns every 12 seconds — so you farm and wait for 6.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses past the Thundering Blow knockback and stuns — 130 seconds spent closing the one gap he cannot reopen.","Eclipse/Profane and the Lvl 9 Q max drop Q to 10s, so Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam into an empowered auto halves an escape-less Jayce.","He swaps to hammer for bonus Armor and MR against your physical burst — you win on every landed R, and lose on every Shock Blast trade."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"karma","win":["Karma","Karma","Skill","Karma","Ambessa","Skill","Karma"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Karma's Inner Flame (Q) reaches 950 against your 650 cone and chips you on every walk-up, and Mantra is already live at level 1 without a skill point — so eat minimal poke and farm off your passive stacks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution (R) is your flip: it blinks 1250 units to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses, then slams her down stunned — 130 seconds buying more lockdown than her 12-second tether answers."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse online with Q lets you chain Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus empowered autos to delete her — force it while Mantra's 40 seconds and her flash are both down."},{"when":"W tether","text":"Karma's real lockdown is Focused Resolve (W), not her ultimate: a 675-range tether on a flat 12 seconds that roots you only if it survives, and heals her when she Mantras it."}],"wants":{"you":["Break the Focused Resolve tether with a Drakehound's Step out of range or behind terrain, so it never converts into the root","Chain Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam with passive-empowered autos to close the gaps her E move speed opens","Get Eclipse and Q max, and buy Grievous Wounds, since a Mantra-empowered tether heals her mid-trade"],"foe":["Poke you with 950-range Inner Flame on every walk-up, which also keeps shortening her Mantra cooldown","Land Focused Resolve and keep the 675-range tether intact so it converts into a root mid-combo","Use Inspire's shield and move speed to soak your Repudiation slam and walk out of your empowered autos"]},"early":"Karma owns the opening — Inner Flame (Q) reaches 950 against your 650 cone and your dash only fires off the back of an ability cast, so every walk-up to last-hit trades health for a creep. Do not try to fight through her poke at Levels 1-2; your cooldowns are long and Inspire (E) hands her a shield and move speed the moment you commit. Last-hit at range, lean on the empowered auto from your passive stacks, and brace Repudiation into her Q so the blocked damage amps your next hit. And know that Mantra is available from level 1 and costs no skill point — the empowered cast exists from wave one.","mid":"Through Levels 4-5 you're still conceding — her poke compounds and Gathering Fire shortens Mantra every time a damaging ability lands. Level 6 is your one real flip: Public Execution blinks 1250 units to the farthest champion in your chosen line, suppresses, then slams her down stunned. The root is Focused Resolve (W), flat 12 seconds at 675 range, and it only converts if the tether survives — a Drakehound's Step out of range or behind terrain breaks it first. Bait Inspire's shield, then R and chain Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam.","late":"This stays a fight against her range. Your first-item Eclipse spike gives real kill threat when your R is up, but two items of poke plus Focused Resolve's 12-second tether let her chip you out before you can ever commit, and Inspire's shield soaks the front of every combo. Buy Grievous Wounds — a Mantra-empowered tether heals her while it extends the root. Pick your all-ins around Mantra's 40 seconds and her flash, and accept that without a Level 6 snowball she scales past you.","whys":["Inner Flame reaches 950 against your 650 cone and your dash needs an ability mid-cast to close, so you eat poke while farming.","Her Q poke and Inspire's shield-and-move-speed beat your trades before 6, and Gathering Fire shortens Mantra every time one of them lands.","Your Q-into-Sundering-Slam punishes a missed Inner Flame, but Focused Resolve's 12s tether keeps it genuinely coin-flip.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window — no commit tool yet — while her 5-second Q poke compounds.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses and stuns — more lockdown than a 12-second tether can answer.","Eclipse plus Q lets your Cunning-Sweep-into-empowered-auto chain burst her squishy frame, but only while Mantra's 40 seconds and her flash are down — coin flip.","Two items of poke plus a Mantra-healed Focused Resolve root let her kite and chip you out before you ever commit."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"kassadin","win":["Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Kassadin","Kassadin","Kassadin","Kassadin"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Cunning Sweep into the unlocked Sundering Slam plus a Lacerate slow is your one clean kill window — Kassadin has no Riftwalk yet and can only walk out of the chain."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Riftwalk flips the lane: a 500-range blink on 5 seconds at rank 1 and 2 by rank 3, and he simply leaves your Public Execution and Lacerate dash behind him."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Catalyst and Rod of Ages plus Null Sphere's shield keep him healthy, while stacked Riftwalks dodge every empowered-auto window and each extra blink only costs him mana."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two-item Kassadin one-shots out of a 2-second Riftwalk, Nether Blade adds bonus magic damage to his autos every 7 seconds, and Force Pulse's cone slow charges off the spells you cast near him."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Cunning Sweep, fire the unlocked Sundering Slam (doubled on the first body), then ride the Lacerate slow in with a Drakehound's Step dash before Riftwalk exists","Force every all-in BEFORE 6 and deny him farm so his Riftwalk timer and Catalyst/RoA stacks arrive late","Space your casts, because spells thrown near Kassadin are what charge up his Force Pulse cone"],"foe":["Soak XP safely behind Null Sphere's shield and reach 6 for Riftwalk","Stack Catalyst and RoA charges, then Riftwalk out of your Public Execution and Lacerate dash","Reach 2 items, where a 2-second Riftwalk and his burst simply delete you"]},"early":"Pre-6 is the only part of this lane that's yours, so be greedy with it. Kassadin has no mobility until Riftwalk, and Null Sphere's shield absorbs magic damage, so your entirely physical kit walks straight through it. At level 3 land Cunning Sweep to unlock Sundering Slam (doubled on the first body), then ride your Lacerate slow in with a Drakehound's Step dash. Void Stone lets him ignore unit collision, so the wave will never hold him for you.","mid":"Level 6 is where this lane turns on you. Public Execution still guarantees the blink, suppress and stun, but Riftwalk is a 500-range blink on 5 seconds at rank 1 and 2 by rank 3, so he leaves every Lacerate dash behind and the lockdown stops converting. Spend your one R the instant he wastes a Riftwalk, while 5 seconds is still a real window. And watch Force Pulse: spells cast near him are what charge it, so your own weave loads his slow.","late":"This is lost if it goes long, full stop. Two-item Kassadin Riftwalks in on a 2-second cooldown, one-shots, and Riftwalks out. Nether Blade loads his autos with bonus magic damage every 7 seconds, and Force Pulse's cone slow charges off the very spells you weave. You deal almost purely physical damage into a target you can't pin, while Catalyst and RoA sustain blunt what you land. Your only realistic win was closing off your pre-6 lead — group and take towers.","whys":["Null Sphere's shield absorbs magic damage and your kit is physical, but at level 1 you have one ability and no Sundering Slam unlocked, so neither of you commits — even.","He's an immobile melee-range AP, but Void Stone walks him through your minions and your cooldowns are long — you trade without killing.","Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus the Lacerate slow out-trades a Kassadin with no Riftwalk yet — his only escape here is walking away.","Your weakest window — longest cooldowns, and Force Pulse charges off the spells you cast near him while he farms toward his spike.","Riftwalk is a 5-second blink at rank 1 and just 2 seconds at rank 3, so he leaves your Public Execution and your Lacerate dash behind him.","Your Eclipse spike is real, but Catalyst and RoA sustain absorb your burst while stacked Riftwalks kite every empowered auto you load.","Two-item Kassadin one-shots out of a 2-second Riftwalk and Nether Blade loads his autos with magic damage — physical burst can't pin a blinking assassin."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"kayle","win":["Ambessa","Skill","Ambessa","Kayle","Ambessa","Ambessa","Kayle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus the Lacerate slow comes online — your first real all-in window, on a Kayle whose Divine Ascent range and speed have barely started ramping."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses and stuns — her only out is Divine Judgment, 160 seconds at rank 1, so spend a Radiant Blast trade baiting it and R the moment it drops."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus your Level 9 Q max drops Q to 10s — Cunning Sweep, empowered auto, Sundering Slam chunks half her HP while she is still melee; force every all-in here, with Grievous Wounds up."},{"when":"Late","text":"At 2+ items Kayle's ranged form kites your dash chains from outside empowered-auto range, Radiant Blast strips the resists you bought, and Divine Judgment voids the all-in outright."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 for the full Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam combo with the Lacerate slow, and trade on a melee, ranged-formless Kayle","All-in at 6 and First item before her spikes — bait Divine Judgment's 160 seconds in a trade, then land Public Execution's suppress-stun as the invuln ends","Deny her CS and XP every wave, and buy Grievous Wounds against Celestial Blessing's 15-second heal"],"foe":["Poke with 900-range Radiant Blast, which also strips your resists, then walk back the second your Q is spent and your energy has run dry","Pre-cast Divine Judgment to eat your Public Execution crash, then heal back up with Celestial Blessing","Farm to two items so her ranged-form on-hit DPS kites your physical-only damage from outside your dash range and out-scales you"]},"early":"Kayle has no ranged form and is one of the weakest level-1s in the game, but so are you — one ability, no Sundering Slam follow-up yet, and you're energy-gated, so don't throw a lone Cunning Sweep expecting to win the opening. Farm with the outer edge of the Q cone for the doubled damage and wait for Level 3, when Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus the Lacerate slow lets you dash-weave an empowered auto onto a melee Kayle who can't kite you yet. Trade when your Medarda Maxim stack is up, then walk out the instant your energy is spent — Divine Ascent's attack speed and a Starfire Spellblade reset out-poke a standing brawl.","mid":"This is your window, and it's a race against her scaling. At 6 Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses and crashes her for the stun — her only escape is Divine Judgment, and that is 160 seconds at rank 1, so force her to spend it in a Radiant Blast trade first, then ult the moment it drops. Through Levels 4-5 your cooldowns are at their longest and she's farming toward her spike, so don't whiff a combo and concede the wave. By First item, with Eclipse and your Level 9 Q max, Cunning Sweep into an empowered auto into Sundering Slam halves her health while she's still melee — and keep Grievous Wounds on her, because Celestial Blessing heals every 15 seconds.","late":"You lose the late game, full stop. At 2+ items Kayle's ranged form lets her kite your dash chains from outside empowered-auto range, her on-hit damage shreds you, and Divine Judgment turns every all-in into a wait where she simply walks away. Radiant Blast also reduces the resistances of everyone it pierces, so your armour buys less than it should while your own damage stays entirely physical. Win this lane before her two-item spike — deny her CS, crack her tower, and convert early leads into objectives. If it goes long, only commit while Divine Judgment is on cooldown.","whys":["Kayle is a bottom-tier level-1, but so are you with one ability and no Sundering Slam — last-hit on the Q edge and don't force the opening.","At 2 you have Cunning Sweep into Lacerate but cooldowns are long and energy is tight — set up the wave, don't commit a fight you can't repeat.","Your full short combo is online — dash-weave Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam with the Lacerate slow onto a still-melee Kayle, before Divine Ascent's range ramps up.","Levels 4-5 are your longest-cooldown window while Radiant Blast pokes from 900 and strips your resists — hold trades until your stack is up.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses and stuns — bait Divine Judgment's 160 seconds in a trade, then crash her when it drops.","Eclipse plus your Level 9 Q max means Cunning Sweep, empowered auto, Sundering Slam chunks half her HP while she is still melee — and Grievous Wounds starves Celestial Blessing.","At two items her ranged form kites your physical-only damage and Radiant Blast strips your resists — farm safe and play for picks while Divine Judgment is on cooldown."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"kennen","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Ambessa","Skill","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Once Lacerate (E) is online you can dash through its slow and chain a stack-empowered auto — but only if Kennen steps into melee to last-hit, since Thundering Shuriken reaches 950 against your 650 cone."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 units to Kennen and suppresses him, so Lightning Rush's move speed can't dodge it — your one clean window to flip the lane, ideally before Slicing Maelstrom is up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus your level-9 Q max lets Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam (doubled on the first target) chunk half his squishy bar — if you pin him to a wall while under three Marks of the Storm."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Kennen has Zhonya's and Liandry's, Slicing Maelstrom's repeated strikes stack Marks on you the instant you blink in, the third one stuns, and Zhonya's stasis then eats your whole follow-up."}],"wants":{"you":["Count his Marks of the Storm: at two stacks back off, and at zero dash Lacerate's slow onto him and land a stack-empowered auto","Hold Public Execution for the instant he uses Lightning Rush or steps to reposition — a 1250-unit blink and suppress ignore his move speed","Buy Mercury's Treads and magic resist — Electrical Surge is on-hit magic damage, so armour reads the trade wrong"],"foe":["Poke with 950-range Thundering Shuriken and marked autos, from outside your empowered-auto reach","Stack you to three Marks of the Storm for the stun, then hold you there under Slicing Maelstrom","Use Lightning Rush to pass straight through your minions and reset spacing out of the Lacerate slow"]},"early":"Kennen owns the opening levels — Thundering Shuriken reaches 950 and Electrical Surge marks you off his autos, while you're an energy-gated melee with only Cunning Sweep until Lacerate at 3. Don't walk into a shuriken just to throw your own cone; last-hit at the back of the wave and eat the chip. Learn to count marks: Mark of the Storm stuns you on the third ability hit, so at two stacks the next thing that touches you locks you down. His melee step-up for a minion is the opening — dash Lacerate's slow on and land one stack-empowered auto.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — your cooldowns are longest while Thundering Shuriken comes back every 5 seconds and you can't reach him. Then 6 flips it: Public Execution blinks 1250 units to Kennen and suppresses, so Lightning Rush's move speed can't dodge it, and it's your single best window to turn a fight. Follow with Repudiation — bait a hit into the brace and the blocked damage amplifies the slam. The trap is his own 6: Slicing Maelstrom is a flat 120 seconds, shorter than your R, and each strike adds a Mark, so blink in with a clean mark count.","late":"This swings back to Kennen as the game opens up. A full-AP Kennen with Zhonya's and Liandry's no longer fears your gap-close — Slicing Maelstrom's repeated strikes stack Marks the moment you blink in, the third one stuns, and Zhonya's stasis eats your follow-up. His 120-second ultimate also comes back faster than your 130, every single cycle. Your job was to close the lane on your level-6 and first-item windows and turn that into side-lane pressure, not to chase a 1v1 you no longer win.","whys":["Thundering Shuriken reaches 950 and his marked autos chip you, while you hold one energy-gated cone and no dash combo until 3.","Lacerate gives you a slow, but your cooldowns are long and Lightning Rush's move speed resets his spacing for free every time.","Your ability-into-empowered-auto chain is online and a melee step-up punishes it, but a 950-range shuriken keeps the trade even at best.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window — longest cooldowns — while Thundering Shuriken drops toward a 4-second cooldown.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units and suppresses him, so Lightning Rush's move speed cannot dodge it — one ult cycle where his kite simply fails.","Eclipse and your Q max let a wall-pinned Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam chunk him, but three Marks of the Storm stun you first.","Full-AP Kennen stacks Marks through Slicing Maelstrom for the stun, and Zhonya's stasis then eats the burst you had loaded."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"kled","win":["Kled","Kled","Skill","Kled","Ambessa","Skill","Kled"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Mounted Kled's Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) reaches 800 and yanks you in only if the shackle holds — concede the level 1-2 trade, last-hit at range, and dash out before the pull resolves."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution (R) blinks 1250 units to Kled, suppresses him and slams him down — your one clean flip window, best used while Skaarl is dismounted and Bear Trap on a Rope is still on cooldown."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus your Level 9 Q max lets you chain Drakehound's Step into Q1-empowered-auto-Q2 and chunk a dismounted Kled before he earns his courage back."},{"when":"Late","text":"Kled scales harder — Chaaaaaaaarge!!! crosses 3500 to 4500 units with a shield attached, and HP stacking plus remount sustain reclaim the duel outright."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the level 1-5 dismounted bully and last-hit at Cunning Sweep (Q) range until your R spike at 6","Catch Kled while Skaarl is dismounted or Bear Trap on a Rope is on cooldown, then chain Drakehound's Step into an empowered auto","All-in at Level 6 with the Public Execution suppress, and again on your first-item Q spike before he remounts"],"foe":["Land Bear Trap on a Rope and hold the shackle long enough to yank you into his Violent Tendencies burst","Drag you into extended trades, because fighting you is what refills Skaarl's courage","Stack HP and use Chaaaaaaaarge!!!'s shield and range to reclaim the duel"]},"early":"Kled owns the opening. He's a level 1-3 skirmish bully and you're at your weakest — one ability, no combo, energy-gated, with very long early cooldowns. Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) reaches 800 and only yanks you in if the shackle holds for a moment, so a Drakehound's Step out of range cancels the pull. Otherwise last-hit with the outer edge of Cunning Sweep from max range and accept the chip. Violent Tendencies (W) is his tell: four fast attacks, and the fourth hits hardest.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — your cooldowns are longest here and he restores Skaarl's courage by fighting you, so every long trade is paying for his remount. Level 6 is your flip: Public Execution (R) blinks 1250 units, suppresses and crashes him down. Use it the moment Bear Trap on a Rope is down and while he's dismounted, where he deals reduced damage to champions — that's your cleanest kill of the lane. Land Lacerate (E) to glue him so Jousting can't recast back out, and brace Repudiation into the fourth Violent Tendencies hit.","late":"This lane drifts back to Kled. He's a hard scaler — HP stacking, remount sustain, and a Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) that crosses 3500 to 4500 units and hands him a shield on the way in, so it re-opens every fight and eats the front of your burst. Once he's got an armour component your Q-auto-Q chunks stop landing clean. Win it on your Level 6 and first-item windows or not at all; if it goes long, use Public Execution as a pick tool rather than soloing him.","whys":["Kled is a true level-1 skirmish bully while you have one ability and no combo — concede the opening and last-hit at Cunning Sweep (Q) range.","Bear Trap on a Rope reaches 800 and Violent Tendencies' four fast attacks beat your level-2 Q+E outright.","By level 3 your dash-weave answers short trades, but Jousting dashes in and recasts straight back out — genuinely even.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window, longest cooldowns, and fighting you is exactly how he refills Skaarl's courage.","Public Execution (R) blinks 1250 units, suppresses and slams him down — your one clean window, and best spent while he is dismounted.","Your Eclipse/Profane plus Q max chains Q1-auto-Q2 to chunk a dismounted Kled, but the courage he earns fighting you remounts him — coinflip.","He out-scales you hard: HP stacking, remount, and a Chaaaaaaaarge!!! that shields him as it engages, against your physical-only damage."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"ksante","win":["Skill","Skill","Ambessa","K'Sante","Ambessa","Ambessa","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q-cone into a Drakehound-dash empowered auto out-trades him before Path Maker's charge is back — his only other out is a Footwork dash."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses and stuns — and the answer he has, All Out, costs him his own resists, so it is a trade you want."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus level-9 Q max drops Q to 10s: Q1-auto-Q2 chunks half his bar before his tank items and Footwork shields stack up."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Two tank items in, Path Maker's charge reduction soaks your burst and All Out heals him while shedding resists to turn duelist — keep anti-heal on him."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q's cone to unlock Sundering Slam, then weave the empowered auto with a Drakehound dash while Path Maker is on cooldown","Force out Footwork's shield-dash first, then commit Lacerate's slow into the level-6 Public Execution suppress","Force the all-in at your first-item Eclipse, and buy Grievous Wounds, because All Out heals him through your burst"],"foe":["Charge Path Maker for the damage reduction, then dash out so every trade of yours stays short","Land two Ntofo Strikes for the shockwave pull, then hold you there while your cooldowns run","Stall to 2+ tank items so Path Maker's charge reduction and a healing All Out outlast your physical-only burst"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is even — you have one ability up, long cooldowns, and Dauntless Instinct marks you for bonus damage on his next attack. Last-hit at the tip of your Q cone and don't throw Lacerate to chase. Path Maker (W) is a charged dash: while charging he takes reduced damage, then he dashes out knocking back and stunning — so committing your empowered auto or Sundering Slam into the charge just feeds the reduction. Bait it, and force out Footwork (E) too: a 10-second dash that shields him is what really eats your burst. At Level 3 your full short combo comes online and the dash-weave starts winning.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his cleanest window — your cooldowns are longest while Ntofo Strikes (Q) returns every 3.5 seconds, so farm and don't force here. Level 6 flips it: Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses and stuns, and All Out answers only by costing him his own defences. Punish once Path Maker's charge is spent and Footwork's shield is down. Learn his real CC too: two Ntofo Strikes stacks fire a shockwave that PULLS you in, so it drags you into his marked follow-up rather than knocking you off it.","late":"Your first-item Eclipse spike with Q maxed is your peak — Q1-auto-Q2 halves him while you stay full, and you win the straight duel here. But K'Sante is a hard scaler: two tank items plus Path Maker's charge reduction soak your combo, and All Out sheds his own resists to turn duelist while healing him, so keep Grievous Wounds on him. Its opening knockback launches you through any wall in the way — that is how the isolation happens. Win before two items land, then let his scaling be someone else's problem.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s, but Dauntless Instinct marks you for bonus damage on his next attack — last-hit at Q-cone range and wait.","At 2 your Q-cone plus Lacerate gives a slow-into-trade, but Path Maker dashes him out and Footwork shields every 10s — stay even, don't extend.","Your short combo is online: Q-cone into a dash-weaved empowered auto out-trades him, since his only outs are Path Maker and a Footwork dash.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window with longest cooldowns, while Ntofo Strikes returns every 3.5s and pulls you in at two stacks.","Public Execution blinks 1250 units to suppress and stun him, and All Out costs him his own defences to use — punish once Path Maker's charge is spent.","Eclipse and level-9 Q max let Q1-auto-Q2 chunk half his bar — force every all-in while Path Maker and Footwork are both down.","He out-scales hard: two tank items, Path Maker's charge reduction, and an All Out that heals him while it sheds resists to turn duelist."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"lillia","win":["Lillia","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Lillia","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-cone-into-Sundering-Slam plus a Lacerate slow is your first real pin window — Lillia has no dash at any level, so once E lands she can only walk out of your empowered auto."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you to the farthest champion in your line and suppress-stuns through her kite — in a 1v1 that is her, and she owns no dash to answer a 1250-range gap-close."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus Q max: a landed Lacerate slow into Q-cone, empowered auto, Sundering Slam chunks half her health before her passive burn and W shield-slam heal the trade back."},{"when":"Late","text":"Her window — full-AP Lillia kites on Blooming Blows' speed stacks, ticks Dream-Laden Bough max-health burn, and opens with Lilting Lullaby from 1600, while one Zhonya's blunts your all-physical damage."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Lacerate's slow first — with no dash in her kit, a slowed Lillia cannot leave your Q cone or your empowered auto","Use level 6: blink-suppress her with Public Execution once Swirlseed's flat 12s is spent, for an all-in she cannot kite","Force the fight through first item where Q-cone-auto-Sundering-Slam outpaces the Dream-Laden Bough burn ticking on you"],"foe":["Kite your ability-into-auto chains on Blooming Blows' stacking move speed, never standing in your Q cone","Tick Dream-Laden Bough max-health burn and clip you with Blooming Blows' true-damage edge, which MR cannot blunt","Reach 2+ items, Lilting Lullaby at 1600 range, and an early Zhonya's so she skirmishes past your all-physical damage"]},"early":"Lillia is a weak early laner and you can press it, but only by making her stand still. Your opener is landing the Q cone and its Sundering Slam follow-up behind a Lacerate slow: she owns no dash at any level, so a slowed Lillia can only walk while your empowered auto and Q2 land. Do not throw Q at empty air chasing her movement; commit E first to glue her, because the slow is what turns your short combo from a whiff into a kill threat. Never wait out Blooming Blows — it is back in 6s at rank 1. Swirlseed is the cooldown that matters, a flat 12s at every rank.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your soft spot: Lacerate is 13s and Repudiation 18s at rank 1, she kites the gaps on Blooming Blows' stacking move speed, and Dream-Laden Bough burns max health while you wait — concede a little and farm toward 6. Then 6 flips it back. Public Execution blinks you to the farthest champion in your line (her, in a 1v1) and suppress-stuns straight through the speed stacks, the one clean answer to a champion who never stands still. Hold it until Swirlseed's flat 12s is spent, then R into Lacerate into Q for the kill. Through first item with Q maxed you out-trade her short combos hard.","late":"This is hers if she survives lane. Full-AP Lillia kites you forever on Blooming Blows' stacking move speed, burns max health with Dream-Laden Bough, and opens from 1600 range with Lilting Lullaby. That sleep only touches enemies already carrying Dream Dust, so the moment any skill of hers clips you, you become the target — walk out during the drowsy, before it lands. Your damage is entirely physical, so an early Zhonya's or armor blunts the combo. Snowball through 6 and first item and end it; never chase a low Lillia into fog.","whys":["Blooming Blows costs her nothing to spam at 6s and its edge is true damage MR cannot blunt, while you have one ability — deny last-hits and set up your 2-3 pin.","Lacerate's slow into Q-cone and Sundering Slam pins her, and Lillia has no dash in her kit at any level — lead with E, never with Q, and her weak early is yours.","Full kit at 3: E-slow into Q-cone, empowered auto, Sundering Slam is more burst than a 500-range Watch Out! Eep! slam can trade back, so take the short fight.","Lacerate at 13s and Repudiation at 18s are your longest waits, but Swirlseed's flat 12s is hers — step up the moment the seed rolls past and she has no answer.","Lilting Lullaby needs Dream Dust already on you, and one Blooming Blows tick is enough — from 1600 range her 6 turns any jungler walking top into a free kill.","Eclipse plus Q max: Q-cone, empowered auto, Sundering Slam chunks her before Dream-Laden Bough's burn is worth anything, and Public Execution closes the last 1250.","Two items on, your combo still kills her before she can kite it — but every Zhonya's or armour piece she buys reads your all-physical damage right."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"lucian","win":["Lucian","Lucian","Lucian","Skill","Lucian","Skill","Lucian"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Lucian's Lightslinger double-tap plus Piercing Light Q chunks you while you hold only Cunning Sweep and no second ability to chain into an empowered auto — his hardest early window."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With Lacerate's slow plus Q-into-Sundering-Slam you can finally pin him for one Drakehound's Step empowered auto — but Relentless Pursuit's cooldown shrinks with every Lightslinger shot."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses him — Relentless Pursuit cannot answer a suppress. It is your one guaranteed all-in before items, and at 130s you get a single attempt."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Lucian's first crit spike (Galeforce/IE) plus Doran's-stacked range out-DPSes your Eclipse all-in once he keeps you at distance and dashes free of your E."}],"wants":{"you":["Deny him Lightslinger shots so Relentless Pursuit stays near its full 16s, then blink Public Execution in and suppress him before the dash is back","Land Cunning Sweep's blades to unlock Sundering Slam, then Lacerate-slow him into a Drakehound's Step empowered auto","Use Repudiation's brace to shield his Lightslinger double-tap, then cash the amped follow-up into your slam"],"foe":["Kite on the move speed Ardent Blaze marks give him, and shave Relentless Pursuit with every Lightslinger shot","Poke you out with Piercing Light Q through the minion line so you can't all-in at full health","Hold Relentless Pursuit for your Lacerate step-in and walk away from your 13s and 18s early cooldowns"]},"early":"Lucian owns these levels and you have to respect it. His Lightslinger double-tap plus Piercing Light Q shreds you while you sit on Cunning Sweep alone — no second ability to chain into an empowered auto, and your energy gate means you can't threaten much back. Don't walk up for a Q you can't follow; last-hit at the edge of your cone and eat the chip. The trap is forcing a level-2 trade: he just Relentless Pursuit dashes out of your E slow and keeps shooting. Wait for level 3 — his dash is 16s at rank 1, but every Lightslinger shot shaves it, so denying autos is what makes it stay down.","mid":"Level 6 is your moment and basically your only clean kill window in lane. Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses on arrival — a suppressed Lucian cannot dash, cannot shoot and cannot start The Culling. Bait the dash first (CS pressure or a fake Q step-up), then R, suppress, slam, and chain Q-Sundering-Slam plus E-spin while he is still locked. Levels 4-5 before that are your worst window — Lacerate 13s, Repudiation 18s, his poke unanswered — so farm and hold R for the one all-in you get.","late":"This drifts back to him as the lane settles into items. Once Lucian completes his first crit item and stacks range with Doran's, he out-DPSes your Eclipse all-in if he keeps the fight at distance — and Ardent Blaze's mark hands him move speed for attacking you, so he usually can. Your R is on cooldown most of the time, and a single R kited out leaves you naked with physical-only damage. Your realistic win is to convert that level 6 kill into a lead and end before his item curve overtakes you; if it goes even, look to roam and group rather than re-dueling a fed Lucian who just walks backward and shoots.","whys":["His Lightslinger double-tap and Piercing Light Q chunk you while you hold only Cunning Sweep with no second ability to chain an empowered auto — you can't trade back.","A level-2 trade fails: Relentless Pursuit slips your Lacerate slow, and Piercing Light pokes you through the minion line at 500 range.","At 3 Lacerate's slow into Q and Sundering Slam finally pins him, but Relentless Pursuit's 16s shrinks with every Lightslinger shot, so it is rarely down.","Levels 4-5 are your longest waits — Lacerate 13s, Repudiation 18s — while Piercing Light's 9s chips you free toward 6.","Public Execution is your one kill window and it is 130s, but The Culling is only 110s — a single dodged blink hands him the next two minutes of lane.","Skill window — Eclipse lands as his first crit item does, and Repudiation's brace into his double-tap decides who opens.","He reclaims it: Ardent Blaze marks give him move speed for attacking you, so he kites while your 130s R sits down and physical damage stalls."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"malphite","win":["Skill","Malphite","Malphite","Skill","Skill","Malphite","Malphite"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Seismic Shard chips you on a flat 8s and steals your move speed for 3s, while you hold only Cunning Sweep and an energy bar to fuel — concede the level-1 and last-hit at range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses him and slams him down — your one clean burst window, but only once Unstoppable Force has gone; both ults are 130s at rank 1."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse's two-hit lets Q1-into-Sundering-Slam actually bite, but armour is his damage too — Ground Slam scales off it — so his second armour item pays him twice over."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two-item Malphite flips you with Unstoppable Force into a Seismic Shard speed steal, and stacked armour blanks your all-physical kit — no clean 1v1 here for you."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Unstoppable Force — 130s at rank 1 — then dash-weave Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam and a Drakehound's Step empowered auto","Hit Level 6 even and use Public Execution's 1250-range blink and suppress for your one real burst window","Buy armour penetration early and snowball the lead before his armour stacking outscales your physical-only damage"],"foe":["Stack armour so her physical-only kit chips, and let Ground Slam turn that armour into damage","Steal her speed with Seismic Shard, cut her attack speed with Ground Slam, and farm up","Hold Unstoppable Force's 130s to knock her out of a Drakehound's Step chain and flip the fight when her combo is spent"]},"early":"Malphite owns these levels and you have to accept it. Seismic Shard chips you on a flat 8s and steals your move speed, and Thunderclap's aftershocks cleave into your face while you still have just Cunning Sweep and an energy bar gating your follow-up. Do not prove anything level 1 — last-hit at max range and stay out of his auto rhythm. Granite Shield absorbs 10% of his max health and recharges every few seconds he goes unhit, so chip it off before you commit anything. He has no kill pressure: farm to 6.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your worst window — Lacerate is 13s and Repudiation 18s while his Ground Slam is a flat 7s, so your dash-weave trades land like noodles off a wall. Then 6 flips it: Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses him and slams him down, and a suppressed Malphite cannot answer. That is your kill — but only if Unstoppable Force is down. Both ults are 130s at rank 1; never all-in into a Malphite who still has his.","late":"This is where you lose the matchup and you need to know it. He stacks armour — Frozen Heart, Randuin's — and Ground Slam turns every point of it into magic damage while cutting your attack speed, so his defence and his offence are the same purchase. A two-item Malphite is a brick wall who flips you with Unstoppable Force into a Seismic Shard speed steal before you can reset. Get your lead at 6 and first item, then stop forcing the 1v1: he is the engage tank your team answers with AP.","whys":["Even start: he has only Seismic Shard level 1 and you have Cunning Sweep and an energy gate — last-hit safe, chip Granite Shield when it is free, and the lane stays neutral.","He out-trades you with a Seismic Shard speed steal into Thunderclap's aftershocks while your long cooldowns can't punish back.","Ground Slam is a flat 7s that scales off his armour and cuts your attack speed, so your dash-weave trades barely dent him and he farms up.","Your weakest window — Lacerate 13s and Repudiation 18s against his flat 7s Ground Slam; concede and farm toward 6.","Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses him on arrival and slams him down — your one clean kill, and only if Unstoppable Force is already spent.","Eclipse's two-hit finally lets Q1-into-Sundering-Slam chunk him, but it's a wash: he buys his second armour item right back, and that is a Ground Slam damage item too.","Stacked armour blanks your physical-only kit while feeding Ground Slam, and Unstoppable Force into a speed steal flips you — no 1v1 here."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"maokai","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Sap Magic heals him on attack, and every spell you land on him shortens that cooldown — chipping a Cunning Sweep cone in pays for his sustain while your Q and E sit long."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses on arrival — but it cannot pick him while Twisted Advance has him untargetable, so fire it after the root lands."},{"when":"Maokai W","text":"Twisted Advance is the trade-ender: he goes untargetable, dashes onto you and roots — 14s at rank 1, and nothing you cast touches him in transit. Never commit a chain with his W up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Even on your Eclipse/Profane Hydra spike, armour plus Sap Magic mean your physical-only burst chunks then heals off — buy Grievous Wounds or you cannot delete a tank like a squishy."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 6 and Public Execution him off his sapling line — suppress him the moment Twisted Advance is spent","Bait Twisted Advance's 14s, then Q-into-empowered-auto weave with Drakehound's Step once the root has whiffed","Buy Grievous Wounds early and win the short burst window before Sap Magic refills what your combo took off"],"foe":["Go untargetable through Twisted Advance, then root your dash chain dead","Toss saplings and let every spell you land on him shorten Sap Magic's heal timer","Stack Bramble Vest and armor early so your AD-only burst falls off a full-HP tank"]},"early":"Maokai is the rare melee you do NOT free-trade into early: Sap Magic heals him on attack and every spell you land on him shortens that heal's cooldown, so chipping a Cunning Sweep cone in actually pays for his sustain. Don't walk up into Bramble Smash's 600 range — its knockback shoves you off your Sundering Slam follow-up, and Twisted Advance goes untargetable, dashes onto you and roots the instant you commit. Farm with the blades of your cone, respect saplings in the bush, and accept that you concede this opening.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — Twisted Advance is 14s at rank 1 against your 13s Lacerate and 18s Repudiation, and he sustains through the chip. Level 6 is your one real flip: Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses and stuns, and a suppressed Maokai cannot cast anything. But it cannot pick him at all while Twisted Advance has him untargetable — bait the root out, then fire R after the dash, never into it. Save it for him stepping up to last-hit or for catching him off a sapling line.","late":"This is where the tank wins. Your kit is entirely physical, so once Maokai is into armour your slam and empowered autos bounce off — and every spell you land shortens Sap Magic's heal, so the burst funds his sustain. Nature's Grasp rolls a rooting wall up the lane from 3000 range while Twisted Advance locks your carries. Convert your Level 6 window into a CS or plate lead, then sidelane and let your team play front-to-back; you do not out-scale a Maokai into items.","whys":["Sap Magic heals him on attack and every spell you land shortens that cooldown, so your cone-Q chip pays for his sustain — even-to-ahead at 1.","Your Drakehound's Step weave is online and he has no armour yet — but hold it until Twisted Advance's 14s is spent, or the root ends the trade.","Full pattern at 3 and he is still soft — trade after Bramble Smash, only 7s at rank 1, and leave before the root.","Twisted Advance at 14s beats your Lacerate 13s and Repudiation 18s cycle, and he out-sustains the chip — your weakest window.","Public Execution suppresses him on arrival, but it cannot target him mid-Twisted-Advance — fire it after the root, never into the dash.","Eclipse and Profane Hydra land, but armour and Sap Magic blunt AD-only burst — Grievous Wounds is what makes the spike real.","He's a sustain tank into your physical-only kit and the better teamfight lockdown — he reclaims the matchup hard."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"mel","win":["Mel","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Mel","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Radiant Volley chips you from 950 on a 10s cooldown while you have only Cunning Sweep — last-hit at range, eat the poke, don't force a trade you can't finish."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses her and slams her down — the immobile mage has no dash, and a suppressed Mel cannot cast Rebuttal."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus Q max: Cunning Sweep into empowered-auto into Sundering Slam chunks half her bar in the window after Rebuttal's 38s has been spent."},{"when":"Her W window","text":"Rebuttal (W) is 38s at rank 1 and prevents damage outright — nothing you cast is a projectile for it to reflect, so bait it, then commit once it drops."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach 6 and R her — the suppress plus Sundering Slam burst is a guaranteed all-in, and a suppressed Mel cannot cast Rebuttal","Use the Drakehound's Step dash mid-cast to close distance so her Q poke never trades for free","Snowball the Eclipse Q-max Cunning-Sweep-into-Slam pattern in every window Rebuttal is down"],"foe":["Land Radiant Volley from 950 and bank Overwhelm on you before 6","Hold Rebuttal for your commit — it prevents damage outright and speeds her out of it","Root you at Solar Snare's centre from 1000 so you never get a walk-up window"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are hers to poke. You've got only Cunning Sweep at 650, no Sundering Slam follow-up yet, and you're energy-gated — so don't walk into Radiant Volley's 950 trying to force. Just last-hit and accept the chip. The good news: her poke can't kill you and she has zero mobility. Once you hit 3 and your Cunning-Sweep-into-Sundering-Slam combo comes online, you win any short dash-weave trade because she can't disengage. Bait Solar Snare before you commit — if the root whiffs you have a free dash window in.","mid":"This is your takeover. At 6, Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses her and slams her down — an immobile artillery mage has no escape from that, and a suppressed Mel cannot cast anything, Rebuttal included. The one correction: the barrier is her W, not her R. Rebuttal prevents damage outright on a 38s cooldown at rank 1, so bait it, then E to slow her, weave the empowered auto, and run Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam through her bar. With Eclipse and Q max your combo chunks half her HP while you stay near full.","late":"You own the straight 1v1 through your item spikes, but Mel is a scaling poke mage — full-build she pokes you down from 950 before you reach her, and Rebuttal blanks your commit for its whole duration. Golden Eclipse then strikes every Overwhelm stack she has banked on you from anywhere on the map, so chip you shrugged off in lane is damage she saves for the teamfight. Close the lane on your power curve, snowball off your 6 and first-item windows, and never let a fed Mel turn the game into a poke war her range wins.","whys":["Radiant Volley out-ranges you at 950 on a 10s cooldown while you hold Cunning Sweep at 650 — concede the opening and just farm.","Your level-2 Cunning-Sweep-into-Slam is a real trade, but Solar Snare roots from 1000 on 11s and her Q answers — even, don't overextend.","Your Cunning-Sweep-into-Sundering-Slam combo is online and she has no dash — once Rebuttal's 38s is spent, dash-weave trades beat her outright.","Through 4-5 you control the wave around Solar Snare's 11s; she pokes, but cannot stop you walking up once the root is spent.","Golden Eclipse strikes every Overwhelm stack she has banked on you from anywhere on the map — your 6 answers one lane, hers answers all three.","Eclipse plus Q max: Cunning Sweep into empowered-auto into Sundering Slam halves her bar in any window Rebuttal is down — your peak.","Full-build she pokes from 950 and Golden Eclipse detonates the Overwhelm on you — a fed Mel reclaims it, so close before two items."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"mordekaiser","win":["Mordekaiser","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Mordekaiser","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Neither of you has a full combo yet — contest the first wave with the blades of your Q cone, hug your minions so Obliterate never catches you isolated, and deny Darkness Rise its third connection."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"His E-pull into isolated Q is the trade he fishes for. Death's Grasp is 16s at rank 1 — stay out of its 700 range while Drakehound's Step is down, dash out of the slam if he steps up, and re-commit only once the pull is spent."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Realm of Death (R) is the scariest button in the lane — it drags you into an isolated 1v1 and steals your stats, and most of your damage is physical. It is 140s at rank 1 against your 130s, so you get the spare window; never open into an up ult, and save your blink-suppress as the answer, not the opener."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus Grievous Wounds is your reclaim window — chain Q-cone into empowered auto into Sundering Slam, then dash off with Drakehound Step before he consumes the Indestructible shield your own damage just finished building for him."}],"wants":{"you":["Keep every trade SHORT — dash in with Drakehound's Step, chain ability-into-empowered-auto, and leave before he consumes the shield your damage helped build","Pre-empt Death's Grasp so he never lands the isolated Obliterate while you sit inside its 700 range","Buy Grievous Wounds early so Indestructible cannot be cashed for a full heal, and hold a Quicksilver/QSS so Realm of Death can't lock you into a stat-stealing 1v1"],"foe":["Land E to pull you in, then isolated Q for the bonus slam while his W shield soaks your empowered autos","Drag the fight long — Indestructible stores the damage he deals AND takes, so your burst builds his shield","Hit R at 6 to steal your stats and duel you in his realm where your physical-heavy kit is gutted"]},"early":"Level 1 is genuinely even — neither of you has a combo online, so contest the first wave with the blades of your Q cone and last-hit tight to your own minions so Obliterate never catches you isolated where its damage goes up. Deny Darkness Rise its third connection and the aura never switches on. From 2-3, Death's Grasp into isolated Q is the exact trade he fishes for, so don't sit inside 700 range with Drakehound's Step down. If he steps up to pull, dash out of the slam — then re-engage once that 16s is running and punish him for it.","mid":"This is his stretch, not yours. Your cooldowns are longest at 4-5 and his whole kit wants the long fight — Indestructible is 12s at rank 1 and stores the damage he deals AND takes, so the harder you commit the bigger the shield he then consumes to heal himself back up. At 6, Realm of Death yanks you into an isolated 1v1 and steals your stats, and since most of your kit is physical that duel guts your damage. Never all-in him near full HP with his R up — play short Q-into-empowered-auto pokes, farm the wave, and respect that he flips any extended trade. Hold your own R as a disengage or a clean execute setup, not as a brawl-opener into his ult.","late":"By 2+ items it swings back to Ambessa's favor — Eclipse with your Q-max lets you chain Q-cone into empowered auto into Sundering Slam and dash off inside a single Indestructible cycle, and Grievous Wounds is what stops him cashing that shield back into health. Build a Quicksilver/QSS so his realm can't isolate you, and be honest: he never stops winning the LONG fight, so this lane is decided by whether you keep every trade short and clean. Group on the map where his single-target R is far less oppressive, never let him drag you off alone into a side lane, and use your R's blink-suppress to pick HIM off rather than dueling into his.","whys":["Neither of you has a combo at 1 — hug your minions so Obliterate never gets its isolated bonus, and deny Darkness Rise the third hit that switches its aura on.","Death's Grasp into isolated Obliterate is online at 16s while your dash and cooldowns are still long — he lands the bonus slam first, so stay out of its 700 range.","Full pattern at 3 is yours: Lacerate's slow into Q-cone and Sundering Slam lands and leaves before he can consume Indestructible for the heal.","Levels 4-5 stay yours if trades stay short — Indestructible is 12s at rank 1 and only stores what he deals and takes, so leave before he cashes it.","Realm of Death drags you into a stat-stealing 1v1 and your kit is mostly physical — never fight near full HP with it up.","Eclipse and Q max chunk him inside one Indestructible cycle — Grievous Wounds on the consume is what keeps the first-item window yours.","Your Eclipse and Q-max reclaim the short trade — chain Q into empowered auto into Sundering Slam, then dash off before he consumes the shield your damage built and heals it all back."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"nasus","win":["Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q cone blades into the Drakehound's Step empowered auto, then Lacerate's slow so he can't walk off the trade — punish every wind-up, and remember Siphoning Strike only stacks if he lands the kill."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"R blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses on arrival, so he cannot cast Wither at all — your cleanest all-in while his stacks are still low."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse online with Q maxed: Q-into-empowered-auto-into-Sundering-Slam chunks half his bar — bring Grievous Wounds, because Soul Eater's life steal refunds anything long."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once his Q stacks pile up, one Wither guts your attack speed for 15s at rank 1 — that is the empowered-auto engine — while Soul Eater's life steal out-sustains your burst. The lane is his on the timer."}],"wants":{"you":["Deny his Q stacks — step on the caster minions he wants to last-hit and force a trade every time he winds up the empowered Q","Land Q with the blades into the empowered auto, then Lacerate so the slow pins him for the Sundering-Slam follow-up","Save R until level 6 and all-in while his stacks are low — a suppressed Nasus cannot cast Wither at all"],"foe":["Land Wither from 700 to gut your move and attack speed, killing the empowered-auto chain that is all your damage","Free-farm Q stacks safely under tower and walk off your trades behind his own slows","Drag the lane long: Soul Eater life steal and a fat Siphoning Strike flip any duel once Wither lands"]},"early":"Nasus is helpless at level 1 — no Wither, no stacks — so set the lane up now: deny his Q last-hits by stepping on the caster minions he needs, because Siphoning Strike only stacks if he lands the kill. At 2 your Q cone into the Drakehound's Step empowered auto already out-trades a Nasus who can only auto back at 255 range, and at 3 Lacerate's slow pins him so he can't reset. The one rule: from level 2 onward respect Wither's 15s — it guts the attack speed your whole chain runs on, so trade before he lands it, not after.","mid":"This is your window — every level he spends not stacking Q is a level you keep him behind. At 6 your R is the kill button: it blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses on arrival, and a suppressed Nasus cannot cast Wither. With Eclipse and Q maxed your Q-into-empowered-auto-into-Sundering-Slam halves him, and Grievous Wounds on Soul Eater's life steal keeps the chunk on his bar. Bait the Wither — if he burns it on one trade, all-in the 15s; if he holds it, make him choose between stacking and saving it.","late":"If you let this go long it inverts hard. A fed Nasus with a fully stacked Q only needs one Wither — it guts your attack speed, and since your damage is empowered autos and dash-weaving, that alone turns most of your kit off. Soul Eater's life steal out-heals your burst, Fury of the Sands hands him bonus armour and a shorter Siphoning Strike, and standing in Spirit Fire strips YOUR armour to feed it. Win on the timer: snowball into plates, towers and roams, and never duel a full-build Nasus alone in a side lane.","whys":["Nasus has no Wither and zero stacks at 1 — but you also have just one ability and no combo yet, so it's a coinflip last-hit duel.","Your Q cone plus the Drakehound's Step empowered auto out-damages a Wither-less Nasus who can only auto back.","Lacerate's slow pins him while you weave Q-auto-Sundering-Slam — a 255-range Q cannot follow you out of the trade.","His cooldowns do not threaten you yet, and every last-hit you deny is a Siphoning Strike stack he never gets.","At 6 your R blinks to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses on arrival, so he cannot cast Wither — and a low-stack Nasus has nothing else to answer the all-in with.","Eclipse and Q-max give you Q-into-empowered-auto-into-Sundering-Slam that halves him, and Grievous Wounds blunts Soul Eater — force every all-in before he scales.","A stacked Nasus Withers off your attack speed, Soul Eater heals through your burst, and Spirit Fire strips YOUR armour to feed his Q — the late duel is his."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"nautilus","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once Dredge Line, the Staggering Blow root and Riptide are online he can hook-auto-E and pin you, and Titan's Wrath shields the return on a flat 12s — don't sit in hook range to last-hit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses him — a suppressed Nautilus cannot hook, Riptide or ult — then slams him down. Your one clean all-in, ideally with his Q down."},{"when":"Whenever Q is up","text":"Dredge Line is his only way to close on you and the front of every combo — bait it and 14s at rank 1 says he cannot reach you, though a wall behind him still pulls him along it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Stacked armor plus Plated Steelcaps blunts your physical-only Q-auto-Q burst while his hook-root-E-R chain peels you off — he reclaims the lane as he tanks up."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait or sidestep his Dredge Line, then dash in on its 14s and chain empowered autos before the Staggering Blow root resets","Hold R for level 6 — the suppression means a Nautilus cannot hook you, cannot Riptide and cannot start Depth Charge","Buy early armour penetration and end every trade before Titan's Wrath refreshes on its flat 12s"],"foe":["Land Dredge Line to pull you in, proc the Staggering Blow root on the follow-up auto, then chain Riptide on top","Stack root, E slow and R knockup to strip your Drakehound dashes and hold you still for his jungler","Tank up on armour and Steelcaps and hold Titan's Wrath so your physical combo bounces off the shield"]},"early":"His Dredge Line hook into a Staggering Blow root on the follow-up auto is the whole problem early — every time he lands it he pins you out of your Drakehound dash-weave and chains Riptide on top, and your Q and E cooldowns are far too long at levels 1-3 to trade back through that. Don't sit in hook range to last-hit; farm from distance with the blades of your Cunning Sweep cone. If he whiffs the hook you get 14s at rank 1 — dash in, land Sundering Slam and an empowered auto, and peel off before the root resets.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — your cooldowns are at their longest and his hook-root-slow chain out-trades your dash pattern, so concede the wave and farm toward 6. At 6 the lane flips for one window: Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses him, and a suppressed Nautilus cannot hook, cannot Riptide and cannot start Depth Charge. All-in with his Q on its 14s and Titan's Wrath already spent. Note his R is 120s against your 130s — the window is yours only once.","late":"This is where he takes the lane back. He's a tank stacking armor and Plated Steelcaps, your damage is entirely physical, so the Q-auto-Q combo that halves a squishy just bounces off him — meanwhile his hook, passive root, Riptide slow and Depth Charge knockup form a full peel chain that pins you for his team. Don't try to solo-kill a two-item Nautilus; use Public Execution to blink past him onto his carries. Titan's Wrath is a shield, not a heal, so force it out on its flat 12s rather than buying anti-heal, and end the game before he is a three-item wall.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — he has only Dredge Line up and you have one ability and no combo yet, so neither commits; just deny last-hits and respect hook range.","His Dredge Line hook chains into the Staggering Blow root and Riptide and pins you out of your dash-weave — your long level-2 cooldowns can't trade back through that.","With hook, root and Riptide online his CC chain out-trades your combo, and Titan's Wrath shields the return — fight only if he wastes Q.","Your Q and E cooldowns are longest at 4-5 while Riptide comes back every 7s at rank 1 — concede the wave and farm toward your R.","Public Execution blinks to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses him out of his own CC — he cannot hook, Riptide or ult while it holds. Your one clean all-in.","Your first item helps, but the hook and the passive root still pin you and he is already stacking armour — it hinges on his 14s Q being down.","He stacks armor and Steelcaps against your physical-only damage while his hook-root-E-R chain peels you off — he out-tanks and out-CCs you with items."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"neeko","win":["Neeko","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Neeko","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Blooming Burst pokes from 800 on a 9s cooldown and Tangle-Barbs roots from 1000 through everything it passes — minions don't block it, so last-hit at max range until your full kit is online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses her, then slams her down for a stun — she is squishy enough that the follow-up kills before she owns Zhonya's."},{"when":"Her Lvl 6 / R","text":"Pop Blossom has a short preparation and only a 600 radius, but the prep is hidden while Inherent Glamour has her disguised — so read the disguise, not the clone, before you commit a dash."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"A full-AP Neeko with Zhonya's stopwatches through your R suppress window and bursts you from outside your dash range — your purely physical damage can't race her, so close the lane before her second item lands."}],"wants":{"you":["Land your Q cone to unlock Sundering Slam, then chain a Drakehound's Step dash into your empowered passive auto for a short trade before her E root lands","Hit Level 6 and use Public Execution to suppress her — immobilizing CC also breaks Inherent Glamour and strips any disguise on the spot","Build early MR (Mercs/Hexdrinker) and sidestep her E so your dash chains and empowered-auto trades stay uninterrupted"],"foe":["Land Tangle-Barbs (E) through a minion it kills so it reaches you bigger, faster and rooting you longer mid-dash","Poke you down with Q from range and deny your empowered-auto windows so you never close the gap","Land Pop Blossom (R) — with Inherent Glamour hiding the preparation — to stun your all-in and burst you down"]},"early":"Neeko owns this opening more than most melees you face. Blooming Burst pokes from 800 every 9s and Tangle-Barbs roots from 1000 through everything in its path, so hiding behind the wave does nothing — worse, a minion the tangle kills on the way makes the root that finally reaches you bigger, faster and longer. Last-hit at max range, accept a little Q poke, and never commit a Drakehound's Step dash into an obvious root angle: if she lands it you eat her whole rotation. Bait the E, then take a short Q-cone-into-Sundering-Slam tap on its 12s, and don't extend.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay rough — her root-into-poke combo out-trades your cooldowns, so keep farming toward 6 and don't force. Level 6 is the lane's pivot: Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses her and slams her down, and because the immobilize breaks Inherent Glamour a disguised Neeko is stripped the moment you land. Her own 6 is Pop Blossom: a short preparation inside a 600 radius, hidden only while she is disguised. Read the disguise rather than the clone, bait her R or her Flash, then commit — an R spent into a decoy is a free reset for her.","late":"Once Neeko has Zhonya's plus a second AP item this slips away. The Zhonya's active eats your R burst exactly when you'd kill her, and a fed full-AP Neeko bursts you from outside your dash range — your physical-only damage can't drop her health bar fast enough. Inherent Glamour also makes her a roam-and-pick threat, so the map gets dangerous, not just the lane. Your only real path is to have already snowballed off your Level 6 and first-item windows; if it's even at 2 items, group and don't facecheck alone.","whys":["You have one usable ability while she has 800-range Q poke, a 1000-range root and Shapesplitter's every-third-attack bonus — trade minimally.","Her level 2 Q at 800 and root at 1000 out-range your step-up, and your cooldowns are too long to punish — concede the poke and farm.","Tangle-Barbs roots you mid-dash from 1000 and passes straight through minions, denying the empowered-auto trades you'd win on an immobile target.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window with your longest cooldowns, and her 12s root plus 9s poke out-trade you — farm to 6, don't force.","Public Execution suppresses her, and the immobilize strips Inherent Glamour too — her squishy frame dies to the follow-up before Zhonya's exists.","Your level-6 spike and Q chunk her in a Q-cone-auto-Sundering-Slam, but her Zhonya's and Pop Blossom keep it from being a free win — it's a coin-flip on who lands first.","Full-AP Neeko with Zhonya's blanks your R burst and out-ranges you, and your physical-only damage can't race her — she reclaims the matchup."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"olaf","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Undertow slows you and strips your armour from 1000 range, then Reckless Swing lands true damage no armour reduces — with one ability and no energy your empowered-auto chain has nothing to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R blinks to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses — but Ragnarok makes him immune to disables while he keeps attacking, so bait it out or the suppress simply does not land."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus Q-max: Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam finally out-chunks his lifesteal — but only inside Ragnarok's 100s at rank 1."},{"when":"Ragnarok up","text":"Ragnarok makes him immune to disables for as long as he keeps attacking, and it passively hands him armour and MR against your all-physical kit — never all-in into an active one."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Ragnarok out in a fake trade, then land your R suppress inside its 100s while nothing is making him immune to it","Reach Level 6 and use R's blink and suppress to flip the lockdown his Undertow shred and lifesteal have been winning pre-6","Hit your Eclipse / Q-max spike and force Cunning Sweep into empowered-auto into Sundering Slam burst while his R is down"],"foe":["Pop Ragnarok to go immune to disables while he keeps swinging, then run you down on Undertow","Land Undertow to slow you and shred your armour, then Reckless Swing for true damage, out-sustaining it all on lifesteal","Win every pre-6 extended trade your one-ability, energy-gated early game can't refuse"]},"early":"Olaf owns this opening and you can't trade it straight — you've got one ability, you're energy-gated, and Reckless Swing is true damage no armour reduces. It costs him health to cast, but Berserker Rage gives him attack speed and lifesteal off missing health, so hurting him partly pays him back. Undertow slows you and strips your armour from 1000, and picking the axe up resets its 9s outright, so he can be perma-aggressive. Don't dash-weave in at 1-3; last-hit at the blades of your cone and don't burn E chasing.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — your cooldowns are longest and Undertow into Reckless Swing out-trades your empowered autos before you chain a full combo. The lane flips at 6: your R blinks to the farthest champion in the line, suppresses and stuns, and that lockdown is the one thing his kit genuinely fears. But it hinges on Ragnarok — while it is up he is immune to disables for as long as he keeps attacking, so the suppress never lands. Bait it: fake the commit, make him burn a 100s ultimate, then unload.","late":"Your Eclipse and Q-max spike give you a real favor window — Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam finally out-chunks his lifesteal in a clean trade. But this stays Olaf-leaning: Berserker Rage means a half-health Olaf swings faster and heals harder than a full-health one, Ragnarok's passive alone hands him armour and MR against your all-physical damage, and its 100s answers your 130s. Pick your all-ins strictly around his R timer, look to roam and snowball elsewhere with R's pick potential, and don't try to farm-lane him out.","whys":["Undertow slows and shreds your armour, Reckless Swing lands true damage, and Berserker Rage pays him attack speed and lifesteal for the health he is missing.","His level 2 Undertow into Reckless Swing out-nukes your long early cooldowns, and Tough It Out's shield eats what you send back.","Your short combo comes online but his lifesteal and true-damage E keep it even at best — never force the extended fight while Ragnarok is up.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window with longest cooldowns; his Q-slow autos and lifesteal reclaim the lane before you can chain empowered hits.","Your R suppresses him — but Ragnarok makes him immune to disables while he keeps attacking, so bait it out first.","Eclipse and Q-max make your chain chunk him, but Ragnarok's 100s comes back thirty seconds before your 130s R does — a coinflip, not a free win.","He out-sustains you late: lifesteal that grows as he drops, plus Ragnarok passive armour and MR against physical damage."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"ornn","win":["Skill","Ornn","Ornn","Skill","Skill","Ornn","Ornn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-into-Sundering-Slam plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto out-trades Volcanic Rupture's 9s poke before he can pillar-into-Searing-Charge for the Brittle knockup."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution suppresses him — but Volcanic Rupture's pillar is terrain he makes himself, so Searing Charge still has something to hit."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level-9 Q max: Q1-empowered-auto-Q2 carves half his bar, and bracing Repudiation into his damage pays for a bigger slam on the way out."},{"when":"Late","text":"The elemental's first pass slows and applies Brittle; only the recast charge knocks up — a teamfight setup, not a 1v1. Close the lane early."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait the Volcanic Rupture pillar and the Searing Charge into it, then dash-weave your Q combo while that 14s Brittle setup is down","Land Q1 then Sundering Slam Q2 and weave Drakehound's Step autos to chunk him before a tank item lands","Snowball your level-6 suppress and Eclipse first-item spike before Ornn self-itemizes and out-scales into 5v5s"],"foe":["Land Volcanic Rupture (Q) against terrain or Searing Charge (E) into a wall to knock you up and apply Brittle","Hold Bellows Breath (W) so its final gout lands the Brittle that sets up every knockup he has","Reach late game and chain Brittle into his double-knockup ult to set up teamfights, not the lane 1v1"]},"early":"Ornn is one of the slowest bodies you will lane into and he has no sustain to grind you back. At level 1 you both have one ability, so trade your Q cone over the minions and don't stand where his Volcanic Rupture pillar will form. Once you have Q-into-Sundering-Slam plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto at 2-3 you out-trade his 9s Q flat — dash in, hit with the blades of your cone, then step out before Searing Charge can pop you off terrain. His punish is pillar-into-E for the Brittle knockup; bait that 14s, then commit.","mid":"This is your takeover. Through 4-5 you farm even and dodge his Brittle setup, then 6 cracks it open: Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses him, and a suppressed Ornn cannot cast anything. Do not assume open lane is safe — Volcanic Rupture drops a pillar after a short delay and Searing Charge only needs that, so the cue is the pillar, not the wall. Brace Repudiation into his damage and the slam comes out bigger; it will not stop the Brittle or the knockup, so time the exit.","late":"Your first-item spike is the cleanest window of the lane — Q1-empowered-auto-Q2 with Eclipse carves half his health while Repudiation and your passive's energy refunds let you re-engage. Keep forcing all-ins here. The honest part: Living Forge gives him extra armour and magic resist from every source, so each tank item is worth more than the tooltip against your all-physical damage, and his job late is Brittle into the Call of the Forge God recast knockup for his team. Build your lead before that matters.","whys":["You both have one ability and no combo at level 1 — trade Q cones over the minions and just don't eat his Volcanic Rupture pillar against a wall.","Your Q into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step auto out-trades his 9s Q before the pillar-into-E Brittle combo is online.","Your dash-weave beats a slow tank, but Searing Charge is 14s at rank 1 and Volcanic Rupture builds the pillar he needs to charge into.","Through Bellows Breath's 12s window you farm even and sidestep the E knockup — he has zero sustain to punish the dance.","Public Execution suppresses him and he casts nothing — but his own pillar is terrain Searing Charge escapes on.","Eclipse and the Q max let Q1-auto-Q2 chunk half his bar, and bracing Repudiation into his damage pays for a bigger slam.","Living Forge adds armour and MR from every source, so his tank items outrun your physical damage — and his R sets up his team, not a duel."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"pantheon","win":["Skill","Pantheon","Pantheon","Skill","Skill","Pantheon","Pantheon"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Pantheon's window: Shield Vault dashes 600 to stun you and Comet Spear pokes on 11s while you have one ability, long cooldowns and an energy gate before your empowered-auto chain exists."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution flips it — the blink and suppress land through anything, and a suppressed Pantheon cannot keep channelling Aegis Assault, his one damage-proof button at 22s."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane Hydra with Q maxed is your peak: Cunning Sweep into the empowered auto into Sundering Slam chunks him while his early-game power has already expired."},{"when":"Late","text":"Pantheon is a non-factor late, and Grand Starfall's 180s means a roam costs him three minutes — but your all-physical damage still stalls into an armour-stacker or a hypercarry."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm levels 1-5 with the blades of Cunning Sweep at 650 so Comet Spear at 575 and Shield Vault at 600 never catch you in a trade one ability cannot win","Reach Level 6 and land Public Execution — the suppress ends an Aegis Assault channel and shuts off the Shield Vault escape","Snowball your first-item window (Eclipse/Profane, Q maxed) where his lane lead is gone and your ability-into-empowered-auto burst is online"],"foe":["Open with the Shield Vault dash-stun from 600, then Comet Spear while your cooldowns and energy are still long","Win every short trade levels 1-5 — Aegis Assault blanks frontal damage and Shield Vault resets any combo you start","Convert his early kill pressure or a global R roam into a lead elsewhere before he falls off into your item spike"]},"early":"Pantheon owns these levels and you have to respect it. Shield Vault is a 600-range dash onto you with a stun and an auto reset attached, and Comet Spear pokes for free from 575 on 11s. Aegis Assault then makes him invulnerable to damage from the FRONT — not a passive, a 22s ability he has to commit — so the answer is to be behind him or to be elsewhere. With one ability, an energy gate at 1 and long cooldowns at 2-3, don't force a dash-weave you'll lose. Farm with the blades of Cunning Sweep at 650 and eat the poke.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — his cooldowns are short and yours are at their longest, so keep farming toward your spike instead of trading into the stun. Level 6 is the flip: Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest champion in the line and suppresses on arrival, and a suppressed Pantheon cannot keep channelling Aegis Assault or vault away. Bait Shield Vault first if you can — with the stun down and his 22s E either spent or cut short, the all-in is clean and he has no second way out.","late":"By first item your damage is there: Eclipse/Profane Hydra with Q maxed lets you open Cunning Sweep, weave the empowered auto and follow with Sundering Slam for a huge chunk, and Pantheon contributes almost nothing to a teamfight this late. The real threat isn't him anymore — your damage is entirely physical, so a Vayne, Kayle or armour-stacking tank on the enemy team reclaims the scaling your kit was winning. Close on your item spike while Pantheon is dead weight; don't let the game drift to where stacked armour eats your output.","whys":["You have one ability and an energy gate while Shield Vault dashes 600 to stun and Comet Spear pokes from 575 — last-hit with the blades at 650 and stay out of his range.","Shield Vault's 600-range dash-stun into a Comet Spear chunks you before your empowered-auto chain and cooldowns are ready — concede level 2 and farm.","Your short combo is up, but Aegis Assault blanks damage from the front for 22s at rank 1 and Shield Vault resets the trade — fish for quick pokes only.","Your weakest window with your longest cooldowns and his kit at full strength — farm toward 6 and refuse the extended fight.","Public Execution suppresses on arrival, and a suppressed Pantheon cannot keep channelling Aegis Assault or vault out — bait the stun first and it is a guaranteed all-in.","Eclipse/Profane and a maxed Q give you the Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam burst that halves him once his early power expires.","Pantheon is irrelevant late, but your purely physical damage stalls into an armor-stacker — close before a scaling AD carry like Vayne or Kayle reclaims it."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"poppy","win":["Skill","Poppy","Poppy","Poppy","Skill","Skill","Poppy"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Steadfast Presence comes online at 2 and stops dashes around her every 20s at rank 1 — a stopped Drakehound's Step also leaves you slowed and grounded, so bait it with a throwaway cast."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution is your one clean window — the blink-behind suppress lands her regardless of W, and the passive armor pen + on-hit healing flips this into a kill if you catch her stepping off her wall."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Eclipse spike lands, but Plated Steelcaps and Heart of Steel blunt your all-physical chunk, and Iron Ambassador re-shields her on every buckler pickup."},{"when":"Late","text":"Keeper's Verdict is a 140s channel and Public Execution's suppress cancels it outright — spend your R on her wind-up rather than on the dive she was always going to bounce."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her W (Steadfast Presence) with a feint or a non-dash poke, then commit your real Drakehound's Step dash once it's on cooldown","Hit Level 6 and use Public Execution to blink behind her and suppress — the lockdown lands through W, and the armor pen cuts her early plating","Fight in open ground so Heroic Charge (14s at rank 1) has no wall to pin you against — no wall, no stun"],"foe":["Hold Steadfast Presence for your cast — a stopped dash leaves you slowed and grounded","Land E (Heroic Charge) to pin you into a wall for the long stun, then chunk with Q (Hammer Shock) follow-up","Stack early armor — Plated Steelcaps and Heart of Steel — so your all-physical burst falls off as she scales into a peel tank"]},"early":"Poppy is the worst possible early target for your weave — her W, Steadfast Presence, point-blank cancels your Drakehound's Step dash mid-cast, so the moment you Cunning Sweep in to land an empowered auto she just braces and turns it off, and you get nothing for the energy. At Level 1 you're roughly even since she has no W yet, so contest a short jab then back off; once she hits 2, never throw your dash into a held W. Last-hit at the outer edge of Cunning Sweep for the doubled damage, and respect her E (Heroic Charge) — stand off the wall or she pins you into terrain for a multi-second stun.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your weakest window and hers is strong — your cooldowns are longest here and every dash-weave gets read and cancelled by her W, so concede the trade and farm toward 6. Level 6 is the one moment this lane is yours: Public Execution blinks you behind her and suppresses regardless of her W, and the passive flat armor pen plus on-hit healing carries you through her early plating. Catch her stepping up off the wall, R for the lockdown, then chain Lacerate's slow and your Cunning Sweep-into-Sundering Slam before her W comes back. That's your kill window — outside of it, don't force.","late":"This stays an uphill fight. Your first-item Eclipse spike is real, but Poppy buys Plated Steelcaps and Heart of Steel and your damage is entirely physical, so the stacked armor eats your Cunning Sweep-auto-Sundering Slam burst. In teamfights she is the perfect anti-diver — her W blanks your engage dash, her E (Heroic Charge) walls you off her carry, and her R (Keeper's Verdict) knockback bounces you straight out the instant you blink in. Pick fights where she has to spend W defensively first, then commit your dive on the second window, and lean on your team to bait her cooldowns.","whys":["No W up at Level 1, so your Drakehound's Step dash works and you can land an empowered auto — but you're one short combo on long cooldowns and she trades evenly, so the opener is a coin-flip.","Steadfast Presence stops your dash and leaves you slowed and grounded, so the failed commit hands her a free Hammer Shock zone on an 8s cooldown and a Heroic Charge into the nearest wall.","Your short combo is online but every dash into her gets cancelled by held W, and standing near terrain risks her E (Heroic Charge) wall-stun — she controls the trade.","This is your longest-cooldown window and her power spike — she out-trades your weave with W up, so you're conceding and farming toward 6.","Public Execution blinks behind her and suppresses through W, and its passive armor pen plus healing cut her plating — the one window your lockdown ignores her whole anti-dash kit.","Your Eclipse spike is real, but Plated Steelcaps plus an early Heart of Steel blunt your all-physical Cunning Sweep-auto-Sundering Slam — the burst that wins other lanes is halved here, so it's even at best.","She scales into a peel tank with Heart of Steel and an R (Keeper's Verdict) knockback that bounces your dive — your physical damage runs into stacked armor and she reclaims the lane."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"quinn","win":["Quinn","Quinn","Skill","Quinn","Skill","Quinn","Quinn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Quinn's Harrier mark plus auto poke chips you for free, and the blind is Blinding Assault (Q) on an 11s cooldown, not Vault — it is what blanks your empowered Drakehound's Step auto. Concede CS, you have no dash-weave yet."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution takes the farthest champion in the line, and in a 1v1 lane that is always Quinn, so it cannot mis-target — the suppress lands through the kite distance she lives in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level-9 Q max lets you Q1-auto-Q2 for half her bar if you pin her with E Lacerate's near-total slow while her vault and Flash are down."},{"when":"Late","text":"Behind Enemy Lines is a channel — Public Execution's suppress ends it on the spot, so hold your R for her takeoff instead of chasing a roam you cannot follow."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Blinding Assault (11s at rank 1) with a throwaway cast, then commit — an empowered Drakehound's Step auto into her blind is the whole trade wasted","Survive levels 1-5 on even CS, then force the all-in the instant Public Execution comes online at 6 — it's your only answer to her kite distance","Pin her with E Lacerate's near-total slow so she can't vault or nimble-step your empowered Q-auto-Q out of range"],"foe":["Vault onto you to interrupt your cast and land back at her own attack range, then blind the follow-up auto with Blinding Assault","Stack Harrier marks and auto-poke you down, then nimble-step away before your Q cone or empowered auto connects","Vault away from your R's crash and roam off the wave with her move speed into lanes your dash-only kit can't rotate to"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Quinn and you have to accept it. At level 1 you have one ability, no combo, and you're energy-gated, while her Harrier mark plus auto poke chips you for free every time you step up to last-hit. Worse, her E doesn't just vault over you with a knockback — it blinds you, so even when you do build a Medarda stack the empowered Drakehound's Step auto whiffs. Do not chase the move speed: her nimble Harrier step means you never catch her in the open, and burning your dash going in just strands you as a dashless duelist inside her E knockback. Farm with the outer edge of your Q cone, eat the poke, and keep your HP high enough to reach 6.","mid":"This is the swing. Through levels 4-5 her vault still kites your dash chains and you keep conceding, but level 6 is your moment — Public Execution blinks you behind the farthest enemy in the line, and in a 1v1 lane that's always Quinn, so it can't mis-target. It suppresses through her kite and crashes her for a stun her nimble step can't escape. Bait or burn her E first (it's both her disengage and her engage, and its blind will eat your empowered auto if you trade into it), then R in, E Lacerate to slow her near-zero, and weave Q-auto-Q while she's pinned. If your R is down, do not engage — she just vaults out and pokes you back down.","late":"She reclaims the game the longer it goes. Your damage is entirely physical and her kit exists to never be in range of it — once she has two items and a Harrier reset to vault away from your R's crash, she out-ranges and out-roams you on a map your dash-only kit can't cross. Your realistic win is to be ahead off a level-6 or first-item kill and end before her scaling and roam pressure take the game elsewhere. If she's even or ahead late, stop hunting her solo: play for picks with your team and let your R lock onto whatever frontline target it can actually reach, not the Quinn kiting at the back of the line.","whys":["Quinn owns level 1 — you have one ability, no combo, and her Harrier mark plus auto poke chip you for free while you're energy-gated.","Vault does not knock you back — it interrupts your cast and drops her at her max range, and Blinding Assault erases the empowered auto you were saving for it.","Roughly even only because you finally have your short combo, but her poke still trades up — keep the wave central and don't overcommit a dash you'll need to escape her vault.","Your longest cooldowns meet her shortest here — Vault falls to 8s and Blinding Assault to 9s at max rank, so concede CS and farm to 6.","Level 6 is your spike: Public Execution blinks behind her, suppresses through the kite, and stuns her where her nimble step can't save her.","Eclipse plus the Q max is your strongest favor window — Q1-auto-Q2 chunks her half-health if E Lacerate's slow pins her with her vault down.","She out-scales the lane — two items and a Harrier reset let her vault away from your R and out-range your physical-only damage all game."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"renekton","win":["Skill","Renekton","Renekton","Skill","Skill","Renekton","Renekton"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Empowered Ruthless Predator stuns for 1.5s instead of 0.75s and destroys damage shields on you, so Repudiation is worthless the moment his Fury bar clears half — don't free-cast into his auto range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution flips it: R blinks behind him, suppresses and stuns, so even if he saves his Ruthless Predator stun he eats your full chain before he can Slice and Dice out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus Q max — Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam chunks half his bar, but Cull the Meek heals him every 7s flat, so Grievous Wounds is what makes the trade stick."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Renekton's biggest window: Ruthless Predator is 16s at rank 1 but 8s by rank 5, so from 4-5 the 1.5s Fury stun is up for nearly every wave and your chain still is not."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive his level 1-5 Fury bully and farm to your Level 6 Public Execution spike","Bait the empowered W — above 50 Fury it stuns 1.5s and strips your Repudiation shield before it works","Force every all-in on your Eclipse plus Q-max timer when his Fury and Ruthless Predator are down"],"foe":["Build past 50 Fury, then W to stun 1.5s and destroy your Repudiation shield in the same cast","Win short level 1-3 trades with point-click double-strike and empowered Cull the Meek heal","Snowball his early lead before your R and first item flip the lane at six"]},"early":"His Ruthless Predator is the whole problem early — at full Fury the empowered W is a hard stun that locks you out of your ability-into-empowered-auto chain, and his double strike plus the empowered Cull the Meek heal beats you in any short trade while your cooldowns are still long. Don't throw a Cunning Sweep into auto range hoping to free-cast; he'll just W-stun you and dump Fury before you can dash out. Farm with the outer edge of the cone, hold your Drakehound's Step dash to flinch out of the stun, and concede the level 1-3 window — you don't have the combo to fight him yet.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — his cooldowns are short, your Lacerate and Repudiation are long, so keep giving ground and farming toward six. Then Public Execution changes the math: it blinks to him, suppresses and stuns, and full Fury cannot buy its way out of a suppress, so you win the all-in he survived a minute earlier. Bait the W first — with Ruthless Predator down he can't stun and can't strip your Repudiation shield, so R-in, E-slow, and weave empowered autos before he can Slice and Dice away. His Fury bar is the tell: under 50 Fury means a 0.75s stun and no shield strip, and that's your window.","late":"This is the honest even part — Renekton falls off hard into items and has no sustained threat once you survive his early, but he stays relevant by playing short, Fury-fueled point-click trades and dashing out before you can extend. Your Eclipse spike and Q max own most mid-game all-ins, yet he refuses the long fights where your Drakehound's Step energy refund and Repudiation shield compound, trading in W-stun bursts instead. Keep trades long, deny the short Fury exchanges he wants, and your scaling edges a lane that otherwise stays a coinflip — not a free win either way.","whys":["His empowered W (Ruthless Predator) hard-stun and point-click double strike own level 1 while you have one ability and a long cooldown — farm, don't fight.","At full Fury his W-stun plus empowered Cull the Meek heal out-trades your level-2 Cunning Sweep before your dash chain even exists.","Around levels 3-4 your short combo starts coming online and his Fury isn't always up, so trades swing on who catches the W cooldown — neither wins on demand.","His cooldowns are shortest and yours longest at 4-5 — he out-trades your Lacerate and Repudiation, so concede the window and farm to six.","Public Execution blinks to him, suppresses and stuns — full Fury cannot answer a suppress, so the all-in his Ruthless Predator used to survive now kills.","Eclipse plus Q max means Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam halves him while you stay full, and his early kit has already fallen off — force fights now.","Your Drakehound's Step energy refund compounds in long fights, but never bank on Repudiation: above 50 Fury his W destroys damage shields outright, Sterak's Gage included."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"riven","win":["Riven","Riven","Skill","Riven","Skill","Riven","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Broken Wings is three casts on one 13s cooldown and the third knocks back, and Ki Burst stuns at 260 range on 11s — she full-combos you before Sundering Slam exists. Don't contest CS."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Now you have Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus Lacerate's slow, so you can punch back in a short trade — but only after all three Broken Wings casts are gone, and that is a 13s gap."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind the farthest target in the line, leaping past her Q dashes, then suppresses so her E shield-dash can't reset out — your cleanest kill window of the lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus your Q max chunks her, and Repudiation braced into her combo hits harder for every point it blocks — but Valor blocks damage back on a 10s cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait all three Broken Wings casts and Ki Burst, then Lacerate-slow and chain Cunning Sweep into an empowered auto","Hit Level 6 and R behind her so the suppress locks her E shield-dash and she can't reset out of the lockdown","Brace Repudiation into her combo — every point it blocks makes its own slam hit harder"],"foe":["Open with Ki Burst at 260 range to stun you into the full Broken Wings chain","Sidestep your Q-cone and E spin with her three Q dashes, then burst inside her own combo window","Step out of your commit with Valor on a 10s cooldown and block the burst on the way"]},"early":"Riven owns the first three levels here — her three-cast Q chains into a knockup on the third hop and her W is a point-blank stun, so she can full-combo you before your Q even unlocks Sundering Slam. Don't walk up to last-hit inside her Q range at level 1-2; she animation-cancels Q-W and you take a free chunk with no answer ready. Once you hit 3 you have your Q-cone into Sundering Slam plus E for the decaying slow, so you can punch back in a short trade — but only after she has thrown her three Q dashes at the wave or whiffed her W. Take her engage on your Drakehound's Step dash, not on your face.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still hers — your cooldowns are at their longest, and a fed Riven snowballs this window hard, so farm and respect her all-in. Then 6 flips it: Public Execution blinks to the farthest champion in your line, past her Broken Wings dashes, and the suppress means Valor cannot step her out of the lockdown. The stun on the crash is what lets you convert. Bait Ki Burst and her three Q casts first, then R the moment her dashes are spent — if you ult into a full combo with Valor still up, she blocks the burst and steps free, and the trade is even at best.","late":"This evens back out — your first-item spike (Eclipse/Profane plus the level-9 Q max) is real: Q-cone, empowered auto, Sundering Slam chunks her while your W brace eats the burst inside her combo window, and you scale into a clean AD bruiser. But Riven is a snowball fighter who never truly falls off, and her Q-W-E animation-cancel can still delete you in one window if she's ahead. Hold your W shield for her combo, never let her free-cast her three dashes onto you, and play it as the coinflip duel it is — whoever lands their full rotation first takes the fight.","whys":["Broken Wings chains three casts into a knockback and Ki Burst stuns at point blank, so she full-combos you at level 1 while you hold one ability and no answer.","She out-trades you through levels 1-2 with her animation-cancelled Q-W burst while your cooldowns are long and your combo isn't assembled yet.","At 3 your Q-cone into Sundering Slam plus the E slow matches her short trade — it's genuinely even once you punish her spent Q dashes.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window with your longest cooldowns, and a snowballing Riven punishes every step-up here.","Public Execution blinks you behind her past her Q dashes and suppresses her E shield-dash — her mobility can't answer your guaranteed lockdown.","Eclipse/Profane plus your Q max means Q-cone into Sundering Slam and an empowered auto halves her while your W brace eats the burst — your strongest favor window.","A coinflip duel — Blade of the Exile hands her bonus AD and attack range plus one Wind Slash, so whoever lands their full rotation first wins."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"rumble","win":["Skill","Rumble","Rumble","Skill","Skill","Rumble","Rumble"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Rumble's Flamespitter (Q) is a 600-range cone that burns for 3 seconds while you have one ability up and no Sundering Slam yet — last-hit at range, don't stand in it chasing a Drakehound's Step auto."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution (R) blinks to him and suppresses, and the crash stun holds him for the follow-up — but read the heat bar first. Above 50% he is in Danger Zone and every ability is empowered; at 100% he Overheats and cannot cast at all. Commit there."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus Q max: Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam (doubled on the first target) chunks him, and bracing Repudiation (W) through his Flamespitter amps your follow-up so his Q can't trade back."},{"when":"Overheat window","text":"Overheat is his weakest moment, not his strongest: at 100% heat he cannot cast a spell for a few seconds, so Lacerate (E) his legs and dump everything before the bar burns back down."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 6 and use Public Execution (R) to blink to him past his Electro Harpoon (E), suppress, and crash him while his heat sits at 100 and he cannot cast","Once Eclipse and Q max land, chain Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam with Drakehound's Step empowered autos, trading only while Flamespitter is on cooldown","Brace Repudiation (W) through his Flamespitter — the damage it blocks makes its own slam hit harder, so slam, then dash clear of the cone"],"foe":["Sit at 50-99% heat so Danger Zone empowers Flamespitter, and never let the bar hit 100 while you are still in range","Stack Scrap Shield (W) move speed with the Electro Harpoon (E) slow to kite your dash-weaves out of his fire cone","Drop the Equalizer (R) line across the choke to zone you off CS and deny your Level 6 all-in window"]},"early":"Rumble owns the first three levels and you have to respect it — his Flamespitter (Q) is sustained point-blank DPS for 3 seconds at 600 range while you have one ability up, long cooldowns, and no Sundering Slam unlocked yet. Do not stand in the fire cone to land a Drakehound's Step empowered auto; you lose every trade where his heat is above 50%, because Danger Zone empowers the cone. Last-hit at range, accept some chip, and step out completely once the heat bar crosses half. Your only clean poke is Lacerate (E) for the slow with a Drakehound's Step dash when his Q is on cooldown — but don't force it before 6.","mid":"Level 6 is where the lane flips to you. Public Execution (R) blinks to him past the Electro Harpoon (E) he wants to land, suppresses him, and the crash stun holds him through the follow-up. Time it by his heat bar, not his shield — Scrap Shield is a flat 6s and is never meaningfully down. Commit when he is at 100% and Overheating, because he cannot cast Flamespitter or The Equalizer for those few seconds; refuse the fight at 50-99%, where Danger Zone empowers everything he has. Brace Repudiation (W) into his Flamespitter so its own slam hits harder, then commit Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam.","late":"This is your window and it stays yours. With Eclipse and your Q maxed, Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam chunks him while a braced Repudiation eats his Flamespitter return and slams back harder for it. Rumble is an AP bruiser with no dash and no scaling escape — once you're on him with R up he can't peel you off. Electro Harpoon strips your magic resist two charges at a time from 850 range, so buy more MR than the matchup looks like it needs, and lead with ability damage into his Plated Steelcaps. Just don't all-in inside The Equalizer zone; bait its 130 seconds, then force the reset.","whys":["His Flamespitter (Q) is sustained point-blank DPS and you have one ability with long cooldowns and no Sundering Slam yet — he wins any level-1 trade inside the fire cone.","Through levels 2-3 his heat management plus Electro Harpoon (E) slow and Scrap Shield (W) speed kite your dash-weaves, and your cooldowns are still too long to fight through his Q.","Your short combo starts coming online, but it's a coin-flip on whether his Flamespitter is down — trade only when his Q is on cooldown and his heat is low.","Levels 4-5 are the turn: Flamespitter is still 8s but your Lacerate is down to 11s and Repudiation braced into his cone slams back harder.","Public Execution blinks to him, suppresses and stuns — spend it while he is Overheated at 100% and he cannot cast a thing back.","Eclipse plus Q max means Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam halves him, and a braced Repudiation punishes his cone return.","He has no dash and no escape, and leading with ability damage beats the Plated Steelcaps he buys — your R gap-close owns a 1v1 he cannot leave."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"ryze","win":["Ryze","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ryze","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With all three abilities you get your first real all-in: Cunning Sweep into the Sundering Slam follow-up, plus a Lacerate spin and its near-total slow, lets you stick to Ryze and land an empowered auto before Spell Flux into Rune Prison can root you again."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks to Ryze and suppresses him, and the crash stun holds him through the follow-up. Realm Warp is not an escape — it is a portal that only teleports a few seconds later, so hold him off it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level-9 Q max turns your Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam into an empowered-auto chain that chunks him in one trade window, before his mana stacks make him a true scaler."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Ryze's window: fully stacked he re-roots you with Spell Flux into Rune Prison every 9 seconds, and Banshee's Veil plus any MR he buys blanks your purely physical burst."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk up only after Rune Prison is on cooldown, dash with Drakehound's Step the moment Spell Flux lands, then chain Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam and a Lacerate slow for the empowered auto","Reach 6 and use Public Execution to blink to Ryze and suppress him — the crash stun holds him off his own Realm Warp portal long enough to finish the burst","Force the Eclipse and level-9 spike all-in while your physical damage still out-trades him, before 2+ items turn him into a raid boss"],"foe":["Land Spell Flux first so Rune Prison roots instead of only slowing, then free-poke with Overload from 1000 range","Buy Banshee's Veil to eat one Repudiation slam, and stack mana safely behind minions so she never gets a clean all-in","Survive to 2+ items where the root-reset combo, spellshield, and realm-warp let him kite her physical-only damage to death"]},"early":"Ryze out-ranges you at levels 1-2 — Overload throws 1000 units and your Cunning Sweep reaches 650 — so farm with the tip of the cone instead of stepping into Rune Prison range. At level 3 you finally have a kit: the root only lands if Spell Flux is on you first, so the orb is your warning, not the cage. Bait it, dash out with a move command mid-cast (Drakehound's Step), then close with Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam and a Lacerate spin so its near-total slow keeps him pinned for an empowered auto.","mid":"Levels 4-5 lean Ryze: your cooldowns are at their longest and his Q-E root cycles back before your trade resets, so concede a little CS and farm toward 6 rather than forcing a losing poke war. At 6 it swings your way — Public Execution blinks you behind him and suppresses him, hard-cancelling his realm-warp and letting you crash him down with R's bonus armor pen while the passive heals you on every hit. Hold the ult until his spellshield is down, or he simply eats the blink-suppress on a shielded instance and you waste your whole burst window.","late":"This is where Ryze reclaims the lane and you have to respect it. A fully stacked Ryze re-applies Spell Flux and re-roots with Rune Prison faster than you can reset trades, and Overload resets off every other cast so the poke never stops, while your purely physical damage stalls into Banshee's Veil and any MR he buys. Your plan is to have closed the game on the 6-and-first-item window; if it goes long, group and force him onto your terms instead of dueling a raid boss who out-kites your melee range.","whys":["Overload reaches 1000 units to your 650 and you have one ability and no dash chain yet, but his level-1 is also weak, so take no trades and last-hit at the cone's edge.","Rune Prison comes online but it only roots through Spell Flux, his early combo damage is low, and your cooldowns are long — it stays a farm lane.","At 3 your full kit unlocks: Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus a Lacerate slow lets you dash on, stick, and land an empowered auto before his root combo is back up.","Levels 4-5 are his: Rune Prison is back every 10s and Overload resets off his other casts, so he roots and pokes while you concede and farm to 6.","Public Execution blinks to Ryze and suppresses him, and the crash stun keeps him off his own Realm Warp portal — that is your clean burst window.","Eclipse plus the level-9 Q max means a Cunning Sweep into empowered-auto into Sundering Slam chain chunks him in one trade before his mana stacks make him a raid boss.","Fully stacked, Ryze re-roots with Spell Flux into Rune Prison on repeat while Banshee's Veil and MR blank your physical-only burst — 2+ items are his."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"sejuani","win":["Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-cone into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step dash gives you a real short-trade combo. Permafrost is on a 1.5s cooldown, so it is never down — the only thing gating her stun is the Frost gauge. Trade before it fills, then dash out."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks to her and suppresses, and the crash stun finishes it. Glacial Prison is 120s at rank 1 — the moment it is spent she has one 18s knockup left and no real way to answer your all-in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level-9 Q max: Q1-auto-Q2 chunks her before Frozen Heart and Sunfire land, and Frost Armor's slow immunity is the only thing blanking your Lacerate."},{"when":"Lvl 6+ (her side)","text":"If she stacks four Frost on you with autos and W and lands the Permafrost E stun, then Q-dashes in, she reverses a trade — never sit in lane with four Frost stacks on you and her E up."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade before she builds four Frost stacks on you, weaving Q-into-Sundering-Slam and an empowered auto, then Drakehound-dash out before her Permafrost E can stun you","Punish Arctic Assault — 18s at rank 1 and her only engage, so all-in the moment she has spent it on the wave","Land R behind her at 6 to suppress + stun through her resists, and close the lane before she finishes the tank items that wall your physical damage"],"foe":["Stack four Frost on you with autos and Winter's Wrath, land the Permafrost E stun, then Q-dash in to reverse the trade","Keep Frost Armor up so your Lacerate slow does nothing at all, and stack Frozen Heart and Sunfire","Survive to mid-game teamfights where her Glacial Prison pick + empowered-R slow zone matter more than the 1v1 she loses"]},"early":"Sejuani's only hard lockdown is Permafrost, and it does not fire until she has stacked four Frost on you with autos and Winter's Wrath — so watch that gauge, because its cooldown is 1.5s and will never save you. Level 1 is even: Frost Armor comes from being out of combat and grants armour, magic resist and slow immunity, so your Lacerate slow does nothing until it breaks. From level 2-3 your Q cone into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step dash lets you weave an empowered auto and pull back before she can stack you. Never sit on four stacks in her range.","mid":"This is your lane. Her engage is Arctic Assault, an 18s knockup at rank 1 that stops on the first champion it hits, and once it is spent she cannot start anything for the better part of twenty seconds — that is the window. Dash-weave Q1-auto-Q2 and crash empowered hits while your Frost gauge is low. At 6 your R is the difference-maker: Public Execution blinks to her, suppresses and stuns, so the moment Glacial Prison is down you have a guaranteed all-in. And never eat the stun: Fury of the North lets her shatter a stunned target for massive magic damage, which is where the real burst in her kit lives.","late":"You out-1v1 her all game, but she is a tank with a teamfight ult, so the threat moves off the lane. She'll stack Frozen Heart and Sunfire and your damage is entirely physical, so a fully-itemized Sejuani is a wall. Snowball your lead into objectives and her tower early; don't expect to delete her once she's tanked up. In fights, dodge Glacial Prison — one stun and Fury of the North shatters you — and don't waste your R blinking onto her when a squishy is the real target.","whys":["Even at 1 — Frost Armor from being out of combat gives her armour, magic resist and slow immunity, and you have one ability, so neither of you wins the opener.","Your Q-into-Sundering-Slam plus a Drakehound dash gives you a short-trade combo before she has stacked four Frost on you to arm her Permafrost stun.","Full kit online: dash-weave an empowered auto after Q and pull out with Drakehound's Step before she can stack you up and land the E stun.","Punish Arctic Assault: 18s at rank 1, her only engage, and it stops dead on the first champion it touches. Trade the moment it is gone.","Public Execution blinks to her, suppresses and stuns, and Glacial Prison is 120s — once she has thrown the bola she has no answer left at all and the all-in is guaranteed.","Eclipse plus the level-9 Q max means Q1-auto-Q2 chunks her, and it lands before Frozen Heart and Sunfire are anywhere near finished.","The lane is yours all game, but as a tank she shifts the threat to teamfights — her Glacial Prison pick and empowered-R slow zone outweigh the 1v1 she loses, so close it out before then."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"sett","win":["Sett","Sett","Sett","Skill","Sett","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Sett's grit-charged W needs damage taken to fill, so at level 1 it hits for almost nothing — chip him with your Q cone's doubled outer edge and step out before his alternating-punch passive trades back."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Facebreaker only stuns if it catches enemies on both sides of him — alone on one side you are only slowed. Keep the wave off his far side and his 16s pull cannot hold you still for the grit-fed Haymaker."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Both ult at 6. The Show Stopper carries you 400 units and slams, and he saves a stored Haymaker for the landing — so dive only after his Grit bar is spent, never into a full one."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse or Profane Hydra lets you burst back in short windows, but Haymaker's shield scales with the damage you just dealt him — punish his 18s cooldown, don't fill the bar first."}],"wants":{"you":["Keep trades SHORT — land the Q cone's doubled outer edge plus one Drakehound's Step empowered auto, then dash out before his Grit bar fills","Bait Facebreaker with your dash and punish the 16s gap, and never let a minion sit on his far side or the pull becomes a stun","Stand off the centre line of Haymaker — the middle is true damage and the sides are only physical — and never extend past one rotation"],"foe":["Line you up with a minion on his far side so Facebreaker stuns instead of only slowing, then dump a full Grit Haymaker","Drag every trade long so his alternating punches and missing-health regen out-grind your energy-gated combo","Hit 6 and Show-Stopper you into terrain, then Haymaker for the kill while your R blink is the weaker reposition"]},"early":"Level 1 is your cleanest window — Haymaker is empty until he soaks damage to fill its Grit bar, so chip him with the doubled outer edge of your Q cone and walk off before his alternating punches add up. From 2 he has Facebreaker, but it only stuns when it catches enemies on both sides of him: stand so the wave is never on his far side and the pull is a slow, not a hold. Trade in single rotations — Q into one Drakehound's Step empowered auto, then dash out on the input — and never stand in the centre of a loaded Haymaker.","mid":"Levels 3 through 6 are his lane to own. Your cooldowns are at their longest here while Grit, his missing-health regen and a charged Haymaker let him out-grind your energy-gated combo past one rotation. Bait Facebreaker with your dash before you commit — it is 16s at rank 1, and if he whiffs it that is your opening for Q1, the Sundering Slam line and an empowered auto. At 6 don't trust your R to win the all-in: The Show Stopper plus a stored Haymaker flips your dive into a kill on you. Farm, keep off his far side, and concede the levels you can't fight through.","late":"Once Eclipse or Profane Hydra and the level-9 Q max come online, the lane finally levels off — your Q1-auto-Q2 burst lands in short windows where his Grit bar cannot fill. Remember which part of Haymaker hurts: the centre is true damage and the sides are physical, so step off the line rather than trying to armour through it. Sett never stops being a Grit threat, and a Bami's-into-Sundered-Sky build out-sustains you in long fights, so punish his 18s cooldown instead of facetanking. This stays a coinflip decided by who lands their CC and who refuses the extended trade.","whys":["Sett's Haymaker is empty at level 1 until grit fills it, so your Q cone's doubled outer edge beats his bare alternating-punch autos before his kit comes online.","At 2-3 his Facebreaker pull and a charging Haymaker arrive, but your Q-slow into one empowered auto still matches him if you fight a single rotation — it's genuinely even on discipline.","Facebreaker plus a Grit-fed Haymaker out-trades you in any extended fight — and the pull stuns whenever the wave is on his far side.","Your cooldowns are longest in this window while Grit and his missing-health regen out-grind your energy-gated combo — he owns 4-5.","Both ult at 6, but his Show Stopper grab-slam and a charged Haymaker flip your R-dive into a kill on you — he wins the all-in.","His Bami's-into-Sundered-Sky sustain out-grinds your first-item burst in long fights, so he keeps the edge until your scaling fully lands.","Your Eclipse/Profane spike and Q max let you trade back in short bursts before Grit fills — the lane evens into a discipline coinflip."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"shen","win":["Skill","Shen","Shen","Skill","Skill","Shen","Shen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Spirit's Refuge blocks attacks, not abilities — your Cunning Sweep, Sundering Slam and Lacerate all land through it. Save the empowered auto for after the zone, and spend spells inside it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks to him, suppresses and stuns, and Shadow Dash is 18s at rank 1 — bait the taunt, then commit while he has nothing left to interrupt the chain with."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus Q max gives you Q1-auto-Q2 burst — your hardest all-in window, before he stacks armour and before Ki Barrier's shield comes back for every spell he casts."},{"when":"Late","text":"Spirit's Refuge eats two empowered autos a fight and stacked armour blunts your all-physical kit, so he stops dying 1v1 and Stand-Unites onto a fight elsewhere on 200s."}],"wants":{"you":["Land the Q-cone to unlock Sundering Slam, then Drakehound's Step dash into an empowered auto before Spirit's Refuge is up","Hit Level 6 and blink-suppress with Public Execution while his Shadow Dash sits on its 18s cooldown","Keep casting inside Spirit's Refuge — it blocks attacks only — and hold the empowered auto until the zone drops"],"foe":["Drop Spirit's Refuge on your empowered-auto window and keep re-shielding with Ki Barrier every cast","Land Shadow Dash to taunt you out of your chain and drag you into his minions","Sit even, sustain through your trades, and use Stand United to swing a fight elsewhere on the map"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are a wash — you have one ability and you're energy-gated on long cooldowns, while he farms with spirit-blade autos and re-shields off Ki Barrier every time he casts. Don't force it. At 3 your Q-cone into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step dash into an empowered auto finally out-damages his auto trades. Spirit's Refuge only blocks attacks, so keep casting inside it and hold the empowered auto until it drops. His E taunt is the trap — never dash at him while it's available or he yanks you and free-trades.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are even — your cooldowns are at their longest and Twilight Assault scales off your max health, so trade only when Spirit's Refuge is spent and never long. Six is your real window: Public Execution blinks to him, suppresses and stuns, and Shadow Dash at 18s is the only thing that could have broken the chain. He has no burst back, so a clean R into Q1-auto-Q2 is a real kill — especially while Stand United sits on its 200s cooldown saving a fight elsewhere, which is exactly why he wants to leave lane.","late":"This flips to him. Late, Spirit's Refuge blocks two of your empowered autos every fight and stacked armour blunts your all-physical damage — you stop killing him 1v1. He becomes a map piece: Stand United shields a diving teammate and teleports to them while you stall a duel you can't close. Win your Level 6 and first-item windows on the scoreboard, or he out-utilities you into the late game.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s — you're one ability and energy-gated, he's just auto-and-shield, so neither side has a real opening.","Level 2 gives you Q plus E for a slow-into-trade, but your cooldowns are long and Spirit's Refuge blanks the empowered auto — stay even and farm.","Your full short combo comes online, and your abilities land through Spirit's Refuge even when your empowered auto does not — you out-trade his blade autos.","Levels 4-5 your cooldowns are at their longest and he sustains through your trades with Q and Spirit's Refuge — neither side wins a clean extended trade.","Public Execution guarantees the gap-close, the suppress and the crash stun, and Shadow Dash at 18s is the only interrupt he owns — bait the taunt and he has no answer.","Eclipse and Q max give you Q1-auto-Q2 burst that beats a Shen with no kill pressure — your hardest favor window before he buys armor.","Spirit's Refuge blocks two empowered autos a fight and stacked armour blunts your all-physical kit, while Stand United shields and teleports elsewhere — late is his."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"singed","win":["Skill","Singed","Singed","Skill","Skill","Singed","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Lacerate's near-total decaying slow pins Singed in place, and dashing out of it with Drakehound's Step re-triggers a second spin at your destination — enough lockdown to land an empowered auto before he Flings you and W's away."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks to the fleeing Singed, suppresses him and crashes him down for a brief stun — the one lockdown his speed can't outrun. His speed is Noxious Slipstream and Insanity Potion, not Mega Adhesive: the goo is a grounding slow zone."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the Q max: Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam (doubled on the first target) chunks him faster than his poison trail and drain sustain heal back — burst him before the fight goes long."},{"when":"Late","text":"Singed's scaling and proxy farm pull the lane even or ahead — Mega Adhesive grounds your dash chains exactly where he wants the fight, and without R up you cannot pin him through his HP."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Lacerate's decaying slow to glue Singed in place, then Drakehound's Step through it for the second spin and an empowered auto before he kites out","Save Public Execution to blink-suppress him when he flees, and use it before he throws Mega Adhesive under your feet","Force short, high-damage trades with Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam at first item, on ground he has not covered with Mega Adhesive yet"],"foe":["Fling you into Mega Adhesive for the root, then walk off on Noxious Slipstream speed","Proxy the wave behind your tower to deny you free farm and dodge your level-6 R timing","Drag every fight long, then pop Insanity Potion so his Poison Trail cuts your Conqueror healing in half"]},"early":"Singed barely contests levels 1-2, and neither do you — Cunning Sweep alone with no Sundering Slam follow-up means just farm and don't chase him into his poison trail. At 3 your kit comes alive: Lacerate's near-total decaying slow is the key, because it's the only thing that lets a Drakehound's Step dash close on a champion who drafts free move speed off Noxious Slipstream — and dashing through the spin re-triggers it at your destination. Land the slow, dash in, weave an empowered auto, and back off before he Flings you. Never stand in Mega Adhesive: it grounds you, and grounded there is no dash to leave with.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his window — he'll proxy behind your tower, deny you free farm, and Noxious Slipstream plus poison chip mean he kites your longest cooldowns. Don't burn dashes chasing; farm and hold for 6. Public Execution is the answer to everything Singed is built around: it blinks to him as he flees, suppresses him, then slams him down for a brief stun — the single lockdown his uncatchable kit can't outrun. Slow with Lacerate, R him, then Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam while he's locked — and fight on clean ground, because Mega Adhesive grounds every dash in your chain.","late":"This is where Singed reclaims it and why the lane sits even — his scaling and proxy farm keep him level, and a fed Singed drops Mega Adhesive on top of you to ground the dash chain you need. Without Public Execution up you simply cannot pin him. His Insanity Potion runs 100s and makes Poison Trail apply Grievous Wounds, so your Conqueror healing is halved for the whole fight. Don't chase him through poison toward his tower. Lean on R to catch him isolated, force the short burst, and let your team answer the proxy sidelane.","whys":["You have only Cunning Sweep and no Sundering Slam follow-up at level 1 — Singed just proxies and poisons, so neither of you commits; farm and stay out of the trail.","Still even at 2 — your cooldowns are long and Noxious Slipstream plus his poison chip kite any trade you start.","At 3 your combo lands: Lacerate's near-total decaying slow glues him long enough for a Drakehound's Step dash and re-spin into an empowered auto, beating his kite.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest and his strongest — he proxies your farm, and Mega Adhesive grounds the dash chain your longest cooldowns depend on.","Public Execution blinks to the fleeing Singed and suppresses him into a brief stun — the one lockdown his uncatchable kit can't escape.","Eclipse plus the Q max spikes you hard: Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam chunks half his health before his poison trail and drain sustain can heal it back.","Singed's scaling and proxy farm keep him level, Mega Adhesive grounds your dash chains, and Insanity Potion's Grievous Wounds halves your healing for 100 seconds at a time."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"sion","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Sion"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q cone into the Sundering Slam follow-up plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto out-trades a Sion who only has his E (Roar of the Slayer) poke and a one-point Decimating Smash to answer with."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks to him and suppresses him out of the fight — and Soul Furnace is not just a shield, it re-detonates after 3 seconds for magic damage, so time the crash to land after it pops."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level 9 Q max lets Q1-auto-Q2 chunk him while you stay full, before his max-HP scaling and stacked armor start mattering."},{"when":"Late","text":"Sion's window: Unstoppable Onslaught is 140s at rank 1 and its knockup scales with how far he has charged, a fully-charged Decimating Smash interrupts your dash chain, and the zombie passive keeps him swinging after you kill him."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his charged Decimating Smash, sidestep the knockup, then dash-weave Q-auto-Q while it recharges and his E is the only threat left","Brace Repudiation into his Q slam or the Soul Furnace pop — the damage it blocks makes Repudiation's own slam hit harder","Hit your level 6 and Eclipse spikes and take plates and tower before his max-HP scaling and armor flip the lane"],"foe":["Land a fully-charged Decimating Smash to knock you up and cancel your Drakehound's Step dash chain","Shred your armour with Roar of the Slayer, bouncing it through a minion if you hide behind the wave, then shield up and shove","Survive lane, stack max HP and armour, and reach the fights where Unstoppable Onslaught starts them from off-screen"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash: Sion shoves and chips you with Roar of the Slayer, which shreds armour and reaches 800 — and if it clips a minion the minion is knocked back through you carrying the same damage, slow and shred, so hiding behind the wave does not help. You only have one ability, so last-hit and don't throw a naked Q. The lane turns at 2 and 3: your Q cone unlocks the Sundering Slam follow-up and the passive dash weaves an empowered auto, out-trading his one-point Decimating Smash. The one thing to respect is a fully-charged Q — the knockup interrupts your dash, so bait it or sidestep.","mid":"This is your best stretch, but keep it honest. Through 4-5 trade only when Decimating Smash is down, and remember Soul Furnace reactivates after 3 seconds to damage everything near him — leaving before the second half is the trade. At 6 Public Execution blinks to him and suppresses, and if his Q is on cooldown that's a real kill, not just a chunk. Don't dump R into a fresh Soul Furnace with his Q up, though, because that's how an even lane hands Sion a free zombie-state revenge kill on the way down.","late":"Honest truth: late game tilts to Sion. Your damage is entirely physical, so once he stacks max HP and armour and the zombie state keeps him swinging after you kill him, your burst stops closing fights — and those zombie attacks heal him off your maximum health, which is the only place Grievous Wounds is worth a slot. Unstoppable Onslaught knocks up harder the further he has charged, so meet him early rather than letting him build speed. Win the lane on your level 6 and Eclipse windows and convert to objectives.","whys":["You have one ability and he can poke your last-hits with E armor-shred, so the opening trade is even — just farm and don't throw a Q he can step away from.","Your Q cone plus the Sundering Slam follow-up and an empowered dash-auto out-damage his one-point Decimating Smash and cooldown-bound E.","Full combo online: you weave Q-auto-Q faster than his cooldowns and win short trades as long as you dodge the charged knockup.","Through 4-5 both your cooldowns are long and Soul Furnace shields then detonates after 3s, so it stays even — trade when his Q is down.","Level 6 is yours when his Q is down — Public Execution blinks to him, suppresses, and crashes him for a stun he cannot shield away.","Eclipse plus the level 9 Q max lets Q1-auto-Q2 chunk him while you stay full, your clearest favor window before his scaling matters.","Late is his: stacked max HP and armour blunt your physical burst, and the zombie state heals off your max health, so close before this point."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"swain","win":["Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Swain","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"His window: Nevermove roots on the RETURN pass, not the outgoing one, and a root into Vision of Empire lands before Sundering Slam exists."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q cone into the unlocked Sundering Slam plus E's near-total slow lets you dash-weave one empowered-auto trade while his E root is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks to him and suppresses — Swain owns no dash, so the gap-close is the one thing his kit cannot answer."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the Q max: Q cone, empowered auto, Sundering Slam chunks half his HP before Demonic Ascension's drain can out-heal it."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk in after Nevermove's wave passes you, then dash in and chain the Q cone into Sundering Slam and an empowered auto","Hit 6 and Public Execution behind him to suppress before his W bomb or R drain matter","Reach Eclipse plus Q max so the Q-auto-Slam burst beats his R drain heal in a full commit"],"foe":["Root you with Nevermove's return pass, pull you in, then drop Vision of Empire straight on top of you","Collect Ravenous Flock soul fragments off you, then drag every fight into his indefinite drain form","Build early armor and Rylai's so his root sticks and your dash-weaving stalls out"]},"early":"Swain's whole early threat is Nevermove — and the trick is that the wave roots on its way BACK to him, not on the way out, so the safe moment is after it passes you and the dangerous one is a beat later. If it lands he pulls you in and gets a free Vision of Empire and Death's Hand while you have no Sundering Slam to answer. Death's Hand fires several bolts that stack damage per bolt, so standing square to him is the worst place to eat it. Last-hit at the edge of your Q cone. From 3 you can dash-weave one short trade — only when his E is down.","mid":"Through 4-5 his root-into-poke still out-trades you if you facecheck it, so farm and wait for 6. At 6 everything flips: Public Execution blinks to him and suppresses — Swain has no dash and no escape, so once you R him he cannot leave. Brace Repudiation into his bomb so its own slam hits harder, then chain Q-Slam. Demonic Ascension lasts indefinitely while he keeps draining a champion, so leave its 650 range rather than waiting it out.","late":"Your first item is your peak: Eclipse plus Q max means the Q cone, empowered auto and Sundering Slam halve him before Ravenous Flock's soul fragments heal it back. You out-1v1 a solo Swain all game because he can't escape your R blink-and-suppress. The real danger is the teamfight, not the lane — Demonic Ascension's drain and Nevermove's roots make him a monster in 5v5, so close the lane, deny his roams, and never let him scale into a frontline drain tank with you behind.","whys":["Nevermove roots on the return pass and Vision of Empire follows it, but he is immobile with no combo yet — neither side wins, so deny his Q last-hits.","He can still chain the root into W and Q if you facecheck it, and Sundering Slam is not unlocked — stay even.","The Q cone into Sundering Slam plus E's near-total slow lets you dash-weave a short empowered-auto trade in his E-root cooldown window.","Once Sundering Slam is online you out-trade his single Q poke when his root is down, tilting the farm lane your way.","Public Execution blinks to him and suppresses — with no dash anywhere in his kit, Swain has no escape from the lockdown.","Eclipse plus Q max means Q-auto-Slam out-bursts his Demonic Ascension drain before he stabilizes.","You own the solo duel — his only out is a teamfight, so end the lane before his AOE drain scales."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"sylas","win":["Sylas","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Chain Lash slows on impact and explodes at the intersection a beat later, and Kingslayer heals him off every trade, while you are one Cunning Sweep deep on long cooldowns."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your combo comes online — Lacerate's near-total slow into a Drakehound's Step dash that re-spins it, weaving an empowered auto, punishes Sylas hard while Abscond is on its 13s cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hijack steals your Public Execution and it is only 80s at rank 1 against your 130s — so his ultimate is up roughly twice as often as the one he is stealing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus your Level 9 Q max: Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam chunks half his bar faster than Kingslayer heals it."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach your Level 3 spike and bait Abscond's 13s cooldown before you commit Lacerate into the empowered auto","Hit your Eclipse window and force short Cunning-Sweep-into-Sundering-Slam trades that Kingslayer's heal cannot cover","Stay on him in extended trades so your Drakehound's Step refunds energy and your empowered autos out-pace his Q-W drain"],"foe":["Chip you with Chain Lash and then heal the whole trade back with Kingslayer's lunge","Dash out with Abscond, then recast Abduct to pull himself back onto you when you disengage","Wait out your R, then steal your Public Execution for a guaranteed blink-suppress gap-close of his own"]},"early":"Sylas owns the first two levels — Chain Lash chips you while you're a single Cunning Sweep deep with painfully long early cooldowns, and Kingslayer is a lunge that heals him back off anything you trade. It is a heal, not a shield, so denying him the hit is the only way to stop it. Farm with the outer edge of your Cunning Sweep cone (it doubles damage on the rim) and accept the chip. The lane flips the moment you hit 3: Lacerate for the near-total slow, then dash out of it with a move command to trigger the second spin, and weave an empowered auto. Bait Abscond first — 13s at rank 1.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your soft spot again — your cooldowns are longest here and Kingslayer out-sustains your short trades, so farm toward your spike rather than forcing. Watch his Petricite Burst charge too: every spell he casts arms an AoE auto. At 6 the lane is a coin flip on energy and ult timing: Hijack steals your Public Execution, and at 80s to your 130s he gets the exchange more often than you do. If your R is up and his isn't, the blink, the suppress and the crash stun guarantee the lockdown — that's your kill window, ideally after baiting Abscond.","late":"Your Eclipse first-item window is your best favor — Cunning Sweep into empowered auto into Sundering Slam with the Level 9 Q max chunks half his bar faster than Kingslayer can recover it, which is why Grievous Wounds earns its slot here. But Sylas scales too: once he stacks AP and cooldown reduction he kites your dash chains with Abscond, heals through your empowered autos, and Hijack comes back every 30s at rank 3. Your physical-only damage also stalls into any armour or Zhonya's he builds. Close the lane on your first-item spike.","whys":["Chain Lash chips you and Kingslayer heals it back while you're one Cunning Sweep deep with long cooldowns and no combo.","Level 2 gives you Cunning Sweep and Lacerate, and Petricite Burst only arms after he casts a spell — so trade on the beat before his charge is loaded.","Your combo is online: Lacerate's near-total slow into a Drakehound's Step dash-weave empowered auto out-trades him while his E chain-dash is down.","Levels 4-5 are your longest cooldowns against Kingslayer's 9s heal — disengage on Lacerate's slow rather than losing the extended fight.","At 6 it's a coin flip on energy management — his R steals your Public Execution, so the ult exchange comes down to who reads the other's energy and cooldowns.","Your Eclipse spike plus Level 9 Q max lets Cunning-Sweep-auto-Sundering-Slam chunk half his bar faster than Kingslayer heals, which is where anti-heal pays.","He out-scales you: a full-AP Sylas kites your dash chains with Abscond, heals through your empowered autos, and Hijack returns every 30s at rank 3."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"tahmkench","win":["Skill","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench","Skill","Skill","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Tongue Lash slows, heals him off you, and stacks An Acquired Taste — at three stacks he can stun you with Q or eat you with Devour, never both. Watch the count, not his cooldowns."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks to him and suppresses him in place, and the crash stun holds him for the follow-up. The number that decides it is his stack count on you: at three he answers with Devour, so commit at two or fewer."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus your Q-max chunk is your cleanest window — force the all-in while he sits under three stacks and Thick Skin's stored damage is already spent."},{"when":"Late","text":"His grey-health and percent-HP sustain scale with his max HP while your damage stays all-physical — every long fight refills the bar you emptied, and his R map roam pressures other lanes you can't follow."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q1 into Sundering Slam and weave the Drakehound-empowered auto before Thick Skin converts to a shield","Hold R until you are carrying fewer than three An Acquired Taste stacks, so he cannot answer the suppress with Devour","Spike to Eclipse and your Q max so your burst outpaces his percent-HP sustain in the 6-and-first-item window"],"foe":["Stack An Acquired Taste to three with Tongue Lash, then consume them for the stun that cancels your dash mid-chain","Bank your all-in as Thick Skin damage, then convert it to a shield and reset the trade","Survive lane and roam with R to snowball elsewhere while out-scaling your physical-only damage"]},"early":"Thick Skin is the whole problem early — your single Level 1 ability and your Level 2 Q+E barely dent him, because the stored damage becomes a shield on demand and heals him back out of combat. Do NOT walk up to free-cast a Q he can answer: Tongue Lash reaches 900, slows you, heals him off the hit, and stacks An Acquired Taste. The third stack is the one that matters — Q consumes it for a stun that cancels your Drakehound dash. Farm with the doubled outer edge of Cunning Sweep and count your stacks.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your worst window — your cooldowns are longest and Thick Skin plus Devour means he wins any extended trade you start, so wait for 6. Abyssal Dive is 21s at rank 1 and knocks up, so it is the one long cooldown worth baiting. Your R is the moment that flips this: Public Execution blinks to him, suppresses him in place, and the crash stun holds him through the follow-up. Time it by his stack count, not by a cooldown — at three stacks he chooses the Q stun or the Devour, so commit while you carry one or two.","late":"This stays his lane long-term. Thick Skin scales with the damage he takes and your damage is entirely physical, so every drawn-out fight refills the bar you just emptied — and once he stacks health items he simply out-lasts your combo. Tongue Lash heals him off every poke too, which is why Grievous Wounds is core rather than optional. Your only edge is tempo: win the 6-and-first-item window hard and cash it before he stops dying.","whys":["Thick Skin banks your single Level 1 ability and heals it back out of combat, and Tongue Lash heals him off you — the lane opens his.","Your Q+E gives a slow-into-trade, but his Q tongue out-slows you and grey health negates the chunk — it nets even, so don't force it.","Your short combo is online but Thick Skin converts the chunk to a shield and Tongue Lash heals him — you can't kill through yet, so it's a tie.","Levels 4-5 are your longest cooldowns against a 7s Tongue Lash — every cast heals him and moves you one stack closer to being stunned or eaten.","Public Execution suppresses him in place and the crash stun follows — your one clean kill window, taken while you carry under three stacks.","Your Eclipse plus Q1-auto-Q2 chunks half his bar before Thick Skin converts — this first-item window is the one you win, so force it.","His percent-HP grey-health sustain and HP scaling out-last your physical-only damage long-term, and his R roams pressure lanes you can't follow."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"teemo","win":["Skill","Teemo","Teemo","Skill","Skill","Teemo","Teemo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With Q (Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam), E (Lacerate) spin-slow and your Drakehound's Step dash all online, you can close the kite inside the 7s after Blinding Dart."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses, then crashes him for a stun and damage — it gap-closes and lands regardless of the blind, turning his one weakness (no escape) into a kill button."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus level-9 Q max is your peak: dash in, Q1-auto-Q2 with the doubled first-hit slam chunks half his bar before poison and shrooms ever matter."},{"when":"Late","text":"Teemo's real threat: shroom walls on every choke detonate your dash paths and a side-lane splitpush your single-target R can't reach through minions — close the lane before ~25 min or it slips."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Blinding Dart on a creep or a feint — it is 7s flat — then dash in and Lacerate-slow so he cannot kite the empowered attack","Reach 6 with health to spend, then R behind him to ignore the kite entirely — the suppress-stun chains straight into your full combo","Hit Eclipse/Profane + Q-max and force every trade on his blind cooldown before his shrooms and splitpush take over the map"],"foe":["Land Blinding Dart on your Drakehound's Step attack so your physical-only burst whiffs the trade","Kite on Move Quick and chip with Toxic Shot while Noxious Trap walls punish your retreat","Survive to late, stack shrooms on chokes and objectives, and splitpush where your single-target R can't body him"]},"early":"Teemo's Q blind is the whole problem early — it negates your basic attacks, including the empowered passive auto you build off every ability cast, which is your entire damage engine. At level 1 you have only Cunning Sweep and you're energy-gated, so don't walk into auto range to throw a Q he just blinds and kites away from. Last-hit at the outer edge of your Q cone (where it deals double), accept some E-poison chip, and wait for 3 — once Q-into-Sundering-Slam, your Lacerate spin-slow and the Drakehound's Step dash are all online, you can finally close on him the instant his blind is down.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your worst window — cooldowns are longest here and his move-speed kite plus poison chips you while you whiff blinded autos, so farm and hold for your spike. Everything flips at 6: Public Execution blinks you behind the farthest target, suppresses, then crashes him down for a stun and damage, and it gap-closes and connects regardless of the blind — the one tool that beats a Teemo who has no escape once reached. Bait the blind, Lacerate-slow to glue him, then R behind to lock the kill. With Eclipse/Profane and your level-9 Q max you out-damage his poke and win every all-in.","late":"You win the straight 1v1 all game once you have R and an item — he has no disengage when you're on top of him, and your R's flat armor pen plus on-ability healing keep you healthy through the dive. But Teemo becomes a map problem: shroom walls on every choke blow up your dash paths, and his splitpush sits in side lane where your single-target R can't body him through minions. Your physical-only damage also gets answered by any armor he or his team builds. Win the lane and snowball a lead before ~25 minutes so his scaling and vision game never get to decide the game.","whys":["Blinding Dart takes the Drakehound's Step attack you build off every ability cast, and at 1 you hold only Cunning Sweep — he chips free with Toxic Shot, so last-hit at the outer edge of the cone.","Q plus Lacerate at level 2 gives a slow-into-trade, but your cooldowns are long and his move speed plus blind keep it even — don't force an extended fight you can't finish.","At 3 your full Q-into-Slam combo and Drakehound's Step dash are online — bait the blind, dash in and Lacerate-slow, and you out-trade his poke while his Q is down.","Levels 4-5 are your longest-cooldown window and Move Quick plus Toxic Shot chip out-trades you here — concede the lane and farm toward 6.","Public Execution blinks behind him, suppresses, then stuns, and it gap-closes through the blind — no escape on Teemo means it is your guaranteed answer to the kite.","Eclipse/Profane plus Q max means Q1-auto-Q2 with the doubled first-hit slam halves him before his poison matters — keep forcing the all-in on his blind timer.","You still win the duel, but it comes down to execution: his shrooms wall your dash paths and his splitpush dodges your single-target R, so the lane is decided by whether you close fast or he scales."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"trundle","win":["Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Skill","Trundle","Trundle","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q-into-Sundering-Slam combo comes online, but Chomp saps your AD again every 3.5s and King's Tribute tops him up off dying minions — chip with the doubled outer-edge Q, don't commit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses and stuns, and your R passive heals you off every ability — your cleanest all-in, and Trundle's R is purely defensive so it can't deny the kill."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level-9 Q max: ability-into-empowered-auto chunks his bar while your R passive lifesteal answers his Chomp heal — this is your strongest favour window before he stacks resists."},{"when":"Late","text":"Subjugate takes a percent of your armor and MR and doubles it over 4 seconds, so armour stacking partly arms him, and Chomp keeps sapping your AD — at 2+ items his steal and Frozen Domain sustain reclaim the duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Land your Q outer-edge plus the Sundering-Slam first-hit double, then Drakehound-dash into an empowered auto before his Chomp bite resets the trade","Hit your level-6 Public Execution all-in for the suppress-and-stun while your R passive lifesteal out-heals his Chomp","Buy Grievous Wounds early — Frozen Domain amplifies every heal he takes — and force your Eclipse spike before his resist-steal scales"],"foe":["Chain Chomp every 3.5s to sap your AD, flipping every short trade in his favour","Drop Pillar of Ice, 21s at rank 1, as impassable terrain across your dash lane in","Reach 2+ items and ult your resistances with Subjugate so his sustain out-grinds your physical-only damage"]},"early":"King's Tribute is the whole early game — he heals a slice of his maximum health off every unit that dies near him, so the wave itself out-sustains your chip. Chomp adds a 3.5s AD sap you cannot wait out; brace Repudiation on the bite instead, because non-minion damage blocked in the brace amplifies the slam you fire back. Don't sit at one ability level 1; you're energy-gated, so farm and chip with the doubled outer edge of your Cunning Sweep. Once your level-3 combo is online you can Drakehound-dash into an empowered auto, but keep trades short and off his Frozen Domain.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your weak window — your cooldowns are longest and King's Tribute refunds him off the wave, so concede and farm toward 6. Then Public Execution flips it: blink 1250 to the farthest target in your line, suppress, and crash him down for the stun — Subjugate is purely defensive, so he can only survive the all-in, not deny it. Pillar of Ice is the real timer: 21s at rank 1, and it is his one answer to your dash chains. Bait it on a step-up, then commit your combo into the 21 seconds it is gone.","late":"Your first-item Eclipse spike is the high point — ability into empowered auto into Q2 chunks his bar, and Grievous Wounds bought before it cuts King's Tribute in half. But this is a clock: at 2+ items Trundle is a drain-tank who reclaims the lane. Subjugate takes a percent of your health, armor and MR and doubles it over 4 seconds, so every resistance you stack partly arms him, while Frozen Domain amplifies every heal he takes. Win it on your first-item all-ins or accept he scales past you.","whys":["Chomp saps your AD every 3.5s and King's Tribute heals him off each unit that dies near him, and you hold one ability — chip with Cunning Sweep's outer edge and don't trade.","Your Q-into-Slam trade exists, but Cunning Sweep is 14s while Chomp is 3.5s, so he bites four times a rotation — it stays a coin-flip skirmish.","Your level-3 dash-weave bursts, but Chomp's AD sap lands again in 3.5s — brace Repudiation on the bite instead of racing it.","Your cooldowns are longest here and King's Tribute refunds him health off every unit that dies near him, so he edges the 4-5 farm fight.","Public Execution blinks 1250 to the farthest target in your chosen line, suppresses, then stuns — Subjugate is purely defensive, so he survives it rather than denying it.","Your Eclipse spike with the level-9 Q max chunks his bar per combo, and Grievous Wounds bought now cuts King's Tribute before Frozen Domain amplifies it — force the all-in.","Subjugate takes a percent of your health, armor and MR and doubles it over 4s, so stacking resists partly arms him — at 2+ items his steal plus Frozen Domain sustain reclaim the duel."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"tryndamere","win":["Skill","Tryndamere","Tryndamere","Skill","Skill","Tryndamere","Tryndamere"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Trynd's crit autos plus Spinning Slash out-DPS your single ability before your Q-into-E combo exists, so concede the level and farm at max Q-cone range where the outer edge doubles your damage."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R blinks behind the farthest target and suppress-stuns him, but it does NOT execute — Undying Rage parks him at minimum HP for 5s and feeds his Fury, so you just get spun down on the way out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse + Profane Hydra online is your one real window — chain Q1-empowered-auto-Q2 to chunk him, but only commit when his E and Undying Rage are both down or you trade the all-in for your own life."},{"when":"Late","text":"He out-duels and splitpushes; crit Spinning Slash shreds you while your all-physical damage hits his late armor, and Undying Rage means you can never close the 1v1 no matter how perfect the R."}],"wants":{"you":["Buy Grievous Wounds, then catch him with Spinning Slash and Undying Rage both down for a Q-empowered-auto-Q burst","Use E (Lacerate)'s near-total slow plus a Drakehound's Step dash for the second spin to stick when he tries to disengage","Bait Undying Rage with Repudiation's braced slam, then re-engage only once the immortality ends and his Fury has drained"],"foe":["Extend every trade so Bloodlust and his rising low-health AD out-grind your long cooldowns","Catch you with your back turned so Mocking Shout slows, land Spinning Slash, then spin out on its 12s","Pop Undying Rage to survive your all-in at minimum HP, regen Fury off the spin, and flip the kill back onto you"]},"early":"Tryndamere just out-damages you levels 1-3 — his crit autos and a free Spinning Slash beat your single early ability, and your Q-into-E combo isn't even online at 1. Don't contest the spin trade; farm at the outer edge of your Q cone (Cunning Sweep) where it deals doubled damage, then back off. Mocking Shout shaves your AD whether or not you face him, but it only slows you if your back is turned — walk out facing him and Spinning Slash arrives a beat late. Bloodlust is 12s and free, so chip you don't convert is chip he simply heals back.","mid":"At 6 you finally have a real combo, but his R is the whole problem: Public Execution blinks you behind the farthest enemy, suppresses and ends in a brief stun — yet it is NOT an execute, so Undying Rage parks him at minimum HP while refunding Fury and your all-in hands him a free spin-down on your exit. Undying Rage is 120s at rank 1 and Spinning Slash is 12s; commit only when both are spent, and lean on E (Lacerate)'s slow and your passive dash rather than trading autos into his crit. Grievous Wounds has to be on the board before the burst, not after it — Bloodlust is a 12s heal. Your first item (Eclipse + Profane Hydra, Q maxed) is your one favour window: Q1-empowered-auto-Q2 chunks him, so look for the pick when his defensives are already spent.","late":"This is his game, not yours. Tryndamere's crit Spinning Slash shreds you in a straight duel, and Undying Rage means you physically cannot close the 1v1 — your R is a blink-suppress-slam, not an execute, so it can't punch through his 5-second immortality. Your damage is all physical, so his late armor and your lack of any true damage stack against you. Don't try to win the splitpush 1v1; group and use Public Execution as engage onto his backline instead of dueling him, and let your team punish whichever side lane he isn't shoving.","whys":["His crit autos and Spinning Slash DPS beat your single level-1 ability — you have no combo and long cooldowns, so you lose the opening trade outright.","Q-into-E gives you a slow-into-burst, but Bloodlust turns his Fury straight back into health — it stays close only if you refuse to extend past a rotation.","Your level-3 Q-E combo plus the Drakehound's Step second spin can win a quick dash-weave, but Spinning Slash is 12s and costs him nothing, so he resets and disengages — still a coinflip.","Your longest-cooldown window against a champion who pays nothing for his, and Bloodlust refunds the chip — farm toward Eclipse.","Your R suppress-stuns but does not execute; Undying Rage holds him at minimum HP for 5s and refunds Fury, so the all-in fails and he spins you down on the exit.","Even at your Eclipse + Profane peak he can pop Undying Rage through your Q-auto-Q burst and survive immortal — you only win if his R is already down.","He out-duels you with crit spin, his late armor blunts your all-physical damage, and Undying Rage means you can never finish the 1v1."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"urgot","win":["Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Urgot owns the opener — his Q (Corrosive Charge) lands a free ranged explosion-and-slow while your single Cunning Sweep and long level-1 cooldowns can't punish back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R blinks you behind him and suppresses straight through his E flip — the flip he wants to land on you does nothing while you're channeling, so it's your first real window to turn this even lane into a kill."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus Q maxed at 9: Q-cone-auto-Sundering-Slam chunks him, and Disdain is 16s at rank 1 — force that shield out on nothing first, then commit into the hole."},{"when":"Late","text":"Purge costs nothing and has no cooldown at rank 5, and his R impales then executes a low target — Disdain shields his exit, so never let a trade drag past your burst."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach 6 and use R to blink behind him, suppress through his E flip, and burst him with armor-pen damage while he can't reposition you","Bait Disdain first — it shields him for the whole charge — then weave your Q cone into a Drakehound's Step auto and step out of Purge","Hit your Eclipse/Profane + Q-max spike and force all-ins while Purge is still on a real cooldown and short on items"],"foe":["Land Corrosive Charge from 800 range and chip you with Purge before you reach empowered-auto range","Catch you with Disdain, shielded through the charge, and hurl you back into Purge range","Drag every fight long so his W percent-max-HP legs and R fear-execute out-DPS your short burst windows"]},"early":"Urgot owns the first few levels — Corrosive Charge drops a free 800-range explosion and slow on you while you have one ability, a 14s cooldown, and no combo to answer with. Don't walk into that range trying to last-hit; you'll eat the charge and his Purge follow-up for nothing. Farm with the outer edge of your Q cone, take the chip, and wait — once Cunning Sweep into Lacerate and your Drakehound's Step dash are online around 3 you can weave one quick empowered auto and leave. Purge slows Urgot himself while he fires it, so step out sideways during the channel rather than dashing straight back.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — short cooldowns, his W legs hurt, and your trades are at their longest CD here, so keep farming toward 6. At 6 everything flips: R blinks you behind him and suppresses straight through his E flip — the move he normally uses to reposition you onto his legs does nothing while you're channeling. Land it, dump your Q cone into Sundering Slam and empowered autos, and your R passive armor pen plus on-ability healing eats his bruiser-tank durability. Bait the E flip before you all-in so it's down when you R.","late":"Your first-item window (Eclipse/Profane, Q maxed at 9) is your best stretch — Q-cone-auto-Sundering-Slam chunks half his bar once you have emptied the Disdain shield, which is 16s at rank 1. But this never becomes a free lane: keep fights SHORT. Purge's cooldown falls to nothing by rank 5, and the longer a fight runs the closer he gets to his R impale-and-execute. Burst on your terms with R up, and never let a low-HP trade drag into his execute range.","whys":["Corrosive Charge lands from 800 range and Purge chips in behind it, while your one ability and long level-1 cooldowns cannot answer.","You get Cunning Sweep into Lacerate for a slow-into-poke, but Purge out-damages it and every cooldown he has is shorter — stay even and farm.","Your short combo and Drakehound's Step dash weave one empowered auto, but Purge answers it and Corrosive Charge is only 10s — a coin-flip trade.","This is your weakest window — longest cooldowns while his Q poke and short CDs let him out-trade you, so concede and farm to 6.","R blinks you behind him and suppresses through his E flip, and your armor-pen burst flips this even lane into a kill threat.","Eclipse/Profane and Q-max give you a Q-auto-Sundering-Slam combo that chunks him — empty his Disdain shield first and the burst lands whole.","He reclaims parity at scale — Purge costs nothing and has no cooldown at rank 5, and his R execute out-grinds your burst if a fight goes long."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"vayne","win":["Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Ambessa","Skill","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Vayne owns the opener — Tumble is a 6s reposition and Condemn out-ranges your melee, energy-gated Cunning Sweep before you've unlocked Sundering Slam or Lacerate."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you 1250 behind her past any kite, suppresses and stuns — your only guaranteed catch, and Condemn's 20s means one baited bolt buys the whole follow-up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Q spike: Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto chunks her before Silver Bolts and her item curve come online."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Vayne's window — Silver Bolts' third hit is percent-HP true damage, and Final Hour cuts Tumble's cooldown so she kites your dash chains and walls you."}],"wants":{"you":["Save R (Public Execution) to blink behind her tumble, suppress and stun so she cannot kite the all-in","Reach your first-item Q spike and force every all-in while her Silver Bolts and item curve are still ramping","Land E (Lacerate)'s near-total slow and dash into a second spin to glue onto her before condemn resets the gap"],"foe":["Tumble every 6s to reposition so your Sundering Slam line and R direction whiff","Stack Silver Bolts true damage and Condemn you into a wall for the extra stun","Kite back to her two-item powerspike where percent-HP true damage out-races your R passive healing"]},"early":"Vayne owns the opener — at level 1 you have only Cunning Sweep and you're energy-gated, while Tumble resets her spacing every 6s and Condemn out-ranges everything you have. Don't walk into auto range to last-hit; farm with the outer edge of Cunning Sweep (it doubles on the rim) and eat a little poke rather than feed her Silver Bolts stacks. Once you hit 2-3 and your Q-into-Sundering-Slam plus Lacerate are online you can punish a spent Tumble, but the trade only pays off if you land E's near-total slow first — and stand off the wall, because Condemn only stuns you into terrain.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your weak window — cooldowns are longest here and a tumbling Vayne pokes and kites you while you farm toward 6. Then R flips it: Public Execution blinks you 1250 behind the farthest enemy in your chosen line, suppresses her on arrival and crashes her down for a stun, and there is no kite that outruns a blink. Bait Condemn first — 20s at rank 1 — then R in, Lacerate to lock her with the near-total slow, and Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam, chaining each cast into a Drakehound's Step empowered auto. Without R up, do not chase; Condemn punishes every overcommit, and it hurts most next to a wall.","late":"This is Vayne's game, not yours. Her Silver Bolts deal percent-max-HP true damage on every third hit, so the more you build the more she eats you — and armour is beside the point against true damage. Once she has two items Final Hour shortens Tumble, hides it, and she kites your Drakehound's Step chains and Condemns you into a wall for the stun. Win this lane on your first-item Q spike and snowball the map; if it goes long, group and force fights where your R catches her out of position rather than ever trying to 1v1 a fed Vayne in an open lane.","whys":["Vayne owns it — at level 1 you hold one energy-gated Cunning Sweep while Tumble resets her spacing every 6s and Condemn out-ranges you.","Roughly even — your Q-into-Sundering-Slam plus Lacerate's slow gives a real trade, but long early cooldowns mean you can't punish a tumble hard yet.","Even — your short combo wins a committed trade, but she only commits if you land Lacerate first; otherwise she kites and poke-resets.","Vayne's window — your level 4-5 cooldowns are longest here and a tumbling kiter out-trades you while you farm to 6.","You own it — Public Execution blinks 1250 behind her, suppresses through the kite and stuns; Condemn is 20s, so bait it first.","Your peak — first-item Q max into a Drakehound's Step auto chunks her before Silver Bolts and her item curve ramp.","Vayne reclaims it — Final Hour shortens Tumble and Silver Bolts' percent-HP true damage cuts straight through resistances at two items."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"vladimir","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Land Cunning Sweep to unlock Sundering Slam, weave a Drakehound's Step dash into the empowered auto, and Lacerate's slow pins a poolless Vlad — Sanguine Pool is 28s at rank 1."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him and suppresses through the wind-up — bait Sanguine Pool first or ult on its cooldown, because if he pools mid-cast he goes untargetable and the suppress whiffs entirely."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Vlad turns the corner here: Tides of Blood drops to 9s and Transfusion under 7s as his AP comes online, so his poke-and-heal cycle starts out-pacing everything your physical autos remove."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two-item Vlad pools your R suppress on reaction, kites your dash chains with Tides of Blood, and drains back everything your physical-only kit chips — Crimson Pact turns the health he buys into AP, so he simply out-scales you."}],"wants":{"you":["Force short dash-weave trades at 2-3 where Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus Lacerate's slow pin a poolless Vlad before his sustain scales","Bait Sanguine Pool with a Q poke, then R the moment it goes on its 28s so the suppress lands with no untargetable answer","Snowball the level-6-to-first-item window and end the game before his AP items turn the drain into an unkillable late"],"foe":["Hold Sanguine Pool for her Public Execution — pool as the R blinks behind you so the suppress whiffs and you reset the trade untargeted","Charge Tides of Blood where no minion blocks the release and heal the health cost back with a 9s Transfusion","Drag the game past two items where Crimson Pact turns his health stacking into AP and the drain out-scales her"]},"early":"Both of you are weak at level 1 — Vlad has one of the worst level-1s in the game, but you have one ability, no combo and an energy gate, so don't force the opening; just deny his Transfusion (Q) last-hits. Once you hit 2-3 you get a real edge: land Cunning Sweep to unlock Sundering Slam, weave a Drakehound's Step dash into the empowered auto, and Lacerate's near-total slow so he can't walk the trade off. Tides of Blood is blocked by your own minions, so hold the caster line and his poke stops paying — a poolless Vlad has no answer to that stick.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your soft spot: your cooldowns are longest here while his Tides of Blood (E) poke and Transfusion (Q) heal chip you as you wait on 6. Don't trade into a Vlad sitting on a full Sanguine Pool — it is 28s at rank 1 and 2 seconds of untargetable, long enough to swallow both the suppress and the slam. At 6 everything flips for one window: bait the pool with a Q poke, watch the 28s start, and ult inside it. Miss that read and you have spent a 130-second ultimate on a puddle — but past first item the lane starts tilting back to him as his AP and sustain scale.","late":"This is his game, not yours. A two-item Vlad pools your R suppress on reaction, kites your dash chains with Tides of Blood and movement, and drains health back with Sanguine and a sub-7-second Transfusion faster than your physical autos remove it. Crimson Pact turns every point of health he buys into AP, so the durability race is one you cannot enter. Win the lane outright in the 6-to-first-item window and make sure the game ends before his drain comes online; if it runs long, group and let your team burst him while he's pooled out of position.","whys":["Vlad has a famously weak level-1, but so are you — one ability, no combo, energy-gated — so neither side wins the opening; just deny his Transfusion last-hits.","Your Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus Lacerate's near-total slow and a Drakehound's Step dash out-trade a poolless Vlad before his sustain scales.","Whether the level 2-3 stick lands cleanly comes down to your combo execution and reading his Sanguine Pool — a fumbled dash-weave or an early pool lets him reset.","Your longest cooldowns land at 4-5 while Tides of Blood chips you — stand behind your casters, they block it, and wait on your ultimate spike.","Public Execution blinks behind him and suppresses — but Sanguine Pool is 2s of untargetable, so bait the 28s first and this is your one clean kill.","By first item Vlad turns the corner: Tides of Blood is down to 9s and Transfusion under 7s, so his poke-and-heal cycle out-paces your physical autos.","Two-item Vlad pools your R suppress, kites with E poke, and out-sustains your physical-only damage as his AP scales — he reclaims the lane and out-scales you."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"volibear","win":["Skill","Volibear","Volibear","Volibear","Volibear","Volibear","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Thundering Smash's run-up stun plus Frenzied Maul on a 5s timer out-brawls your one-ability, energy-gated early — don't trade until your combo exists."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your E slow plus a Drakehound's-Step second spin pins an immobile Voli in place for the Q-cone into empowered-auto trade he can't kite out of."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks 1250 behind him and suppresses through the brawl — deny his second Frenzied Maul on the mark and the heal never arrives."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus the Q max means Q1-auto-Q2 chunks him to half while you sidestep his Q stun approach and Sky Splitter slam."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach your level 3 combo so E-slow into a Drakehound's-Step second spin pins him for the Q-cone trade","Break Thundering Smash's run-up before the attack lands, dash clear, then R behind him while the Maul mark is dead","Force every all-in at first item where Q1-auto-Q2 outpaces his bite-heal sustain"],"foe":["Win levels 1-2 with the Thundering Smash run-up and a second Frenzied Maul on the mark to heal","Land the Thundering Smash attack to freeze your dash chain, then Maul twice while you're stunned","Ramp The Relentless Storm's attack speed in a long brawl, then dive with Stormbringer"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are genuinely his — Thundering Smash speeds him at you and the stun rides the first attack he lands, and Frenzied Maul is a 5s bite that heals him on the second cast against the same mark, so an extended trade refills whatever you chip. Hold farm and break the mark between bites rather than standing in them. The flip comes at 3: once your E spins the drakehounds for that near-total slow, a Drakehound's Step dash out of it triggers the second spin and an immobile Voli is glued in place for your Q-cone into empowered auto. Trade on that window, not before.","mid":"Through 4-5 it's even-to-his — your cooldowns are longest here and his Maul brawl is sticky, so farm and set up rather than forcing. At 6 you take over: Public Execution blinks you 1250 behind him and suppresses on arrival, and if you break the Frenzied Maul mark between his casts the bite never heals him, which flips a coinflip brawl into a kill. The thing that ruins it is Thundering Smash — the stun rides the first attack he lands, freezing your dash chain mid-combo. Don't give him that attack; hold out of range for the 12s, then commit.","late":"First item is your peak and you should be ending here — Eclipse/Profane plus the Q max turns Q1-auto-Q2 into half his bar while you stay full, and you beat him in any straight 1v1. He doesn't out-scale you the way a Vayne or Kayle does; his danger is the dive — at 2+ items Stormbringer lands on your tower to disable it and hands him bonus health for the brawl, where his stacked health and Maul heal grind you. Keep the lead you built, don't feed him the Thundering Smash attack that starts every all-in, and don't let his tankiness turn a won lane into a coinflip fight.","whys":["His empowered Q run plus a Frenzied Maul bite that heals out-brawls your one-ability, energy-gated level 1 — concede the opening and farm.","He edges level 2 because a second Frenzied Maul on the mark heals him back, but your Q+E gives a slow-trade — stay even, don't force.","Your E slow into a Drakehound's-Step second spin pins an immobile Voli for the Q-cone into empowered-auto trade he can't escape.","Your cooldowns are longest here and his bite-heal brawl is sticky — farm toward 6 rather than trading into his sustain.","Public Execution blinks 1250 behind him and suppresses; break the Frenzied Maul mark before his second cast and the bite never heals him.","Eclipse/Profane plus the Q max means Q1-auto-Q2 chunks him to half while you stay full — force every all-in once his Q stun is on cooldown.","You win the straight 1v1, but Stormbringer hands him bonus health and disables your tower for the dive — close the lane before two items."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"warwick","win":["Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Skill","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Eternal Hunger heals him only once HE drops below 50% health — above that his attacks are bonus magic damage and nothing more. Your one-ability, energy-gated level 1 still loses the auto war, but the poke you land does not get licked back."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your worst stretch: your Q-into-Sundering-Slam combo sits on its longest cooldowns while Jaws of the Beast comes back every 8s and heals him for damage scaled off YOUR maximum health, so short trades just feed it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is a directional leap, not a point-and-click: it suppresses the first champion it collides with for 1.5s, and the leap goes further the faster he is — stay above 50% health, Blood Hunt stays off, and his R stays short."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus Q-rank is your one true window: Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus an empowered auto chunks him faster than an 8s Jaws can heal — but bait Primal Howl first, because 2.5s of damage reduction eats exactly that burst."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Primal Howl's 2.5s of damage reduction first, then E-slow into Cunning Sweep → Sundering Slam with the empowered auto behind it","Reach Eclipse and a Q rank — your only window where the combo outruns his passive drain and Q heal","Stay above 50% health so Blood Hunt never switches on and his Infinite Duress leap keeps its short range"],"foe":["Heal back your short trades with an 8s Jaws of the Beast that scales off your maximum health","Land the Infinite Duress leap the instant you commit a dash chain and suppress you for 1.5s","Drop you under 50% so Blood Hunt switches on, then chase with the speed and a longer R leap"]},"early":"Eternal Hunger heals him only once HE is under 50% health, so at full bars his attacks are pure magic damage and the poke you land stays landed — but your level 1 is one ability and energy-gated, so you still concede the opener. Last-hit at the outer edge of Cunning Sweep where it doubles, and don't throw a Q just to poke; Jaws of the Beast is back every 8s and heals him for what it deals. Your E spin and its near-total slow is your one early pin, and Blood Hunt only switches on once you are under half, so keeping your own bar high keeps him slow.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your weakest window — your cooldowns are longest and an 8s Jaws of the Beast refunds him off your max health, so don't force extended fights you cannot finish. At 6 his R is the problem, but not the way it is usually described: Infinite Duress is a directional leap that suppresses the first champion it collides with for 1.5s, so a minion in the path eats it and a held dash beats it. The leap also scales with his bonus move speed — stay above 50% health, Blood Hunt never triggers, and his R stays short. Bait Primal Howl before you commit.","late":"Your one real favour window is your first item: Eclipse plus a Q rank lets Cunning Sweep → Sundering Slam plus an empowered auto chunk him faster than an 8s Jaws can recover, so all-in there or never — after baiting Primal Howl's 2.5 seconds of damage reduction. After that he reclaims it: Jaws scales off your maximum health so stacking it feeds him, Blood Hunt turns any dip under 50% into a chase, and his healing triples under 25%. Close it on your Eclipse spike or accept you lose the long drain fight.","whys":["Your level 1 is one ability and energy-gated, so he wins the opener — but Eternal Hunger heals him nothing until he himself drops under 50%.","You get your E-slow into the combo, but Jaws of the Beast is back in 8s and heals him for what it deals, so the trade washes out.","This is your longest-cooldown window and Jaws of the Beast returns every 8s scaling off your max health — short trades feed him.","Eternal Hunger triples his healing once HE falls under 25%, so a long 4-5 fight spirals the moment you take him low without finishing.","Infinite Duress is a directional leap that suppresses the first champion it hits for 1.5s — body-block it, or hold a dash for the leap.","Eclipse plus Q rank lets Cunning Sweep → Sundering Slam plus an empowered auto burst him faster than his heals — your single clean all-in window.","He out-scales hard: max-health damage on Jaws, a Blood Hunt chase that only switches on under 50%, and healing that triples when he is low."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"wukong","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q cone into Sundering Slam plus a passive-empowered auto trades even, but his Crushing Blow shreds your armor and his Nimbus Strike (E) gives him the dash to disengage, so neither of you can run the other down."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"His threat window: Warrior Trickster is 22s at rank 1 — clone plus invisibility to bait your Lacerate spin, then a targeted Nimbus Strike in and Cyclone for the all-in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution picks the farthest enemy CHAMPION in your chosen line, so a Warrior Trickster clone can never be the target — the real Wukong eats the suppress."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus the Lvl 9 Q max: Q1-auto-Q2 with your passive auto chunks him before his armor/Stone Skin stacking and item powerspike pull the attrition even."}],"wants":{"you":["Land the Q cone into Sundering Slam, then weave a passive-empowered auto and chain a Drakehound's Step dash before his E lets him peel away","Hold R until Warrior Trickster resolves — it picks champions, so the clone is never a target","Force the all-in at 6 and at first item, before his armor stacking and Cyclone teamfight engage blunt your physical-only burst"],"foe":["Drop the Warrior Trickster clone and go invisible to bait your Lacerate spin onto the fake","Cut your armour with an 8s Crushing Blow, Nimbus Strike off a minion to reach you, then Cyclone you up","Stack Stone Skin armour and its health regen to soak your all-physical damage and stall to even"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a real coinflip — you're both melee with long cooldowns and no full combo yet. Your Q cone (doubled on the outer edge) into the Sundering Slam line-slam, capped by a Drakehound's Step empowered auto, trades roughly evenly with his Crushing Blow, an 8s auto-reset that gains range and cuts your armour, so don't overcommit chasing a kill that isn't there. Nimbus Strike is TARGETED, so a minion between you is a gap-close and spacing alone will not keep him off. Trade in short bursts, refund energy off your passive auto, and farm.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his window, not yours — Warrior Trickster is 22s at rank 1, and he can drop the clone, go invisible, bait your Lacerate spin onto the decoy, then Nimbus Strike in and Cyclone you up for the real all-in. Hold your big cooldowns until the clone resolves; refuse the bait and he has no engage for twenty-two seconds. Then 6 flips it: Public Execution picks the farthest enemy CHAMPION in your chosen line, so the clone cannot be the target and the real body always eats the suppress. Bait his E or wait out the clone, then commit.","late":"This stays a true coinflip into items. Your first-item spike (Eclipse/Profane plus Q max) is your best honest window — Q1-auto-Q2 with your passive auto chunks him while you stay healthy. But Wukong is item-dependent and an armor-stacker, so at 2+ items his Steelcaps and Stone Skin armor blunt your physical-only output, and his Cyclone is a real teamfight engage that scales alongside your R. Close trades on your terms in the mid-game; if it goes long, it's a flat skill lane decided by who lands their lock-on or clone-bait cleanly.","whys":["You're both melee with long level-1 cooldowns and no combo — last-hit, don't force a trade neither of you wins.","Your Q-cone-into-Slam plus a passive-empowered auto trades evenly with his Crushing Blow armor-shred poke — burst, don't extend.","Your short combo is online, but Nimbus Strike is 10s and targeted, so he dashes off a minion and neither of you runs the other down.","Levels 4-5 are his clone-bait window — Warrior Trickster is 22s, and the decoy plus a targeted Nimbus Strike flips a trade on your longest cooldowns.","Public Execution picks the farthest enemy CHAMPION in your line, so the clone is never a legal target — the real Wukong eats the suppress every time.","Eclipse/Profane plus Q max means Q1-auto-Q2 halves him before his armor stacking and Cyclone engage fully come online.","He stacks armor, so at 2+ items Steelcaps and Stone Skin blunt your physical-only damage and his Cyclone scales as a real engage — back to a coinflip."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"yasuo","win":["Skill","Yasuo","Yasuo","Skill","Skill","Yasuo","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-cone-into-Sundering-Slam plus an empowered auto and E slow all come online — and Sweeping Blade cannot re-dash the same target for seconds, so once he goes through you he is stuck."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him and suppresses through his passive shield — a hard-CC all-in that Windwall can't block because none of your kit is a projectile."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level 9 Q max: Q-empowered-auto-Q chunks half his health while your W braces against his first crit and amps your slam back."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His crit takes over — IE/Shieldbow out-DPS you, and Last Breath falls to 30s, so every two-stack tornado is another full knockup on your combo."}],"wants":{"you":["Catch him the beat after Sweeping Blade goes through you — it locks out on the same target — then Q-cone, empowered auto, E slow","Remember Wind Wall blocks none of your kit (it's all melee) — don't waste tempo baiting it; just commit your empowered-auto and W slam when his E is down","At 6 use R to blink behind him and suppress — it's hard CC that ignores his passive shield and Wind Wall and pins him for the full combo"],"foe":["Sweeping Blade off fresh minions every 0.5s to reset distance whenever your slow lands","Land a two-stack Steel Tempest tornado, since Last Breath only leaps to an Airborne target","Stack crit to IE/Shieldbow and reach 2+ items, then out-DPS you with auto-resets and Wind Wall the auto your empowered passive needs"]},"early":"Wind Wall blocks none of your kit — your Q cone, Sundering Slam, W slam and E spin are all melee or ground-targeted, not projectiles — so against you it's just his panic button for jungle ganks, not a lane tool. The real early threat is his E: he dashes through the minion wave to poke and dash back, dodging your Drakehound's Step trade. Punish him the moment his E is on minion cooldown — Q the cone, weave the empowered auto off the dash, then E for the near-total slow so he can't reposition. Don't force level 1-2 fights: your cooldowns are long and his passive shield plus Q double-strike out-trade a single empowered auto.","mid":"Level 3 you have the Q-into-Sundering-Slam combo and start winning the dash-weave trades the beat after Sweeping Blade goes through you, since it locks out on the same target. Levels 4-5 stay even: his tornado windup and shield make him slippery, so farm toward 6. At 6 your R is the equalizer — blink behind him, suppress straight through the shield, and crash him down with your W braced to soak his first crit. You don't need to bait Wind Wall — nothing you cast is a projectile — so commit the empowered auto and W slam the moment his dash is spent.","late":"This is where Yasuo reclaims the lane. Once he hits IE/Shieldbow at 2 items his crit auto-resets out-DPS your empowered-passive rhythm, and Last Breath is down to 30 seconds — every two-stack tornado he lands is another free knockup into it. Wind Wall still blocks nothing you cast, but his items, shield uptime and any armour he buys outscale your physical-only output. Win the game before then — snowball your 6-and-first-item windows into a lead, group, and use R to blink onto his carries rather than soloing a fed Yasuo.","whys":["You both have one ability and no combo at level 1, and his Wind Wall doesn't even block your melee kit — neither side has a reason to commit.","Your cooldowns are long while Steel Tempest returns every 4s and counts as a basic attack, so it out-chips one empowered auto — farm.","Your full Q-cone into Sundering-Slam, empowered auto and E slow come online and lock him when his E-dash is on minion cooldown — your first real trade win.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest cooldown window; deny the two-stack tornado and his Last Breath has nothing to leap to.","R blinks behind him and suppresses through his passive shield — hard CC and a gap-close that Wind Wall can't touch since nothing you throw is a projectile.","Eclipse and the level 9 Q max let you Q-empowered-auto-Q for half his health while your W braces his first crit and amps your slam.","At 2+ items Last Breath is down to 30s, Steel Tempest crits like a basic attack, and his auto-resets reclaim the duel — your physical-only damage falls off into his scaling."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"yone","win":["Skill","Yone","Yone","Skill","Skill","Yone","Yone"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Mortal Steel poke and a Spirit Cleave that shields him out-tempo your single energy-gated ability — last-hit with the cone tip and accept the chip; nothing answers his level 1."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Cunning Sweep cone into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto out-trades him in a short burst — but only inside Soul Unbound's 22 seconds at rank 1."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind the farthest enemy and suppresses, locking a champion built to never get pinned — but E only returns him to where he cast it, so it does not save him from your R."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"The two-stack Mortal Steel dash-knockup, a Spirit Cleave shield on a timer that shrinks as he buys attack speed, and Fate Sealed blinking behind to pull you back reclaim the lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach level 3, bait Soul Unbound's 22s, then commit Cunning Sweep cone into Sundering Slam with the empowered auto","Hold R until he has spent E, then Public Execution behind him and chain W (Repudiation) shield into the Q follow-up while he is suppressed","Force short trades on your empowered-auto windows and your Lacerate slow, ending before his W cleave and crit steroids take over"],"foe":["Poke with Mortal Steel to the two-stack knockup, then Soul Unbound back to his body to undo your damage","Stack attack speed so Spirit Cleave's shield and its cooldown both scale against your burst","Scale to 2+ items where he kites your dash chains and Fate Sealed blinks behind to pull you back mid-commit"]},"early":"Yone owns the very first levels — Mortal Steel poke and a Spirit Cleave that shields him out-tempo your one energy-gated ability, so don't try to dash-weave before your level 3 combo is online. Last-hit with the tip of your Cunning Sweep cone (the outer edge deals double) and accept the chip; you can't win level 1 here. The trap is Soul Unbound: his spirit leaves the body, and it snaps back to where he cast it while echoing a chunk of the damage he dealt — so a trade you commit while he holds it gets partly undone. It is 22 seconds at rank 1, so baiting it out really does buy you a window. By level 3 your cone-into-slam plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto is a real short trade — inside those 22 seconds.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your soft spot — your cooldowns are longest and his Q poke chips you while you wait, so farm toward 6 rather than forcing. Then 6 flips it: Public Execution blinks you behind the farthest enemy in your line and suppresses, which pins a champion designed to never be pinned — and his E only rewinds him to where he cast it, so it can't pull him out of your suppress. Save R for after he's spent E, then use the Repudiation brace to block his counter-damage (amplifying your output) and crash the W slam plus your Q follow-up into him while he's locked. That's your kill window, but it's not a free 1v1 — if he respects you and holds E for the rewind, your suppress is just a long trade and his R can still knock you up after.","late":"Your first-item spike (Eclipse/Profane plus level 9 Q max) still beats him in a straight fight — force all-ins here while you can. But at 2+ items the lane becomes his: the two-stack Mortal Steel dash-knockup, a Spirit Cleave shield whose cooldown shrinks as he buys attack speed, and Fate Sealed blinking behind the last champion in a line to pull everyone back toward him. His passive adds magic damage on every second attack, so armour alone reads his damage wrong. Close this before he gets two items, or accept that he becomes the mobile carry you can't catch.","whys":["Mortal Steel poke and a Spirit Cleave that shields him out-tempo your one energy-gated ability — nothing you have answers level 1.","Level 2 is roughly even — Lacerate exists but your cooldowns are long, and Soul Unbound is 22s of insurance against any trade you start.","Your level 3 Cunning Sweep cone into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step auto out-trades him in a short burst once Soul Unbound is spent.","Levels 4-5 are your weakest window — longest cooldowns while his Q poke chips you down with no combo to retaliate.","Public Execution blinks behind him and suppresses through a window his E rewind can't escape, turning an even lane into a real kill threat at 6.","Your Eclipse/Profane spike plus Q max lets you cone-auto-slam chunk him while staying full behind a Repudiation shield — your strongest favor window.","Yone reclaims it as a scaler — the two-stack Mortal Steel knockup and a Spirit Cleave shield kite you, and Fate Sealed pulls you straight back in."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"yorick","win":["Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Ambessa","Skill","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q-cone into Sundering Slam plus a Drakehound's Step empowered auto is your first real trade — burst him before his Q (Last Rites) heal and a ghoul or two are up to soak it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses and stuns through the ghoul swarm — your one guaranteed all-in. Dark Procession is 20s and destructible, so break out, don't burn dashes."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse plus the level 9 Q max lets you Q1-auto-Q2 chunk him — buy Grievous Wounds first, because Last Rites heals him back every 6 seconds."},{"when":"Late","text":"Maiden of the Mist plus four ghouls and W to wall off your escape let him out-trade and splitpush — he reclaims the matchup once he has two items and a Maiden snowballing the side wave."}],"wants":{"you":["Burst with Q-into-Sundering-Slam and the empowered auto before a 6s Last Rites heals the chip back","Hit Level 6 even and use Public Execution to blink past his ghoul swarm, suppress him, and lock down the all-in","Force the 1v1 on your Eclipse spike before Maiden and his splitpush hand him the side lane and the map"],"foe":["Land Mourning Mist to cut your armour, slow you, and speed every ghoul and the Maiden at you","Spawn Maiden and shove waves so he can splitpush and trade towers instead of dueling you head-on","Drop Dark Procession behind you after you blink in — 20s at rank 1 — then grind you down with ghoul pressure"]},"early":"Last Rites heals him every 6 seconds and digs the grave that becomes his next ghoul, so he contests the first waves while you are one-ability and energy-gated — concede a little CS rather than walking into the swarm. Once you have Q-into-Sundering-Slam and a Drakehound's Step empowered auto you can dash-weave a short burst trade, but the moment Mourning Mist lands you are slowed, marked, and short on armour while every ghoul speeds toward the mark. Commit only when his ghoul count is low and that 12s globule is spent.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your weakest window and his Maiden is coming, so do not force — farm toward 6 and save your E (Lacerate) slow for disengage when he tries to mark you. At 6 everything flips for one window: Public Execution blinks you behind him through the ghoul swarm, suppresses and stuns, and Repudiation braced against the ghoul chip turns their damage into your amplified slam. Land it when Mourning Mist is down and his ghoul count is thin and it is a kill; blink into a full swarm with a fresh 20s Dark Procession behind you and you are the one who dies.","late":"This is his game, not yours. Once Maiden of the Mist is up with two items he out-trades you with four ghouls, zones the side wave with E-marks, and uses W (Dark Procession) to trap you mid-fight, then just trades towers while you struggle to reach a ghoul-shielded target. Your physical-only damage stops mattering as he splitpushes, so your job is to group, use Public Execution to blink onto and suppress his backline in teamfights, and never get caught alone in the side lane where his swarm and W wall can collapse on you.","whys":["His Q (Last Rites) heal and ghoul generation contest the first wave while you are one-ability and energy-gated — give CS, do not brawl into the swarm.","Your Q-cone burst trade is online but his Q sustain and ghoul soak even it out — trade only when his ghoul count is low and his E is down.","You have your dash-weave combo, but Mourning Mist cuts your armour, slows and marks you for every ghoul at once, so neither of you commits cleanly.","Your cooldowns are longest at 4-5 and Maiden is arriving — he out-zones you with E-marks and ghoul pressure, so farm safe and wait for 6.","Public Execution blinks behind the swarm, suppresses and stuns — Dark Procession is 20s and destructible, so break it or wait it out first.","Eclipse plus Q max means Q1-auto-Q2 halves him, and Grievous Wounds shuts the 6s Last Rites heal that answers your chip.","Maiden, four ghouls and W walls let him out-trade and splitpush you off the side lane — his scaling and your physical-only damage hand him the late game."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"zac","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Zac's best window into you: your cooldowns are longest here, and every Cell Division blob he sheds and reabsorbs heals back the chip your Q-cone and empowered autos do, so walk the blobs or he farms even."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"R behind him into the suppress-and-stun is your first real kill threat — it blinks past Elastic Slingshot, 21s at rank 1, and lands on a Zac with no armour yet. Cell Division still revives him every five minutes."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Eclipse/Profane plus the Lvl 9 Q max: Q1-into-empowered-auto-into-Sundering-Slam chunks half his bar, and timing your W brace onto his E-sling knock-up amps the slam that follows."},{"when":"Late","text":"Zac's biggest threat window — Unstable Matter is percent-max-health magic every 5s, so every health item he buys hits you harder, and Let's Bounce! peels for his carries while you bounce off him."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 6 and R behind him into the suppress-stun inside Elastic Slingshot's 21 seconds","Land Q1's cone then the Sundering Slam line on an isolated Zac to unlock your empowered-auto burst","Brace your W onto his E-sling knock-up so the blocked damage amps your follow-up slam"],"foe":["Reabsorb every Cell Division blob so your cone-and-auto chip just heals back to even","Grab you with Stretching Strikes, then hit a minion to slam you both together","Stall to two items where health stacking makes Unstable Matter's percent damage bite harder"]},"early":"Zac trades you evenly early and that is the problem — your level-1-through-3 window is genuinely weak with long cooldowns, and every ability he lands sheds a Cell Division blob he picks back up to heal off your chip. Don't force extended fights here: throw Q1 for the cone, follow with the Sundering Slam line if it connects for the empowered auto, then dash out before Stretching Strikes grabs you and a minion hit slams you both together. He has no real kill pressure on you either, so match farm, walk over every stray blob to deny his sustain, and aim for 6.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your sag — longest cooldowns, and his blob pickups out-sustain your chip while he sits on the wave. Hold for 6: your R blinks behind him and suppresses through Elastic Slingshot, which is 21 seconds at rank 1, so the moment he spends it you own the window. That plus your first-item Eclipse/Profane and the Q max is the one stretch you genuinely win the lane — bait the sling onto your W brace, then all-in while the amp is up.","late":"This is where Zac reclaims it. Unstable Matter is percent-max-health magic every 5 seconds, so every health item he finishes makes him hurt you more while your all-physical damage bounces off, and he slings into your backline and R-bounces to peel for his carries. Your spike was Level 6 through first item — if you didn't build a lead there, the 1v1 drifts his way. Splitpush a side lane rather than facecheck a fight he is built to survive.","whys":["Your level 1 is weak with one ability and no combo, and Cell Division sheds a blob on every ability he lands that he picks back up to heal.","Level 2 Q+E gives a slow-into-trade, but every Cell Division blob you leave on the ground resets the trade to even.","Your short combo is online but his blob pickups undo your poke, so the lane stays a genuine coinflip on engages.","Levels 4-5 are your longest-cooldown window and Unstable Matter chips you every 5s while his blobs refund what you land.","R blinks behind him and suppresses through Elastic Slingshot's 21s — your first real kill threat, but Cell Division revives him every 5 minutes.","Eclipse/Profane and the Q max let Q1-auto-Sundering-Slam chunk half his bar while your W brace eats his E knock-up and amps the slam.","Full-tank Zac blunts your physical-only damage while Unstable Matter's percent-max-health magic hits harder for every point of health he buys."]},
  {"a":"ambessa","b":"ziggs","win":["Ziggs","Ziggs","Ziggs","Skill","Ziggs","Skill","Ziggs"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Ziggs' Bouncing Bomb out-ranges your whole kit — expect to eat poke before your Q-into-empowered-auto and your move-command dash come online."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam plus Lacerate's near-total slow lets you dash-weave through one Satchel Charge knockback and finally crash a trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses and stuns — the one button his Satchel and minefield can't displace you out of, and your kill window opens here."},{"when":"1st item","text":"First-item physical damage shreds his squishy artillery frame — Satchel Charge is 20s at rank 1, so reach him once it is spent with R up and he is dead."}],"wants":{"you":["Make him spend Satchel Charge, then R behind him inside its 20 seconds so nothing displaces the gap-close","Use Lacerate's near-total slow plus a Drakehound's Step dash to close the range his Bouncing Bomb keeps open","Save Public Execution for the all-in — it blinks behind him and suppresses, so his Satchel and minefield can't peel you off"],"foe":["Chunk you with an 850-range Bouncing Bomb every 6s so you walk up already low","Hold the 20s Satchel Charge to knock you out of your dash-weave as you commit","Wall the chokes with a 16s Hexplosive Minefield and kite so you never get a clean empowered auto"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 belong to him — Bouncing Bomb reaches 850 against your 650 Cunning Sweep and comes back every 6 seconds, and you have no Sundering Slam follow-up or move-command dash yet, so soak the wave from the back and accept the chip. Watch Short Fuse: every ability he casts shortens it, so a cast is the tell that a bonus-damage attack comes with his step-up. The lane flips at 3: once Q-into-empowered-auto is online and Lacerate's slow lands, you dash-weave through one Satchel knockback and make contact. Dash straight through Hexplosive Minefield rather than around it — repeat detonations on one target deal less.","mid":"This is where you take over. His whole defence is Satchel Charge and a minefield, and neither survives your R. From Levels 4-5 hold the wave near you so he has to step up to farm, slow him with Lacerate, and once Public Execution is up at 6 you blink behind him, suppress and crash the stun, then chain Q1-auto-Q2. Satchel Charge is 20s at rank 1 and it is his only escape, so the moment he spends it you have twenty seconds against a mage with no mobility — that is the whole kill window.","late":"You still win the straight fight if you can reach him, but late-game Ziggs becomes a siege and waveclear problem — his Hexplosive Minefield zones objectives and his bombs delete waves from screens away. Your physical-only damage also wants to end before he buys range and his team peels him. Use your mobility and R to force the pick before teamfights spread out; once he's behind a frontline with Satchel and minefield walls between you, you're a sidelane threat, not a teamfight one. Close it on the back of your 6-and-first-item kill pressure.","whys":["Bouncing Bomb reaches 850 against your 650 Cunning Sweep and returns every 6s, so he pokes for free before your dash exists.","Q-into-E gives you a slow-into-trade, but early cooldowns and his bomb range keep the window even — don't force the gap yet.","With your combo online, dash straight through Hexplosive Minefield — repeat detonations on one target deal less — and crash the trade his poke cannot sustain.","Satchel Charge is his only escape and it is 20s at rank 1 — hold the wave near you and make him spend it walking up to farm.","Public Execution blinks you behind him, suppresses and stuns — neither Satchel nor minefield can peel you off it.","First-item physical shreds his squishy artillery frame; reach him inside Satchel Charge's 20s with R up and Q1-auto-Q2 ends it.","You still win the duel, but his minefield siege and bomb waveclear take over the map — force the pick before fights spread out."]}
