window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"ambessa","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Aureate Rush is his only dash, 10s at rank 1 — trade inside it and leave before The Darkin Glaive lands."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Grim Deliverance is 110s and heals him off its damage; Public Execution is 130s but picks the fight."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Grievous Wounds by first item: The Darkin Glaive heals every 10s and Grim Deliverance heals off its damage."},{"when":"Late","text":"Stay the aggressor: Cultivation of War stacks into bonus AD and a revive, so kill him before that bar fills."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade inside his 10s E, then go","Public Execution starts the fight on your timer — 1250 range and a suppress he has no answer to","Grievous Wounds before Eclipse"],"foe":["Refill your chip with a Darkin Glaive heal every 10s and Grim Deliverance off its own damage","Catch a dash with Dreaded Return, an 850-range stab that pulls you straight back to him","Fill Cultivation of War for the bonus AD and the revive, then farm even through 4-5"]},"early":"Level 1 is a mutual farm — nothing is online. Then you take over: at 2 your dashes and Q trade and leave before The Darkin Glaive's double slash answers, and by 3 Aureate Rush is one 10s dash against your three. Bleed him with short combos, sidestep the 850-range Dreaded Return, and don't let his Glaive heal refill the chip.","mid":"The Darkin Glaive heals him every 10s and starts absorbing your poke at 4-5, and both ults land at 6 — Grim Deliverance heals him off its own damage. Buy Grievous Wounds. At first item you're ahead again: the dash-reset pattern out-DPSes him in extended trades, so force the long fight on your engage.","late":"Stay the aggressor — that's the whole matchup. Two-plus items you out-burst him inside your combo window, so open with R on your timing, dump the chain, and disengage if the kill isn't there rather than filling his Determination bar for free. In teamfights, R their carry and let your burst cash it.","whys":["Level 1 is even — neither combo is online yet, so it's pure farming until level 2 arrives.","Ambessa spikes at 2: trade and leave before The Darkin Glaive's double slash and its knockup recast land.","Level 3 is yours — Aureate Rush is a single 10s dash against your three, so hit and run and chip him down.","Levels 4-5 flatten out: The Darkin Glaive heals him every 10s and absorbs your poke, so bank CS and wait on items.","At 6 Grim Deliverance heals him off its own damage on 110s — Grievous Wounds before you contest that window.","First item is Ambessa's, but only with Grievous Wounds — a 10s Glaive heal refunds the whole long trade.","Two-plus items stay yours, but Aureate Rush scales off maximum health, so stacking health feeds it — burst inside your window."]});
